0\n \n-\uc0dd\uc131\ub41c \ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8\ub294 \ub2e4\uc74c\uacfc \uac19\uc740 \uad6c\uc870\ub97c \uac00\uc9c0\uace0 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc2dc\uc791\uc6a9 embedded crew\ub294 \ud074\ub798\uc2dd Python/YAML \ub808\uc774\uc544\uc6c3\uc744 \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4. Flow \uc548\uc5d0\uc11c JSON-first crew\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud558\ub824\uba74 crew \ud3f4\ub354\uc5d0 `crew.jsonc`\uc640 `agents/*.jsonc`\ub97c \ub9cc\ub4e4\uace0 `crewai.project.load_crew`\ub85c \ub85c\ub4dc\ud558\uc138\uc694. \uc608\uc2dc\ub294 [Flows](/ko/concepts/flows#building-your-crews)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n+\uc0dd\uc131\ub41c \ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8\ub294 \ub2e4\uc74c\uacfc \uac19\uc740 \uad6c\uc870\ub97c \uac00\uc9c0\uace0 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc2dc\uc791\uc6a9 embedded crew\ub294 \ud074\ub798\uc2dd Python/YAML \ub808\uc774\uc544\uc6c3\uc744 \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4. Flow \uc548\uc5d0\uc11c JSON-first crew\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud558\ub824\uba74 crew \ud3f4\ub354\uc5d0 `crew.jsonc`\uc640 `agents/*.jsonc`\ub97c \ub9cc\ub4e4\uace0 `crewai.project.load_crew`\ub85c \ub85c\ub4dc\ud558\uc138\uc694. \uc608\uc2dc\ub294 [Flows](/ko/concepts/flows)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n \n ```\n guide_creator_flow/\n@@ -370,7 +370,7 @@ if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n \n ## 6\ub2e8\uacc4: \ud658\uacbd \ubcc0\uc218 \uc124\uc815\ud558\uae30\n \n-\ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8 \ub8e8\ud2b8\uc5d0 `.env` \ud30c\uc77c\uc744 \uc0dd\uc131\ud558\uace0 API \ud0a4\ub97c \uc785\ub825\ud558\uc138\uc694. \uacf5\uae09\uc790 \uad6c\uc131\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \uc790\uc138\ud55c \ub0b4\uc6a9\uc740 [LLM \uc124\uc815 \uac00\uc774\ub4dc](/ko/concepts/llms#setting-up-your-llm)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n+\ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8 \ub8e8\ud2b8\uc5d0 `.env` \ud30c\uc77c\uc744 \uc0dd\uc131\ud558\uace0 API \ud0a4\ub97c \uc785\ub825\ud558\uc138\uc694. \uacf5\uae09\uc790 \uad6c\uc131\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \uc790\uc138\ud55c \ub0b4\uc6a9\uc740 [LLM \uc124\uc815 \uac00\uc774\ub4dc](/ko/concepts/llms#llm-\uc124\uc815\ud558\uae30)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n \n ```sh .env\n OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/learn/human-feedback-in-flows.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/learn/human-feedback-in-flows.mdx\nindex fc490f201e..6856913ab8 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/learn/human-feedback-in-flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/learn/human-feedback-in-flows.mdx\n@@ -697,7 +697,7 @@ class ArticleReviewFlow(Flow):\n \n - [Flow \uac1c\uc694](/ko/concepts/flows) - CrewAI Flow\uc5d0 \ub300\ud574 \uc54c\uc544\ubcf4\uae30\n - [Flow \uc0c1\ud0dc \uad00\ub9ac](/ko/guides/flows/mastering-flow-state) - Flow\uc5d0\uc11c \uc0c1\ud0dc \uad00\ub9ac\ud558\uae30\n-- [Flow \uc601\uc18d\uc131](/ko/concepts/flows#persistence) - Flow \uc0c1\ud0dc \uc601\uc18d\ud654\n+- [Flow \uc601\uc18d\uc131](/ko/concepts/flows#\ud50c\ub85c\uc6b0-\uc9c0\uc18d\uc131) - Flow \uc0c1\ud0dc \uc601\uc18d\ud654\n - [@router\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud55c \ub77c\uc6b0\ud305](/ko/concepts/flows#router) - \uc870\uac74\ubd80 \ub77c\uc6b0\ud305\uc5d0 \ub300\ud574 \ub354 \uc54c\uc544\ubcf4\uae30\n - [\uc2e4\ud589 \uc2dc \uc778\uac04 \uc785\ub825](/ko/learn/human-input-on-execution) - \ud0dc\uc2a4\ud06c \uc218\uc900 \uc778\uac04 \uc785\ub825\n - [\uba54\ubaa8\ub9ac](/ko/concepts/memory) - HITL \ud559\uc2b5\uc5d0\uc11c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ub418\ub294 \ud1b5\ud569 \uba54\ubaa8\ub9ac \uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/mcp/dsl-integration.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/mcp/dsl-integration.mdx\nindex 33eb6f81ea..17ec576f93 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/mcp/dsl-integration.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/mcp/dsl-integration.mdx\n@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ CrewAI\uc758 MCP DSL(Domain Specific Language) \ud1b5\ud569\uc740 \uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8\ub97c MCP(Model\n <Info>\n   \uc774\ub294 \ub300\ubd80\ubd84\uc758 MCP \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uc0ac\ub840\uc5d0 **\uad8c\uc7a5\ub418\ub294 \uc811\uadfc \ubc29\uc2dd**\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc218\ub3d9 \uc5f0\uacb0 \uad00\ub9ac\uac00\n   \ud544\uc694\ud55c \uace0\uae09 \uc2dc\ub098\ub9ac\uc624\uc758 \uacbd\uc6b0\n-  [MCPServerAdapter](/ko/mcp/overview#advanced-mcpserveradapter)\ub97c \ucc38\uc870\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n+  [MCPServerAdapter](/ko/mcp/overview)\ub97c \ucc38\uc870\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n </Info>\n \n ## \uae30\ubcf8 \uc0ac\uc6a9\ubc95\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/quickstart.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/quickstart.mdx\nindex 4ccaa1a473..f808133624 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/quickstart.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/quickstart.mdx\n@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ CrewAI\ub97c \uc544\uc9c1 \uc124\uce58\ud558\uc9c0 \uc54a\uc558\ub2e4\uba74 \uba3c\uc800 [\uc124\uce58 \uac00\uc774\ub4dc](/ko/install\n ## \uc0ac\uc804 \uc694\uac74\n \n - Python \ud658\uacbd\uacfc CrewAI CLI([\uc124\uce58](/ko/installation) \ucc38\uace0)\n-- \uc62c\ubc14\ub978 API \ud0a4\ub85c \uc124\uc815\ud55c LLM \u2014 [LLM](/ko/concepts/llms#setting-up-your-llm) \ucc38\uace0\n+- \uc62c\ubc14\ub978 API \ud0a4\ub85c \uc124\uc815\ud55c LLM \u2014 [LLM](/ko/concepts/llms#llm-\uc124\uc815\ud558\uae30) \ucc38\uace0\n - \uc774 \ud29c\ud1a0\ub9ac\uc5bc\uc758 \uc6f9 \uac80\uc0c9\uc6a9 [Serper.dev](https://serper.dev/) API \ud0a4(`SERPER_API_KEY`)\n \n ## \uccab \ubc88\uc9f8 Flow \ub9cc\ub4e4\uae30\n@@ -155,7 +155,7 @@ CrewAI\ub97c \uc544\uc9c1 \uc124\uce58\ud558\uc9c0 \uc54a\uc558\ub2e4\uba74 \uba3c\uc800 [\uc124\uce58 \uac00\uc774\ub4dc](/ko/install\n   \ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8 \ub8e8\ud2b8\uc758 `.env`\uc5d0 \ub2e4\uc74c\uc744 \uc124\uc815\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \n     - `SERPER_API_KEY` \u2014 [Serper.dev](https://serper.dev/)\uc5d0\uc11c \ubc1c\uae09\n-    - \ubaa8\ub378 \uc81c\uacf5\uc790 \ud0a4 \u2014 [LLM \uc124\uc815](/ko/concepts/llms#setting-up-your-llm) \ucc38\uace0\n+    - \ubaa8\ub378 \uc81c\uacf5\uc790 \ud0a4 \u2014 [LLM \uc124\uc815](/ko/concepts/llms#llm-\uc124\uc815\ud558\uae30) \ucc38\uace0\n   </Step>\n \n   <Step title=\"\uc124\uce58 \ubc0f \uc2e4\ud589\">\n@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@ CrewAI\ub97c \uc544\uc9c1 \uc124\uce58\ud558\uc9c0 \uc54a\uc558\ub2e4\uba74 \uba3c\uc800 [\uc124\uce58 \uac00\uc774\ub4dc](/ko/install\n 2. **Crew** \u2014 `kickoff_content_crew`\uac00 `crew.jsonc`\ub97c \ub85c\ub4dc\ud558\uace0 \uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8 \ud55c \uba85\u00b7\uc791\uc5c5 \ud558\ub098\ub85c \uc2e4\ud589\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc5f0\uad6c\uc6d0\uc774 **Serper**\ub85c \uc6f9\uc744 \uac80\uc0c9\ud558\uace0 \uad6c\uc870\ud654\ub41c \ubcf4\uace0\uc11c\ub97c \uc501\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n 3. **\uacb0\uacfc\ubb3c** \u2014 \uc791\uc5c5\uc758 `output_file`\uc774 `output/report.md`\uc5d0 \ubcf4\uace0\uc11c\ub97c \uc501\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \n-Flow \ud328\ud134(\ub77c\uc6b0\ud305, \uc9c0\uc18d\uc131, human-in-the-loop)\uc744 \ub354 \ubcf4\ub824\uba74 [\uccab Flow \ub9cc\ub4e4\uae30](/ko/guides/flows/first-flow)\uc640 [Flows](/ko/concepts/flows)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694. Flow \uc5c6\uc774 crew\ub9cc \uc4f0\ub824\uba74 [Crews](/ko/concepts/crews)\ub97c, \uc791\uc5c5 \uc5c6\uc774 \ub2e8\uc77c `Agent`\uc758 `kickoff()`\ub9cc \uc4f0\ub824\uba74 [Agents](/ko/concepts/agents#direct-agent-interaction-with-kickoff)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n+Flow \ud328\ud134(\ub77c\uc6b0\ud305, \uc9c0\uc18d\uc131, human-in-the-loop)\uc744 \ub354 \ubcf4\ub824\uba74 [\uccab Flow \ub9cc\ub4e4\uae30](/ko/guides/flows/first-flow)\uc640 [Flows](/ko/concepts/flows)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694. Flow \uc5c6\uc774 crew\ub9cc \uc4f0\ub824\uba74 [Crews](/ko/concepts/crews)\ub97c, \uc791\uc5c5 \uc5c6\uc774 \ub2e8\uc77c `Agent`\uc758 `kickoff()`\ub9cc \uc4f0\ub824\uba74 [Agents](/ko/concepts/agents#kickoff-\uc744-\uc0ac\uc6a9\ud55c-\uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8-\uc9c1\uc811-\uc0c1\ud638\uc791\uc6a9)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n \n <Check>\n \uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8 crew\uc640 \uc800\uc7a5\ub41c \ubcf4\uace0\uc11c\uae4c\uc9c0 \uc774\uc5b4\uc9c4 Flow\ub97c \uc644\uc131\ud588\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc774\uc81c \ub2e8\uacc4\u00b7crew\u00b7\ub3c4\uad6c\ub97c \ub354\ud574 \ud655\uc7a5\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4.\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool.mdx\nindex 1b2ec234ee..92b12e7807 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool.mdx\n@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ Docker\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud560 \uc218 \uc5c6\uc744 \uacbd\uc6b0\u2014\uc124\uce58\ub418\uc5b4 \uc788\uc9c0 \uc54a\uac70\ub098 \uc5b4\ub5a4 \uc774\n ### \ube44\uc548\uc804 \uc2e4\ud589\n \n **\ud504\ub85c\ub355\uc158 \ud658\uacbd\uc5d0\uc11c\ub294 \uad8c\uc7a5\ud558\uc9c0 \uc54a\uc74c**\n-\uc774 \ubaa8\ub4dc\ub294 `sys, os..` \ubc0f \uc720\uc0ac\ud55c \ubaa8\ub4c8\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \uc704\ud5d8\ud55c \ud638\ucd9c\uc744 \ud3ec\ud568\ud558\uc5ec \ubaa8\ub4e0 Python \ucf54\ub4dc\ub97c \uc2e4\ud589\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uac8c \ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\ube44\uc548\uc804 \ubaa8\ub4dc \ud65c\uc131\ud654 \ubc29\ubc95](/ko/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool#enabling-unsafe-mode)\ub97c \ud655\uc778\ud558\uc138\uc694\n+\uc774 \ubaa8\ub4dc\ub294 `sys, os..` \ubc0f \uc720\uc0ac\ud55c \ubaa8\ub4c8\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \uc704\ud5d8\ud55c \ud638\ucd9c\uc744 \ud3ec\ud568\ud558\uc5ec \ubaa8\ub4e0 Python \ucf54\ub4dc\ub97c \uc2e4\ud589\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uac8c \ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\ube44\uc548\uc804 \ubaa8\ub4dc \ud65c\uc131\ud654 \ubc29\ubc95](/ko/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool)\ub97c \ud655\uc778\ud558\uc138\uc694\n \n ## \ub85c\uae45\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/llms.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/llms.mdx\nindex ce46c01ddd..a055e2b604 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/llms.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/llms.mdx\n@@ -804,7 +804,7 @@ O CrewAI suporta respostas em streaming de LLMs, permitindo que sua aplica\u00e7\u00e3o\n     ```\n \n     <Tip>\n-      [Clique aqui](/pt-BR/concepts/event-listener#event-listeners) para mais detalhes\n+      [Clique aqui](/pt-BR/concepts/event-listener#criando-um-listener-de-evento-personalizado) para mais detalhes\n     </Tip>\n   </Tab>\n </Tabs>\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/production-architecture.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/production-architecture.mdx\nindex 1cbcb804bc..4e7def4c08 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/production-architecture.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/production-architecture.mdx\n@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ Delegue tarefas complexas para Crews. Um Crew deve ser focado em um objetivo esp\n Aproveite as primitivas de controle do CrewAI para adicionar robustez e controle aos seus Crews.\n \n ### 1. Task Guardrails\n-Use [Task Guardrails](/pt-BR/concepts/tasks#task-guardrails) para validar as sa\u00eddas das tarefas antes que sejam aceitas. Isso garante que seus agentes produzam resultados de alta qualidade.\n+Use [Task Guardrails](/pt-BR/concepts/tasks#guardrails-em-tarefas) para validar as sa\u00eddas das tarefas antes que sejam aceitas. Isso garante que seus agentes produzam resultados de alta qualidade.\n \n ```python\n def validate_content(result: TaskOutput) -> Tuple[bool, Any]:\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/guides/crews/first-crew.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/guides/crews/first-crew.mdx\nindex 7368a56419..b41a8c58ca 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/guides/crews/first-crew.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/guides/crews/first-crew.mdx\n@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ Neste guia, voc\u00ea criar\u00e1 uma crew com dois agentes que pesquisa um t\u00f3pico e es\n Antes de come\u00e7ar:\n \n 1. Instale o CrewAI seguindo o [guia de instala\u00e7\u00e3o](/pt-BR/installation)\n-2. Configure sua chave de LLM seguindo o [guia de LLMs](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#setting-up-your-llm)\n+2. Configure sua chave de LLM seguindo o [guia de LLMs](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#configurando-seu-llm)\n 3. Tenha uma chave [Serper.dev](https://serper.dev/) se quiser usar busca web\n \n ## Etapa 1: Criar uma nova Crew\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/guides/flows/first-flow.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/guides/flows/first-flow.mdx\nindex c810aec55e..db5f84a1cb 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/guides/flows/first-flow.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/guides/flows/first-flow.mdx\n@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ Vamos come\u00e7ar e construir seu primeiro flow!\n Antes de come\u00e7ar, certifique-se de ter:\n \n 1. Instalado o CrewAI seguindo o [guia de instala\u00e7\u00e3o](/pt-BR/installation)\n-2. Configurado sua chave de API LLM no ambiente, conforme o [guia de configura\u00e7\u00e3o do LLM](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#setting-up-your-llm)\n+2. Configurado sua chave de API LLM no ambiente, conforme o [guia de configura\u00e7\u00e3o do LLM](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#configurando-seu-llm)\n 3. Conhecimentos b\u00e1sicos de Python\n \n ## Passo 1: Crie um Novo Projeto de CrewAI Flow\n@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ Isso gerar\u00e1 um projeto com a estrutura b\u00e1sica necess\u00e1ria para seu flow.\n \n ## Passo 2: Entendendo a Estrutura do Projeto\n \n-O projeto gerado possui a seguinte estrutura. A crew inicial embutida usa o layout cl\u00e1ssico Python/YAML. Para usar uma crew JSON-first dentro de um Flow, crie `crew.jsonc` e `agents/*.jsonc` na pasta da crew e carregue com `crewai.project.load_crew`, como mostrado em [Flows](/pt-BR/concepts/flows#building-your-crews).\n+O projeto gerado possui a seguinte estrutura. A crew inicial embutida usa o layout cl\u00e1ssico Python/YAML. Para usar uma crew JSON-first dentro de um Flow, crie `crew.jsonc` e `agents/*.jsonc` na pasta da crew e carregue com `crewai.project.load_crew`, como mostrado em [Flows](/pt-BR/concepts/flows).\n \n ```\n guide_creator_flow/\n@@ -370,7 +370,7 @@ Este \u00e9 o poder dos flows \u2013 combinar diferentes tipos de processamento (intera\n \n ## Passo 6: Configure suas Vari\u00e1veis de Ambiente\n \n-Crie um arquivo `.env` na raiz do projeto com suas chaves de API. Veja o [guia de configura\u00e7\u00e3o do LLM](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#setting-up-your-llm) para detalhes sobre como configurar o provedor.\n+Crie um arquivo `.env` na raiz do projeto com suas chaves de API. Veja o [guia de configura\u00e7\u00e3o do LLM](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#configurando-seu-llm) para detalhes sobre como configurar o provedor.\n \n ```sh .env\n OPENAI_API_KEY=sua_chave_openai\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/learn/human-feedback-in-flows.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/learn/human-feedback-in-flows.mdx\nindex 74693caeae..ea874b42e8 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/learn/human-feedback-in-flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/learn/human-feedback-in-flows.mdx\n@@ -697,7 +697,7 @@ class ArticleReviewFlow(Flow):\n \n - [Vis\u00e3o Geral de Flows](/pt-BR/concepts/flows) - Aprenda sobre CrewAI Flows\n - [Gerenciamento de Estado em Flows](/pt-BR/guides/flows/mastering-flow-state) - Gerenciando estado em flows\n-- [Persist\u00eancia de Flows](/pt-BR/concepts/flows#persistence) - Persistindo estado de flows\n+- [Persist\u00eancia de Flows](/pt-BR/concepts/flows#persist\u00eancia-de-flow) - Persistindo estado de flows\n - [Roteamento com @router](/pt-BR/concepts/flows#router) - Mais sobre roteamento condicional\n - [Input Humano na Execu\u00e7\u00e3o](/pt-BR/learn/human-input-on-execution) - Input humano no n\u00edvel de task\n - [Mem\u00f3ria](/pt-BR/concepts/memory) - O sistema unificado de mem\u00f3ria usado pelo aprendizado HITL\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/mcp/dsl-integration.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/mcp/dsl-integration.mdx\nindex ec036e4205..81d4dc9032 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/mcp/dsl-integration.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/mcp/dsl-integration.mdx\n@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ A integra\u00e7\u00e3o DSL (Domain Specific Language) MCP do CrewAI oferece a **forma ma\n <Info>\n   Esta \u00e9 a **abordagem recomendada** para a maioria dos casos de uso de MCP.\n   Para cen\u00e1rios avan\u00e7ados que requerem gerenciamento manual de conex\u00e3o, veja\n-  [MCPServerAdapter](/pt-BR/mcp/overview#advanced-mcpserveradapter).\n+  [MCPServerAdapter](/pt-BR/mcp/overview).\n </Info>\n \n ## Uso B\u00e1sico\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/quickstart.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/quickstart.mdx\nindex df783f5fa6..3b2aa417e8 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/quickstart.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/quickstart.mdx\n@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ Se ainda n\u00e3o instalou o CrewAI, siga primeiro o [guia de instala\u00e7\u00e3o](/pt-BR/i\n ## Pr\u00e9-requisitos\n \n - Ambiente Python e a CLI do CrewAI (veja [instala\u00e7\u00e3o](/pt-BR/installation))\n-- Um LLM configurado com as chaves corretas \u2014 veja [LLMs](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#setting-up-your-llm)\n+- Um LLM configurado com as chaves corretas \u2014 veja [LLMs](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#configurando-seu-llm)\n - Uma chave de API do [Serper.dev](https://serper.dev/) (`SERPER_API_KEY`) para busca na web neste tutorial\n \n ## Construa seu primeiro Flow\n@@ -155,7 +155,7 @@ Se ainda n\u00e3o instalou o CrewAI, siga primeiro o [guia de instala\u00e7\u00e3o](/pt-BR/i\n   Na raiz do projeto, no arquivo `.env`, defina:\n \n     - `SERPER_API_KEY` \u2014 obtida em [Serper.dev](https://serper.dev/)\n-    - As chaves do provedor de modelo conforme necess\u00e1rio \u2014 veja [configura\u00e7\u00e3o de LLM](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#setting-up-your-llm)\n+    - As chaves do provedor de modelo conforme necess\u00e1rio \u2014 veja [configura\u00e7\u00e3o de LLM](/pt-BR/concepts/llms#configurando-seu-llm)\n   </Step>\n \n   <Step title=\"Instalar e executar\">\n@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@ Se ainda n\u00e3o instalou o CrewAI, siga primeiro o [guia de instala\u00e7\u00e3o](/pt-BR/i\n 2. **Crew** \u2014 `kickoff_content_crew` carrega `crew.jsonc` e executa uma tarefa com um agente: o pesquisador usa **Serper** na web e escreve o relat\u00f3rio.\n 3. **Artefato** \u2014 O `output_file` da tarefa grava o relat\u00f3rio em `output/report.md`.\n \n-Para ir al\u00e9m em Flows (roteamento, persist\u00eancia, human-in-the-loop), veja [Construa seu primeiro Flow](/pt-BR/guides/flows/first-flow) e [Flows](/pt-BR/concepts/flows). Para crews sem Flow, veja [Crews](/pt-BR/concepts/crews). Para um \u00fanico `Agent` com `kickoff()` sem tarefas, veja [Agents](/pt-BR/concepts/agents#direct-agent-interaction-with-kickoff).\n+Para ir al\u00e9m em Flows (roteamento, persist\u00eancia, human-in-the-loop), veja [Construa seu primeiro Flow](/pt-BR/guides/flows/first-flow) e [Flows](/pt-BR/concepts/flows). Para crews sem Flow, veja [Crews](/pt-BR/concepts/crews). Para um \u00fanico `Agent` com `kickoff()` sem tarefas, veja [Agents](/pt-BR/concepts/agents).\n \n <Check>\n Voc\u00ea tem um Flow ponta a ponta com um crew de agente e um relat\u00f3rio salvo \u2014 uma base s\u00f3lida para novas etapas, crews ou ferramentas.\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool.mdx\nindex 9b48a51e49..9364156cbe 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool.mdx\n@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ Esse ambiente \u00e9 bastante limitado, com restri\u00e7\u00f5es severas a v\u00e1rios m\u00f3dulos\n ### Execu\u00e7\u00e3o N\u00e3o Segura\n \n **N\u00c3O RECOMENDADO PARA PRODU\u00c7\u00c3O**\n-Este modo permite a execu\u00e7\u00e3o de qualquer c\u00f3digo Python, inclusive chamadas perigosas para os m\u00f3dulos `sys, os..` e semelhantes. [Veja aqui](/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool#enabling-unsafe-mode) como habilitar este modo.\n+Este modo permite a execu\u00e7\u00e3o de qualquer c\u00f3digo Python, inclusive chamadas perigosas para os m\u00f3dulos `sys, os..` e semelhantes. [Veja aqui](/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/codeinterpretertool) como habilitar este modo.\n \n ## Registro de Logs\n \n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "docs: internal anchor links point to English slugs on translated (ko/pt-BR/ar) pages\n## Summary\n\nInternal anchor links in the docs point to English heading slugs, but the headings on the translated pages (ko / pt-BR / ar) are localized, so the anchors no longer exist. The same audit also found two broken anchors in the English docs themselves.\n\n## Evidence (all verified against the live site)\n\nExample: `docs/edge/pt-BR/quickstart.mdx` links to `/pt-BR/concepts/llms#setting-up-your-llm`, but the pt-BR page heading is \"Configurando seu LLM\", which renders as `id=\"configurando-seu-llm\"` on https://docs.crewai.com/pt-BR/concepts/llms. The English slug `setting-up-your-llm` appears 0 times on that page.\n\nAnother example from the English docs: `en/learn/human-feedback-in-flows.mdx` links to `/en/concepts/flows#persistence`, but the heading is \"Flow Persistence\" (`id=\"flow-persistence\"`, verified live).\n\n## Affected patterns\n\n- `#setting-up-your-llm` -> ko `#llm-\uc124\uc815\ud558\uae30` / pt-BR `#configurando-seu-llm` / ar `#\u0625\u0639\u062f\u0627\u062f-llm-\u0627\u0644\u062e\u0627\u0635-\u0628\u0643`\n- `#direct-agent-interaction-with-kickoff` -> ko `#kickoff-\uc744-\uc0ac\uc6a9\ud55c-\uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8-\uc9c1\uc811-\uc0c1\ud638\uc791\uc6a9` (section absent in pt-BR/ar -> page-level link)\n- `#event-listeners` -> \"Creating a Custom Event Listener\" section per locale (anchor does not exist even on the en page)\n- `#task-guardrails`, `#building-your-crews`, `#persistence`, `#router`, `#advanced-mcpserveradapter`, `#enabling-unsafe-mode` (en slug is `enabling-unsafe_mode` with underscore), `#provider-configuration-examples`\n- Links to sections that were never translated (ko/pt-BR mcp overview \"Advanced: MCPServerAdapter\", codeinterpretertool \"Enabling unsafe_mode\", flows \"Building your Crews\") -> drop the fragment, keep the page-level link\n\n## Scope\n\n38 link fixes across 28 files, applied to both `docs/edge` and `docs/v1.15.28` (56 files total). Every replacement target was verified against the rendered `id=` attributes on the live docs site (including Arabic diacritics, e.g. `id=\"\u0627\u0644\u0645\u0648\u062c\u0651\u0647\"` for the Router heading).\n\nPR to follow.\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-23T11:42:52Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8426, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8426", "issue_numbers": ["8425"], "base_commit": "de0a167dc45049b9f555a7cc5d137d3052be932e", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/_actions.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/_actions.py\nindex bf820cebe2..1328f923c0 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/_actions.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/_actions.py\n@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ def run(self, *_args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:\n             ToolExecutionFailedError,\n             ToolFailureRecord,\n             detect_tool_failure,\n+            handle_tool_failure,\n         )\n \n         local_context = _pop_local_context(kwargs)\n@@ -122,11 +123,26 @@ def run(self, *_args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:\n         ).render_template()\n         result = self.tool.run(**rendered)\n         if failure := detect_tool_failure(result):\n-            raise ToolExecutionFailedError(\n-                ToolFailureRecord(\n-                    tool_name=self.tool.name, failure=failure, tool_args=rendered\n+            if getattr(self.tool, \"tool_failure_policy\", None) is not None:\n+                # The tool declares an explicit policy, which per BaseTool's\n+                # contract overrides everything for this tool: WARN records\n+                # the failure, emits ToolFailureDetectedEvent and the flow\n+                # continues; IGNORE stays silent; RAISE aborts. Only a tool\n+                # that sets no policy keeps flow actions' fail-hard default.\n+                handle_tool_failure(\n+                    failure,\n+                    tool_name=self.tool.name,\n+                    tool_args=rendered,\n+                    tool=self.tool,\n+                )\n+            else:\n+                raise ToolExecutionFailedError(\n+                    ToolFailureRecord(\n+                        tool_name=self.tool.name,\n+                        failure=failure,\n+                        tool_args=rendered,\n+                    )\n                 )\n-            )\n         return result\n \n     def _build_tool(self) -> Any:\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_tool_action_failure_policy.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_tool_action_failure_policy.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..51489f5dc0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_tool_action_failure_policy.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@\n+\"\"\"Flow tool actions must honor the tool's explicit ``tool_failure_policy``.\n+\n+``BaseTool.tool_failure_policy`` documents \"Overrides the agent's and task's\n+tool_failure_policy for this tool only\", and the agent execution path resolves\n+it (``handle_tool_failure`` / ``resolve_tool_failure_policy``): WARN records\n+the failure, emits ``ToolFailureDetectedEvent`` and continues; IGNORE stays\n+silent; only RAISE aborts. A tool action that raises on every detected\n+``ToolFailure`` regardless of the declared policy breaks that contract and\n+gives flows zero observability (no ``ToolFailureDetectedEvent`` at all).\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from crewai.events.event_bus import crewai_event_bus\n+from crewai.events.types.tool_usage_events import ToolFailureDetectedEvent\n+from crewai.flow import Flow\n+from crewai.flow.flow_definition import FlowDefinition\n+from crewai.tools import BaseTool, ToolFailure\n+from crewai.tools.tool_failure import ToolExecutionFailedError, ToolFailurePolicy\n+\n+\n+class WarnPolicyTool(BaseTool):\n+    name: str = \"WarnPolicyTool\"\n+    description: str = \"Reports a soft failure under an explicit WARN policy.\"\n+    tool_failure_policy: ToolFailurePolicy = ToolFailurePolicy.WARN\n+\n+    def _run(self) -> ToolFailure:\n+        return ToolFailure(message=\"soft failure\", code=\"soft\")\n+\n+\n+class RaisePolicyTool(BaseTool):\n+    name: str = \"RaisePolicyTool\"\n+    description: str = \"Reports a failure under an explicit RAISE policy.\"\n+    tool_failure_policy: ToolFailurePolicy = ToolFailurePolicy.RAISE\n+\n+    def _run(self) -> ToolFailure:\n+        return ToolFailure(message=\"fatal failure\", code=\"fatal\")\n+\n+\n+def _tool_flow(ref: str) -> Flow:\n+    definition = FlowDefinition.from_declaration(\n+        contents={\n+            \"schema\": \"crewai.flow/v1\",\n+            \"name\": \"ToolFailurePolicyFlow\",\n+            \"methods\": {\n+                \"run_tool\": {\n+                    \"start\": True,\n+                    \"do\": {\"call\": \"tool\", \"ref\": ref, \"with\": {}},\n+                }\n+            },\n+        }\n+    )\n+    return Flow.from_declaration(contents=definition)\n+\n+\n+def test_warn_policy_tool_does_not_kill_the_flow():\n+    events: list[ToolFailureDetectedEvent] = []\n+\n+    with crewai_event_bus.scoped_handlers():\n+\n+        @crewai_event_bus.on(ToolFailureDetectedEvent)\n+        def on_failure(source, event):\n+            events.append(event)\n+\n+        flow = _tool_flow(f\"{__name__}:WarnPolicyTool\")\n+        result = flow.kickoff()\n+\n+    # Under the tool's explicit WARN policy the flow completes (the soft\n+    # failure is the step's output) and the failure is observable.\n+    assert isinstance(result, ToolFailure), \"WARN policy must not abort the flow\"\n+    assert events, \"expected a ToolFailureDetectedEvent under the WARN policy\"\n+\n+\n+def test_raise_policy_tool_still_aborts_the_flow():\n+    flow = _tool_flow(f\"{__name__}:RaisePolicyTool\")\n+    with pytest.raises(ToolExecutionFailedError, match=\"fatal failure\"):\n+        flow.kickoff()\n", "problem_statement": "Flow tool actions ignore tool_failure_policy: WARN/IGNORE tools kill the flow and no ToolFailureDetectedEvent is emitted\n## Description\n\nA flow tool action raises `ToolExecutionFailedError` on **every** detected `ToolFailure`, regardless of the tool's explicit `tool_failure_policy`. A tool configured with `WARN` (or `IGNORE`) still aborts the whole flow, and because the raise bypasses `handle_tool_failure` entirely, **no `ToolFailureDetectedEvent` is ever emitted** \u2014 flow tool failures have zero observability on the event bus.\n\nThis regressed in #8367, which added the failure detection to `ToolAction.run`.\n\n## How to reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom crewai.flow import Flow\nfrom crewai.flow.flow_definition import FlowDefinition\nfrom crewai.tools import BaseTool, ToolFailure\nfrom crewai.tools.tool_failure import ToolFailurePolicy\n\n\nclass WarnPolicyTool(BaseTool):\n    name: str = \"WarnPolicyTool\"\n    description: str = \"Reports a soft failure under an explicit WARN policy.\"\n    tool_failure_policy: ToolFailurePolicy = ToolFailurePolicy.WARN\n\n    def _run(self) -> ToolFailure:\n        return ToolFailure(message=\"soft failure\", code=\"soft\")\n\n\ndefinition = FlowDefinition.from_declaration(\n    contents={\n        \"schema\": \"crewai.flow/v1\",\n        \"name\": \"ToolFailurePolicyFlow\",\n        \"methods\": {\n            \"run_tool\": {\n                \"start\": True,\n                \"do\": {\"call\": \"tool\", \"ref\": \"__main__:WarnPolicyTool\", \"with\": {}},\n            }\n        },\n    }\n)\nFlow.from_declaration(contents=definition).kickoff()\n# ToolExecutionFailedError: Tool 'WarnPolicyTool' failed: soft failure (code: soft)\n# ...and 0 ToolFailureDetectedEvent on the event bus\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`BaseTool.tool_failure_policy` is documented as:\n\n> Overrides the agent's and task's tool_failure_policy for this tool only. None inherits.\n\nand the agent execution path honors it via `resolve_tool_failure_policy` / `handle_tool_failure` (`tools/tool_failure.py`): **WARN** records the failure and emits `ToolFailureDetectedEvent` while execution continues; **IGNORE** stays silent; only **RAISE** aborts. The same tool run through a flow should not silently change semantics based on the caller.\n\n## Observed behavior\n\n`ToolAction.run` (`flow/runtime/_actions.py`) does `if failure := detect_tool_failure(result): raise ToolExecutionFailedError(...)` unconditionally \u2014 the policy system is never consulted and the failure never reaches `handle_tool_failure` (so no event, no failure record).\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nIn `ToolAction.run`, when the tool declares an explicit `tool_failure_policy`, route the detected failure through `handle_tool_failure(failure, tool_name=..., tool_args=..., tool=self.tool)`; keep the hard raise only for tools that set no policy (preserving #8367's default). Happy to send a PR with tests.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-22T16:24:20Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8424, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8424", "issue_numbers": ["8423"], "base_commit": "2a5548a233d3a673ca73ff74d3bf98ea5f57ea67", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/__init__.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/__init__.py\nindex 8b7a3cf104..a0c79e9c0b 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/__init__.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/__init__.py\n@@ -2096,6 +2096,20 @@ async def run_flow() -> Any:\n         output_holder.append(stream_session)\n         return stream_session\n \n+    def _reset_tool_action_usage_budgets(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Give every tool action a fresh usage budget for this run.\n+\n+        Tool actions build their tools once (``_flow_post_init``) and reuse\n+        them across kickoffs, so ``current_usage_count`` would otherwise\n+        survive runs. Agents zero the counter each time they prepare tools\n+        (``parse_tools``); flows reset at the kickoff boundary instead. A\n+        budget exhausted in an earlier kickoff must not fail later ones.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        for tool in getattr(self, \"_tool_action_tools\", None) or ():\n+            reset = getattr(tool, \"reset_usage_count\", None)\n+            if callable(reset):\n+                reset()\n+\n     def kickoff(\n         self,\n         inputs: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n@@ -2208,6 +2222,7 @@ async def kickoff_async(\n                 restore_from_state_id=restore_from_state_id,\n             )\n \n+        self._reset_tool_action_usage_budgets()\n         self._cel_now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n \n         ctx = baggage.set_baggage(\"flow_inputs\", inputs or {})\ndiff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/_actions.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/_actions.py\nindex afa25de3c9..bf820cebe2 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/_actions.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/runtime/_actions.py\n@@ -98,6 +98,16 @@ def __init__(self, flow: Flow[Any], definition: FlowToolActionDefinition) -> Non\n         self.definition = definition\n         self.tool = self._build_tool()\n         self.kwargs = definition.with_ or {}\n+        # Tool instances are built once per flow object and reused across\n+        # kickoffs; register the tool so each kickoff can reset its usage\n+        # budget (Flow._reset_tool_action_usage_budgets). Without the reset,\n+        # current_usage_count survives runs and a budget exhausted in an\n+        # earlier kickoff makes every later kickoff fail.\n+        tools = getattr(flow, \"_tool_action_tools\", None)\n+        if tools is None:\n+            tools = []\n+            object.__setattr__(flow, \"_tool_action_tools\", tools)\n+        tools.append(self.tool)\n \n     def run(self, *_args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:\n         from crewai.tools.tool_failure import (\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_tool_action_usage.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_tool_action_usage.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..dbb3d0c45b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_tool_action_usage.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@\n+\"\"\"Flow tool actions must get a fresh tool usage budget for every kickoff.\n+\n+Tool actions build their tool instances once per flow object (in\n+``_flow_post_init``) and reuse them across kickoffs. Without resetting\n+``current_usage_count`` at the kickoff boundary, a ``max_usage_count`` budget\n+exhausted in an earlier kickoff makes every later kickoff of the same flow\n+object fail with ``ToolExecutionFailedError`` (``BaseTool.run`` answers with a\n+``ToolFailure(USAGE_LIMIT)`` and the tool action turns it fatal).\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from crewai.flow import Flow\n+from crewai.flow.flow_definition import FlowDefinition\n+from crewai.tools import BaseTool\n+from crewai.tools.tool_failure import ToolExecutionFailedError\n+\n+\n+class BudgetedEchoTool(BaseTool):\n+    name: str = \"BudgetedEchoTool\"\n+    description: str = \"Echo tool with a per-run usage budget.\"\n+    max_usage_count: int = 2\n+\n+    def _run(self, text: str) -> str:\n+        return f\"ok:{text}\"\n+\n+\n+class SingleShotTool(BaseTool):\n+    name: str = \"SingleShotTool\"\n+    description: str = \"Single-shot tool.\"\n+    max_usage_count: int = 1\n+\n+    def _run(self, text: str) -> str:\n+        return f\"ok:{text}\"\n+\n+\n+def _tool_flow(ref: str, with_: dict) -> Flow:\n+    definition = FlowDefinition.from_declaration(\n+        contents={\n+            \"schema\": \"crewai.flow/v1\",\n+            \"name\": \"ToolUsageBudgetFlow\",\n+            \"methods\": {\n+                \"run_tool\": {\n+                    \"start\": True,\n+                    \"do\": {\"call\": \"tool\", \"ref\": ref, \"with\": with_},\n+                }\n+            },\n+        }\n+    )\n+    return Flow.from_declaration(contents=definition)\n+\n+\n+def test_tool_action_usage_budget_resets_between_kickoffs():\n+    flow = _tool_flow(f\"{__name__}:BudgetedEchoTool\", {\"text\": \"${state.text}\"})\n+    assert flow.kickoff(inputs={\"text\": \"a\"}) == \"ok:a\"\n+    assert flow.kickoff(inputs={\"text\": \"b\"}) == \"ok:b\"\n+    # Third kickoff on the same flow object: without the per-kickoff reset the\n+    # shared tool instance's current_usage_count (2) already meets the budget,\n+    # so BaseTool.run returns ToolFailure(USAGE_LIMIT) and the flow crashes.\n+    assert flow.kickoff(inputs={\"text\": \"c\"}) == \"ok:c\"\n+\n+\n+def test_tool_action_usage_budget_still_enforced_within_a_kickoff():\n+    # The budget is per kickoff, not per call: an each: loop invoking a\n+    # max_usage_count=1 tool twice in ONE kickoff still exhausts it mid-run.\n+    definition = FlowDefinition.from_declaration(\n+        contents={\n+            \"schema\": \"crewai.flow/v1\",\n+            \"name\": \"EachBudgetFlow\",\n+            \"methods\": {\n+                \"loop\": {\n+                    \"start\": True,\n+                    \"do\": {\n+                        \"call\": \"each\",\n+                        \"in\": \"${state.items}\",\n+                        \"do\": [\n+                            {\n+                                \"name\": \"call_tool\",\n+                                \"action\": {\n+                                    \"call\": \"tool\",\n+                                    \"ref\": f\"{__name__}:SingleShotTool\",\n+                                    \"with\": {\"text\": \"${item}\"},\n+                                },\n+                            }\n+                        ],\n+                    },\n+                }\n+            },\n+        }\n+    )\n+    flow = Flow.from_declaration(contents=definition)\n+    with pytest.raises(ToolExecutionFailedError, match=\"usage limit\"):\n+        flow.kickoff(inputs={\"items\": [\"a\", \"b\"]})\n", "problem_statement": "Flow tool actions leak max_usage_count across kickoffs \u2014 the flow permanently fails after the budget is exhausted once\n## Description\n\nA flow tool action's tool instance (and its `current_usage_count`) is built once per `Flow` object and never reset between kickoffs. After the tool's `max_usage_count` budget is consumed, **every subsequent kickoff of the same flow object crashes** with `ToolExecutionFailedError`.\n\nSince #8367 turned a detected `ToolFailure` into a hard `raise`, the previously silent `ToolFailure(reason=USAGE_LIMIT)` returned by `BaseTool.run` now kills the run \u2014 so the leak became a permanent failure for long-lived flow objects (services, loops re-kicking the same flow).\n\n## How to reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom crewai.flow import Flow\nfrom crewai.flow.flow_definition import FlowDefinition\nfrom crewai.tools import BaseTool\n\n\nclass BudgetedEchoTool(BaseTool):\n    name: str = \"BudgetedEchoTool\"\n    description: str = \"Echo tool with a per-run usage budget.\"\n    max_usage_count: int = 2\n\n    def _run(self, text: str) -> str:\n        return f\"ok:{text}\"\n\n\ndefinition = FlowDefinition.from_declaration(\n    contents={\n        \"schema\": \"crewai.flow/v1\",\n        \"name\": \"ToolUsageBudgetFlow\",\n        \"methods\": {\n            \"run_tool\": {\n                \"start\": True,\n                \"do\": {\n                    \"call\": \"tool\",\n                    \"ref\": \"__main__:BudgetedEchoTool\",\n                    \"with\": {\"text\": \"${state.text}\"},\n                },\n            }\n        },\n    }\n)\nflow = Flow.from_declaration(contents=definition)\n\nprint(flow.kickoff(inputs={\"text\": \"a\"}))  # ok:a\nprint(flow.kickoff(inputs={\"text\": \"b\"}))  # ok:b  (budget now exhausted)\nprint(flow.kickoff(inputs={\"text\": \"c\"}))  # ToolExecutionFailedError:\n# Tool 'BudgetedEchoTool' has reached its usage limit of 2 times and cannot be used anymore.\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n- `ToolAction.__init__` builds the tool once (`_flow_post_init` runs a single time per flow object) and reuses `self.tool` for every kickoff; `current_usage_count` is never reset.\n- The agent path resets the counter every time tools are prepared (`utilities/agent_utils.py` `parse_tools`: `structured_tool.current_usage_count = 0`); the flow runtime has no equivalent at the kickoff boundary.\n- `BaseTool.run` does not raise on budget exhaustion \u2014 it returns `ToolFailure(reason=USAGE_LIMIT)`. #8367's `detect_tool_failure` \u2192 `raise ToolExecutionFailedError` then converts that leaked soft failure into a fatal flow error on kickoff N+1.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nA usage budget should apply **per kickoff** (mirroring the agent path, which zeroes the counter each time tools are prepared), not for the lifetime of the flow object. A budget exhausted in one run must not break later runs.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nReset tool usage counters at the kickoff boundary \u2014 e.g. register the tools built by `ToolAction` and call `reset_usage_count()` on each at the start of `kickoff_async` (the single seam every run path \u2014 `kickoff`, `kickoff_async`, `astream`, checkpoint resume \u2014 goes through).\n\nHappy to send a PR with regression tests.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-22T16:22:18Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8420, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8420", "issue_numbers": ["8419"], "base_commit": "0b5053e33faee24f5d04133f668bfe97323275bf", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\nindex d9fbcc1145..fe33471fe9 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\n@@ -2344,20 +2344,23 @@ def test(\n \n         Uses concurrent.futures for concurrent execution.\n         \"\"\"\n+        # Emit the start event before setup: crew_test_failed is\n+        # scope-ending, so a failure during create_llm must find its opener\n+        # already on the stack instead of popping the caller's scope.\n+        crewai_event_bus.emit(\n+            self,\n+            CrewTestStartedEvent(\n+                crew_name=self.name,\n+                n_iterations=n_iterations,\n+                eval_llm=eval_llm,\n+                inputs=inputs,\n+            ),\n+        )\n         try:\n             llm_instance = create_llm(eval_llm)\n             if not llm_instance:\n                 raise ValueError(\"Failed to create LLM instance.\")\n \n-            crewai_event_bus.emit(\n-                self,\n-                CrewTestStartedEvent(\n-                    crew_name=self.name,\n-                    n_iterations=n_iterations,\n-                    eval_llm=llm_instance,\n-                    inputs=inputs,\n-                ),\n-            )\n             test_crew = self.copy()\n \n             evaluator = CrewEvaluator(test_crew, llm_instance)\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\nindex 89491b9b4c..f20b180edc 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\n@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@\n     CrewKickoffFailedEvent,\n     CrewKickoffStartedEvent,\n     CrewTestCompletedEvent,\n+    CrewTestFailedEvent,\n     CrewTestStartedEvent,\n     CrewTrainCompletedEvent,\n     CrewTrainStartedEvent,\n@@ -4276,6 +4277,50 @@ def on_crew_test_completed(source, event: CrewTestCompletedEvent):\n     assert isinstance(received_events[1], CrewTestCompletedEvent)\n \n \n+def test_crew_test_setup_failure_pairs_events(researcher):\n+    \"\"\"A failure during test() setup must still pair Started with Failed.\n+\n+    crew_test_failed is scope-ending: the start event used to be emitted\n+    only after create_llm succeeded, so a create_llm failure emitted an\n+    unpaired Failed that popped the caller's enclosing event scope.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    task = Task(\n+        description=\"Summarize the topic.\",\n+        expected_output=\"A summary.\",\n+        agent=researcher,\n+    )\n+    crew = Crew(agents=[researcher], tasks=[task])\n+\n+    started: list[CrewTestStartedEvent] = []\n+    failed: list[CrewTestFailedEvent] = []\n+\n+    @crewai_event_bus.on(CrewTestStartedEvent)\n+    def on_started(source, event: CrewTestStartedEvent):\n+        started.append(event)\n+\n+    @crewai_event_bus.on(CrewTestFailedEvent)\n+    def on_failed(source, event: CrewTestFailedEvent):\n+        failed.append(event)\n+\n+    crewai_event_bus.register_handler(CrewTestStartedEvent, on_started)\n+    crewai_event_bus.register_handler(CrewTestFailedEvent, on_failed)\n+    try:\n+        with patch(\"crewai.crew.create_llm\", side_effect=RuntimeError(\"no key\")):\n+            with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match=\"no key\"):\n+                crew.test(2, \"gpt-4o-mini\")\n+        crewai_event_bus.flush()\n+    finally:\n+        crewai_event_bus.off(CrewTestStartedEvent, on_started)\n+        crewai_event_bus.off(CrewTestFailedEvent, on_failed)\n+\n+    assert started, \"test() must emit CrewTestStartedEvent before setup runs\"\n+    assert failed, \"test() setup failure must emit CrewTestFailedEvent\"\n+    assert failed[-1].started_event_id == started[-1].event_id, (\n+        \"the Failed event must pair with the test's own start event, not pop \"\n+        \"the caller's enclosing scope\"\n+    )\n+\n+\n def test_hierarchical_verbose_manager_agent(researcher, writer):\n     task = Task(\n         description=\"Come up with a list of 5 interesting ideas to explore for an article, then write one amazing paragraph highlight for each idea that showcases how good an article about this topic could be. Return the list of ideas with their paragraph and your notes.\",\n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] Crew.test emits CrewTestFailedEvent with no CrewTestStartedEvent when create_llm fails \u2014 unpaired scope-ending event pops the caller's scope\n### Description\n\n`Crew.test` (`crew.py`) emits `CrewTestStartedEvent` only AFTER `create_llm(eval_llm)` succeeds. The `except` emits `CrewTestFailedEvent` unconditionally \u2014 and `crew_test_failed` is a **scope-ending** event (`VALID_EVENT_PAIRS['crew_test_failed'] = 'crew_test_started'`), so a setup failure (bad model spec, missing key) emits an unpaired Failed that pops whatever enclosing event scope is open in the calling context, corrupting later event parentage. Same theft shape as the a2a delegation bug (#8407), reached through the test harness path.\n\n`CrewTestStartedEvent.eval_llm` is typed `str | Any | None`, so the start event can carry the requested spec before the instance exists \u2014 the opener can simply move above the setup.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```python\nwith patch(\"crewai.crew.create_llm\", side_effect=RuntimeError(\"no key\")):\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError):\n        crew.test(2, \"gpt-4o-mini\")\n# observed: CrewTestFailedEvent emitted with no CrewTestStartedEvent \u2014\n# started_event_id is None and the enclosing scope frame is consumed\n```\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nEmit the start event before `create_llm` (passing the requested `eval_llm` spec, which the field type already allows) so every Failed has its opener. I can open a PR with a regression test asserting the Failed event pairs with the test's own start event.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-22T15:39:15Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8418, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8418", "issue_numbers": ["8417"], "base_commit": "90192810cf939f4f7d1057ecd48bd9b7464a8369", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\nindex ecab6d596c..d9fbcc1145 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\n@@ -2162,7 +2162,21 @@ def replay(self, task_id: str, inputs: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> CrewOutp\n             self.tasks[i].output = task_output\n \n         self._logging_color = \"bold_blue\"\n-        return self._execute_tasks(self.tasks, start_index, True)\n+        try:\n+            return self._execute_tasks(self.tasks, start_index, True)\n+        except Exception as e:\n+            # Mirror kickoff()'s failure terminal: the start event above is\n+            # scope-starting, so a failed replay must close its own scope or\n+            # the leaked frame parents every later event in this context.\n+            crewai_event_bus.emit(\n+                self,\n+                CrewKickoffFailedEvent(\n+                    error=str(e),\n+                    crew_name=self.name,\n+                    started_event_id=self._kickoff_event_id,\n+                ),\n+            )\n+            raise\n \n     def query_knowledge(\n         self, query: list[str], results_limit: int = 3, score_threshold: float = 0.35\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\nindex 1205fae83d..89491b9b4c 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\n@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@\n from crewai.crews.crew_output import CrewOutput\n from crewai.events.event_bus import crewai_event_bus\n from crewai.events.types.crew_events import (\n+    CrewKickoffFailedEvent,\n     CrewKickoffStartedEvent,\n     CrewTestCompletedEvent,\n     CrewTestStartedEvent,\n@@ -3207,6 +3208,153 @@ def on_started(source, event: CrewKickoffStartedEvent):\n     assert crew._kickoff_event_id == replay_starts[-1].event_id\n \n \n+def test_replay_failure_emits_kickoff_failed_event(researcher, writer):\n+    \"\"\"A failed replay must terminate its own start event like kickoff() does.\n+\n+    replay() emits CrewKickoffStartedEvent (scoping the completion), but its\n+    execution tail had no except: a failure raised out of _execute_tasks left\n+    the start event dangling \u2014 no CrewKickoffFailedEvent for listeners, and a\n+    leaked crew_kickoff_started frame on the event-scope stack that parents\n+    every later event in the context.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    list_ideas = Task(\n+        description=\"Generate a list of 5 interesting ideas.\",\n+        expected_output=\"Bullet point list of 5 ideas.\",\n+        agent=researcher,\n+    )\n+    write = Task(\n+        description=\"Write a sentence about the events\",\n+        expected_output=\"A sentence about the events\",\n+        agent=writer,\n+        context=[list_ideas],\n+    )\n+\n+    crew = Crew(\n+        agents=[researcher, writer],\n+        tasks=[list_ideas, write],\n+        process=Process.sequential,\n+    )\n+\n+    started_events: list[CrewKickoffStartedEvent] = []\n+    failed_events: list[CrewKickoffFailedEvent] = []\n+\n+    def on_started(source, event: CrewKickoffStartedEvent):\n+        started_events.append(event)\n+\n+    def on_failed(source, event: CrewKickoffFailedEvent):\n+        failed_events.append(event)\n+\n+    crewai_event_bus.register_handler(CrewKickoffStartedEvent, on_started)\n+    crewai_event_bus.register_handler(CrewKickoffFailedEvent, on_failed)\n+    try:\n+        with patch.object(Task, \"execute_sync\") as mock_execute_task:\n+            mock_execute_task.side_effect = [\n+                TaskOutput(\n+                    description=task.description,\n+                    raw=\"Mocked output\",\n+                    agent=\"Researcher\",\n+                    json_dict=None,\n+                    output_format=OutputFormat.RAW,\n+                    pydantic=None,\n+                    summary=\"Mocked output\",\n+                    messages=[],\n+                )\n+                for task in [list_ideas, write]\n+            ]\n+            crew.kickoff()\n+        kickoff_start_ids = {event.event_id for event in started_events}\n+\n+        with patch.object(Task, \"execute_sync\") as mock_execute_task:\n+            mock_execute_task.side_effect = RuntimeError(\"boom during replay\")\n+            with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match=\"boom during replay\"):\n+                crew.replay(str(write.id))\n+        crewai_event_bus.flush()\n+    finally:\n+        crewai_event_bus.off(CrewKickoffStartedEvent, on_started)\n+        crewai_event_bus.off(CrewKickoffFailedEvent, on_failed)\n+\n+    replay_starts = [\n+        event for event in started_events if event.event_id not in kickoff_start_ids\n+    ]\n+    assert replay_starts, \"replay() must emit its own CrewKickoffStartedEvent\"\n+    assert failed_events, (\n+        \"replay() failure emitted no CrewKickoffFailedEvent; the \"\n+        \"CrewKickoffStartedEvent from replay is left dangling\"\n+    )\n+    assert failed_events[-1].started_event_id == replay_starts[-1].event_id\n+    assert \"boom during replay\" in failed_events[-1].error\n+\n+\n+def test_replay_failure_does_not_leak_kickoff_scope_into_next_kickoff(\n+    researcher, writer,\n+):\n+    \"\"\"The leaked replay start scope must not parent the next kickoff's events.\"\"\"\n+    from crewai.events.event_context import _event_id_stack\n+\n+    list_ideas = Task(\n+        description=\"Generate a list of 5 interesting ideas.\",\n+        expected_output=\"Bullet point list of 5 ideas.\",\n+        agent=researcher,\n+    )\n+    write = Task(\n+        description=\"Write a sentence about the events\",\n+        expected_output=\"A sentence about the events\",\n+        agent=writer,\n+        context=[list_ideas],\n+    )\n+\n+    crew = Crew(\n+        agents=[researcher, writer],\n+        tasks=[list_ideas, write],\n+        process=Process.sequential,\n+    )\n+\n+    def _mocked_outputs():\n+        return [\n+            TaskOutput(\n+                description=task.description,\n+                raw=\"Mocked output\",\n+                agent=\"Researcher\",\n+                json_dict=None,\n+                output_format=OutputFormat.RAW,\n+                pydantic=None,\n+                summary=\"Mocked output\",\n+                messages=[],\n+            )\n+            for task in [list_ideas, write]\n+        ]\n+\n+    started_events: list[CrewKickoffStartedEvent] = []\n+\n+    def on_started(source, event: CrewKickoffStartedEvent):\n+        started_events.append(event)\n+\n+    _event_id_stack.set(())\n+    crewai_event_bus.register_handler(CrewKickoffStartedEvent, on_started)\n+    try:\n+        with patch.object(Task, \"execute_sync\") as mock_execute_task:\n+            mock_execute_task.side_effect = _mocked_outputs()\n+            crew.kickoff()\n+\n+        with patch.object(Task, \"execute_sync\") as mock_execute_task:\n+            mock_execute_task.side_effect = RuntimeError(\"boom during replay\")\n+            with pytest.raises(RuntimeError):\n+                crew.replay(str(write.id))\n+\n+        with patch.object(Task, \"execute_sync\") as mock_execute_task:\n+            mock_execute_task.side_effect = _mocked_outputs()\n+            crew.kickoff()\n+        crewai_event_bus.flush()\n+    finally:\n+        crewai_event_bus.off(CrewKickoffStartedEvent, on_started)\n+        _event_id_stack.set(())\n+\n+    assert started_events[-1].parent_event_id is None, (\n+        \"previous failed replay's crew_kickoff_started scope leaked onto the \"\n+        \"event-id stack; the next kickoff's start event is parented to it\"\n+    )\n+\n+\n def test_replay_rejects_changed_task_order(researcher):\n     \"\"\"Replay must not restore a saved output onto a different current task.\"\"\"\n     research = Task(\n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] Crew.replay() emits CrewKickoffStartedEvent but no CrewKickoffFailedEvent on failure \u2014 leaked kickoff scope corrupts later event lineage\n### Description\n\n#8366 taught `replay()` to emit its own `CrewKickoffStartedEvent` so the success path's completion pairs correctly. But replay's execution tail (`crew.py`, `return self._execute_tasks(...)`) has no `except`, while `kickoff()`'s except-clause emits `CrewKickoffFailedEvent` (`crew_kickoff_failed` is a scope-ending event). A replay whose tasks raise therefore:\n\n1. leaves the replay's `crew_kickoff_started` frame on the thread-local event-scope stack \u2014 the stack is only popped by a scope-ending event;\n2. never signals the failure to `CrewKickoffFailedEvent` listeners (telemetry/trace listeners keep the replay dangling as in-flight);\n3. corrupts the lineage of everything after it in the same context \u2014 the next kickoff's `CrewKickoffStartedEvent.parent_event_id` points at the leaked replay frame instead of `None`;\n4. after enough failed replays on one thread, `push_event_scope` hits its depth limit and raises.\n\n### Reproduction (offline, `Task.execute_sync` mocked)\n\n```python\ncrew.kickoff()                                    # seed task outputs\nwith patch.object(Task, \"execute_sync\") as m:\n    m.side_effect = RuntimeError(\"boom\")\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError):\n        crew.replay(str(task_id))                  # fails mid-replay\n# observed: no CrewKickoffFailedEvent emitted; the next kickoff's start\n# event has parent_event_id == the leaked replay frame's id (must be None)\n```\n\nSame pairing class as #8402 (guardrail) and #8406 (a2a); this one is the failure-path gap left by #8366 itself.\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nWrap replay's tail in try/except emitting `CrewKickoffFailedEvent(error, crew_name, started_event_id=self._kickoff_event_id)` and re-raise \u2014 the exact shape of kickoff()'s except-clause. I can open a PR with the two regression tests above (scoped Failed event; no scope leak into the next kickoff).\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-22T15:29:23Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8403, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8403", "issue_numbers": ["8402"], "base_commit": "9f791dbfdad9b5b5c653e8a2f2c17b1e2ef414ce", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/utilities/guardrail.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/utilities/guardrail.py\nindex 8454ffd925..e0dfa8659f 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/utilities/guardrail.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/utilities/guardrail.py\n@@ -188,6 +188,24 @@ def process_guardrail(\n             ),\n         )\n         raise\n+    except Exception as e:\n+        # an exception ends the validation too; without a terminal event the\n+        # \"evaluate guardrail\" span survives until the end-of-execution sweep\n+        # closes it as orphaned, and the trace loses the real error\n+        crewai_event_bus.emit(\n+            event_source,\n+            LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent(\n+                success=False,\n+                result=None,\n+                error=f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\",\n+                retry_count=retry_count,\n+                guardrail_type=started_event.guardrail_type,\n+                guardrail_name=started_event.guardrail_name,\n+                from_agent=from_agent,\n+                from_task=from_task,\n+            ),\n+        )\n+        raise\n \n     guardrail_result = GuardrailResult.from_tuple(result)\n \n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_guardrail_events_on_exception.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_guardrail_events_on_exception.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..026c615bc0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_guardrail_events_on_exception.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@\n+\"\"\"A guardrail that raises owes its started event a terminal one.\n+\n+``process_guardrail`` emits ``LLMGuardrailStartedEvent`` before calling the\n+guardrail and ``LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent`` after it returns. A deny\n+(``HookAborted``) already gets its terminal event; an ordinary exception did\n+not, so the tracing listener's \"evaluate guardrail\" span stayed open until the\n+end-of-execution sweep closed it as \"orphaned\", losing the real error from the\n+trace. The caller sees the exception either way \u2014 only the event pairing\n+differs.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+from typing import Any\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from crewai.events.event_bus import crewai_event_bus\n+from crewai.events.types.llm_guardrail_events import (\n+    LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent,\n+    LLMGuardrailStartedEvent,\n+)\n+from crewai.tasks.task_output import TaskOutput\n+from crewai.utilities.guardrail import process_guardrail\n+\n+from tests.utils import wait_for_event_handlers\n+\n+\n+def test_a_raising_guardrail_still_reports_the_validation_it_started():\n+    task_output = TaskOutput(\n+        description=\"Say hi\", raw=\"hi\", agent=\"Doer\", expected_output=\"A greeting.\"\n+    )\n+\n+    def raising_guardrail(_output: Any) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n+        raise ValueError(\"guardrail exploded\")\n+\n+    started: list[LLMGuardrailStartedEvent] = []\n+    completed: list[LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent] = []\n+\n+    with crewai_event_bus.scoped_handlers():\n+\n+        @crewai_event_bus.on(LLMGuardrailStartedEvent)\n+        def _on_started(_source: Any, event: LLMGuardrailStartedEvent) -> None:\n+            started.append(event)\n+\n+        @crewai_event_bus.on(LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent)\n+        def _on_completed(_source: Any, event: LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent) -> None:\n+            completed.append(event)\n+\n+        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"guardrail exploded\"):\n+            process_guardrail(\n+                output=task_output, guardrail=raising_guardrail, retry_count=0\n+            )\n+\n+        wait_for_event_handlers()\n+\n+    assert len(started) == 1\n+    assert len(completed) == 1\n+    assert completed[0].success is False\n+    assert \"guardrail exploded\" in (completed[0].error or \"\")\n+\n+\n+def test_a_raising_guardrail_keeps_the_exception_for_the_caller():\n+    task_output = TaskOutput(\n+        description=\"Say hi\", raw=\"hi\", agent=\"Doer\", expected_output=\"A greeting.\"\n+    )\n+\n+    def raising_guardrail(_output: Any) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n+        raise RuntimeError(\"context lost\")\n+\n+    with crewai_event_bus.scoped_handlers():\n+        with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match=\"context lost\"):\n+            process_guardrail(\n+                output=task_output, guardrail=raising_guardrail, retry_count=1\n+            )\n+        wait_for_event_handlers()\n", "problem_statement": "A guardrail that raises leaves LLMGuardrailStartedEvent without its completed event, so the trace span closes as orphaned\n### Description\n\n`process_guardrail` (`lib/crewai/src/crewai/utilities/guardrail.py`) emits `LLMGuardrailStartedEvent` before calling the guardrail, and `LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent` after it returns. A `HookAborted` deny gets its terminal event before re-raising. An ordinary exception from the guardrail callable does not: it propagates immediately and the started event is left unpaired.\n\nThe tracing listener opens an `evaluate guardrail` span on the started event and closes it on the completed event (`telemetry/tracing/handlers.py`, `handle_llm_guardrail_started` / `handle_llm_guardrail_completed`). With the completed event missing, the span survives until `TelemetrySession.finish_spans()` force-closes it at end of execution with the status `Span orphaned \u2014 execution ended before completion event`. The real error (`ValueError: ...` from the guardrail) never reaches the trace; the orphan sweep label is all that remains. In a retry loop that mixes a raising guardrail with returning ones, every raise stacks another orphaned span.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```python\nfrom crewai.events.event_bus import crewai_event_bus\nfrom crewai.events.types.llm_guardrail_events import (\n    LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent,\n    LLMGuardrailStartedEvent,\n)\nfrom crewai.tasks.task_output import TaskOutput\nfrom crewai.utilities.guardrail import process_guardrail\n\nstarted, completed = [], []\n\ndef raising_guardrail(_output):\n    raise ValueError(\"guardrail exploded\")\n\nwith crewai_event_bus.scoped_handlers():\n    @crewai_event_bus.on(LLMGuardrailStartedEvent)\n    def _s(_src, event): started.append(event)\n\n    @crewai_event_bus.on(LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent)\n    def _c(_src, event): completed.append(event)\n\n    try:\n        process_guardrail(\n            output=TaskOutput(description=\"d\", raw=\"r\", agent=\"a\"),\n            guardrail=raising_guardrail,\n            retry_count=0,\n        )\n    except ValueError:\n        pass\n\nassert len(started) == 1\nassert len(completed) == 0  # <- the terminal event is missing\n```\n\nThe same shape is already handled for `HookAborted` in `process_guardrail` (added with the model-call hook deny propagation), and `tests/hooks/test_hook_abort_propagation.py::test_a_denied_guardrail_still_reports_the_validation_it_started` asserts the deny keeps the pairing. An exception deserves the same terminal event: it ends the validation just as decisively, and the trace should carry the real error instead of an orphan label.\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nMirror the existing `HookAborted` branch: catch `Exception` after it, emit `LLMGuardrailCompletedEvent(success=False, error=f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}`, retry_count=..., guardrail_type/name from the started event), then re-raise so caller behavior is unchanged. I can open a PR with the regression test above.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-22T11:16:42Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8400, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8400", "issue_numbers": ["8399"], "base_commit": "6ae4fb51edda686d67d9d0d6ffa157e18a63453d", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/recall_flow.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/recall_flow.py\nindex fbeb5c5c6d..f952199d38 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/recall_flow.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/recall_flow.py\n@@ -110,7 +110,11 @@ def _search_one(\n                 raw = [\n                     (r, s)\n                     for r, s in raw\n-                    if not r.private or r.source == self.state.source\n+                    # Match the shallow path: a private record with source=None\n+                    # must not leak to default (source=None) callers via\n+                    # None == None.\n+                    if not r.private\n+                    or (self.state.source is not None and r.source == self.state.source)\n                 ]\n             return scope, raw\n \ndiff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/unified_memory.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/unified_memory.py\nindex c0654a2bab..d37f0d82ba 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/unified_memory.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/unified_memory.py\n@@ -752,7 +752,12 @@ def recall(\n                         raw = [\n                             (r, s)\n                             for r, s in raw\n-                            if not r.private or r.source == source\n+                            # A private record is visible only to the source that\n+                            # created it. `r.source == source` alone would also\n+                            # match source=None records (None == None) and leak\n+                            # them to every default caller.\n+                            if not r.private\n+                            or (source is not None and r.source == source)\n                         ]\n                     results = []\n                     for r, s in raw:\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/memory/test_unified_memory.py b/lib/crewai/tests/memory/test_unified_memory.py\nindex 2ac391950b..19a4543577 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/memory/test_unified_memory.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/memory/test_unified_memory.py\n@@ -1315,3 +1315,93 @@ def test_close_drains_and_shuts_down(tmp_path: Path, mock_embedder: MagicMock) -\n     mem.close()\n     # After close, records should be persisted\n     assert mem._storage.count() == 1\n+\n+\n+def _memory_with_private_records(lancedb_path: Path):\n+    from crewai.memory.storage.lancedb_storage import LanceDBStorage\n+    from crewai.memory.unified_memory import Memory\n+\n+    storage = LanceDBStorage(path=str(lancedb_path), vector_dim=2)\n+    storage.save(\n+        [\n+            MemoryRecord(\n+                content=\"secret api key sk-abc123\",\n+                scope=\"/notes\",\n+                embedding=[1.0, 0.0],\n+                private=True,\n+                source=None,\n+            ),\n+            MemoryRecord(\n+                content=\"team-wide note\",\n+                scope=\"/notes\",\n+                embedding=[1.0, 0.0],\n+            ),\n+        ]\n+    )\n+    mem = Memory(\n+        llm=MagicMock(),\n+        storage=storage,\n+        embedder=lambda texts: [[1.0, 0.0]] * len(texts),\n+    )\n+    return mem\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"depth\", [\"shallow\", \"deep\"])\n+def test_private_record_without_source_does_not_leak(lancedb_path: Path, depth: str) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"A private record saved with source=None must not be visible to default\n+    (source=None, include_private=False) recalls.\n+\n+    The filter used to be `not r.private or r.source == source`, and\n+    `None == None` passed \u2014 every default caller saw the \"private\" record.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    mem = _memory_with_private_records(lancedb_path)\n+\n+    results = mem.recall(\n+        \"secret api key\", scope=\"/notes\", depth=depth, include_private=False\n+    )\n+\n+    contents = [m.record.content for m in results]\n+    assert \"secret api key sk-abc123\" not in contents, (\n+        \"private source=None record leaked to an unprivileged recall \"\n+        f\"({depth} path): {contents!r}\"\n+    )\n+    assert \"team-wide note\" in contents, \"public records must stay visible\"\n+\n+\n+def test_private_record_still_visible_to_its_source_and_when_included(lancedb_path: Path) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"The tightening must not hide private records from legitimate access.\"\"\"\n+    from crewai.memory.storage.lancedb_storage import LanceDBStorage\n+    from crewai.memory.types import MemoryRecord as MR\n+    from crewai.memory.unified_memory import Memory\n+\n+    storage = LanceDBStorage(path=str(lancedb_path), vector_dim=2)\n+    storage.save(\n+        [\n+            MR(\n+                content=\"private to worker-1\",\n+                scope=\"/notes\",\n+                embedding=[1.0, 0.0],\n+                private=True,\n+                source=\"worker-1\",\n+            )\n+        ]\n+    )\n+    mem = Memory(\n+        llm=MagicMock(),\n+        storage=storage,\n+        embedder=lambda texts: [[1.0, 0.0]] * len(texts),\n+    )\n+\n+    as_owner = mem.recall(\n+        \"private to worker\", scope=\"/notes\", depth=\"shallow\", source=\"worker-1\"\n+    )\n+    assert [m.record.content for m in as_owner] == [\"private to worker-1\"], (\n+        \"the owning source must still see its private record\"\n+    )\n+\n+    with_private = mem.recall(\n+        \"private to worker\", scope=\"/notes\", depth=\"shallow\", include_private=True\n+    )\n+    assert [m.record.content for m in with_private] == [\"private to worker-1\"], (\n+        \"include_private=True must still see everything\"\n+    )\n", "problem_statement": "Private memories saved without a source are visible to every recall\n## Description\n\n`Memory.remember(private=True)` without a `source` stores a private record whose `source` is `None`. The privacy filters in both recall paths test\n\n```python\nif not r.private or r.source == source\n```\n\n(`lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/unified_memory.py` in the shallow path, `lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/recall_flow.py` in the deep RecallFlow path). For such a record, `r.source == source` reduces to `None == None` \u2014 **True** \u2014 so the record is returned to every default caller (`source=None`, `include_private=False`). The privacy flag is effectively void for source-less records.\n\n## Reproduction (current main)\n\n```python\nstorage.save([MemoryRecord(content=\"secret api key sk-abc123\", scope=\"/notes\", embedding=[1.0, 0.0], private=True, source=None)])\nmem = Memory(llm=..., storage=storage, embedder=...)\nresults = mem.recall(\"secret api key\", scope=\"/notes\", depth=\"shallow\", include_private=False)\n# -> returns the private record to an unprivileged caller\n```\n\nSame leak through the default `depth=\"deep\"` path.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nA private record should only be visible when the caller supplies the matching non-None `source`, or passes `include_private=True`. Private records saved without a source should be invisible to unprivileged recalls (they opted into privacy; nothing can prove ownership).\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nTighten both filters to `not r.private or (source is not None and r.source == source)`. Legitimate access is unaffected: records with a real source stay visible to that source, and `include_private=True` still sees everything.\n\nA possible follow-up hardening: warn (or validate) on `remember(private=True, source=None)` at save time, since such records can then only be retrieved via `include_private=True`.\n\nHappy to submit a PR with regression tests for both paths.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-22T09:41:28Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8393, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8393", "issue_numbers": ["8392"], "base_commit": "5d58569ae2a24ada934d1e7743dcdd7d13fed45c", "patch": "diff --git a/docs/edge/ar/concepts/flows.mdx b/docs/edge/ar/concepts/flows.mdx\nindex 6c4f9f51a1..c96ddce8d6 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ar/concepts/flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ar/concepts/flows.mdx\n@@ -1039,13 +1039,13 @@ crewai flow plot\n \n \u0625\u0630\u0627 \u0643\u0646\u062a \u0645\u0647\u062a\u0645\u064b\u0627 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u0643\u0634\u0627\u0641 \u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629 \u0625\u0636\u0627\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642\u0627\u062a\u060c \u0644\u062f\u064a\u0646\u0627 \u0645\u062c\u0645\u0648\u0639\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0646\u0648\u0639\u0629 \u0645\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0648\u0635\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0641\u064a \u0645\u0633\u062a\u0648\u062f\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629. \u0625\u0644\u064a\u0643 \u0623\u0631\u0628\u0639\u0629 \u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629 \u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u062d\u062f\u062f\u0629\u060c \u0643\u0644 \u0645\u0646\u0647\u0627 \u064a\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u062d\u0627\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u062f\u0629 \u0644\u0645\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f\u062a\u0643 \u0641\u064a \u0645\u0637\u0627\u0628\u0642\u0629 \u0646\u0648\u0639 \u0645\u0634\u0643\u0644\u062a\u0643 \u0627\u0644\u062d\u0627\u0644\u064a\u0629 \u0645\u0639 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0645\u062d\u062f\u062f:\n \n-1. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0627\u0644\u0631\u062f \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a**: \u064a\u0648\u0636\u062d \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u062d\u0644\u0642\u0629 \u0644\u0627 \u0646\u0647\u0627\u0626\u064a\u0629 \u062d\u064a\u062b \u062a\u0639\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0647\u0645\u0629 \u062e\u0644\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u0645\u0631\u0627\u0631 \u0644\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0631\u062f\u0648\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a. \u0625\u0646\u0647\u0627 \u062d\u0627\u0644\u0629 \u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0631\u0627\u0626\u0639\u0629 \u0644\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u062a\u062d\u062a\u0627\u062c \u0625\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0646\u0641\u064a\u0630 \u0628\u0634\u0643\u0644 \u0645\u062a\u0643\u0631\u0631 \u062f\u0648\u0646 \u062a\u062f\u062e\u0644 \u064a\u062f\u0648\u064a. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/email_auto_responder_flow)\n+1. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0627\u0644\u0631\u062f \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a**: \u064a\u0648\u0636\u062d \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u062d\u0644\u0642\u0629 \u0644\u0627 \u0646\u0647\u0627\u0626\u064a\u0629 \u062d\u064a\u062b \u062a\u0639\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0647\u0645\u0629 \u062e\u0644\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u0645\u0631\u0627\u0631 \u0644\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0631\u062f\u0648\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a. \u0625\u0646\u0647\u0627 \u062d\u0627\u0644\u0629 \u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0631\u0627\u0626\u0639\u0629 \u0644\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u062a\u062d\u062a\u0627\u062c \u0625\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0646\u0641\u064a\u0630 \u0628\u0634\u0643\u0644 \u0645\u062a\u0643\u0631\u0631 \u062f\u0648\u0646 \u062a\u062f\u062e\u0644 \u064a\u062f\u0648\u064a. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow)\n \n-2. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u062a\u0642\u064a\u064a\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646**: \u064a\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0625\u0636\u0627\u0641\u0629 \u062a\u063a\u0630\u064a\u0629 \u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639\u0629 \u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0641\u0631\u0648\u0639 \u0634\u0631\u0637\u064a\u0629 \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641\u0629 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0648\u062c\u0651\u0647. \u0625\u0646\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0645\u0645\u062a\u0627\u0632 \u0644\u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u062f\u0645\u062c \u0627\u062a\u062e\u0627\u0630 \u0627\u0644\u0642\u0631\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062f\u064a\u0646\u0627\u0645\u064a\u0643\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0631\u0642\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629 \u0641\u064a \u0633\u064a\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644\u0643. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/lead-score-flow)\n+2. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u062a\u0642\u064a\u064a\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646**: \u064a\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0625\u0636\u0627\u0641\u0629 \u062a\u063a\u0630\u064a\u0629 \u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639\u0629 \u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0641\u0631\u0648\u0639 \u0634\u0631\u0637\u064a\u0629 \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641\u0629 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0648\u062c\u0651\u0647. \u0625\u0646\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0645\u0645\u062a\u0627\u0632 \u0644\u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u062f\u0645\u062c \u0627\u062a\u062e\u0627\u0630 \u0627\u0644\u0642\u0631\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062f\u064a\u0646\u0627\u0645\u064a\u0643\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0631\u0642\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629 \u0641\u064a \u0633\u064a\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644\u0643. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow)\n \n-3. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628**: \u064a\u062a\u0641\u0648\u0642 \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0641\u064a \u0631\u0628\u0637 \u0641\u0631\u0642 Crew \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0639\u064b\u0627\u060c \u062d\u064a\u062b \u062a\u064f\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645 \u0645\u062e\u0631\u062c\u0627\u062a \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0628\u0648\u0627\u0633\u0637\u0629 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0622\u062e\u0631. \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0648\u062c\u0647 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062f\u060c \u064a\u0642\u0648\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0628\u0648\u0636\u0639 \u0645\u062e\u0637\u0637 \u0644\u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628 \u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644\u060c \u0648\u064a\u0642\u0648\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0622\u062e\u0631 \u0628\u0625\u0646\u0634\u0627\u0621 \u0641\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0628\u0646\u0627\u0621\u064b \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062e\u0637\u0637. \u0641\u064a \u0627\u0644\u0646\u0647\u0627\u064a\u0629\u060c \u064a\u062a\u0645 \u0631\u0628\u0637 \u0643\u0644 \u0634\u064a\u0621 \u0644\u0625\u0646\u062a\u0627\u062c \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628 \u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644. \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062e\u0637\u0648\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u062a\u062a\u0637\u0644\u0628 \u062a\u0646\u0633\u064a\u0642\u064b\u0627 \u0628\u064a\u0646 \u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641\u0629. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/write_a_book_with_flows)\n+3. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628**: \u064a\u062a\u0641\u0648\u0642 \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0641\u064a \u0631\u0628\u0637 \u0641\u0631\u0642 Crew \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0639\u064b\u0627\u060c \u062d\u064a\u062b \u062a\u064f\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645 \u0645\u062e\u0631\u062c\u0627\u062a \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0628\u0648\u0627\u0633\u0637\u0629 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0622\u062e\u0631. \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0648\u062c\u0647 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062f\u060c \u064a\u0642\u0648\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0628\u0648\u0636\u0639 \u0645\u062e\u0637\u0637 \u0644\u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628 \u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644\u060c \u0648\u064a\u0642\u0648\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0622\u062e\u0631 \u0628\u0625\u0646\u0634\u0627\u0621 \u0641\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0628\u0646\u0627\u0621\u064b \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062e\u0637\u0637. \u0641\u064a \u0627\u0644\u0646\u0647\u0627\u064a\u0629\u060c \u064a\u062a\u0645 \u0631\u0628\u0637 \u0643\u0644 \u0634\u064a\u0621 \u0644\u0625\u0646\u062a\u0627\u062c \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628 \u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644. \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062e\u0637\u0648\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u062a\u062a\u0637\u0644\u0628 \u062a\u0646\u0633\u064a\u0642\u064b\u0627 \u0628\u064a\u0646 \u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641\u0629. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/write_a_book_with_flows)\n \n-4. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u0627\u062a**: \u064a\u0648\u0636\u062d \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u062b \u062d\u062f\u062b \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0644\u062a\u0634\u063a\u064a\u0644 \u0625\u062c\u0631\u0627\u0621\u0627\u062a \u0645\u062a\u0627\u0628\u0639\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629. \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0633\u0628\u064a\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u060c \u0628\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0643\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0644 \u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u060c \u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062b \u0644\u0648\u062d\u0629 Trello \u0648\u0625\u0631\u0633\u0627\u0644 \u0631\u0633\u0627\u0644\u0629 Slack \u0648\u062d\u0641\u0638 \u0627\u0644\u0646\u062a\u0627\u0626\u062c. \u0625\u0646\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0631\u0627\u0626\u0639 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0646\u062a\u0627\u0626\u062c \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0646 \u062d\u062f\u062b \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f\u060c \u0645\u0645\u0627 \u064a\u062c\u0639\u0644\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u064a\u064b\u0627 \u0644\u0625\u062f\u0627\u0631\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0634\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0629 \u0648\u0623\u0646\u0638\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0634\u0639\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/meeting_assistant_flow)\n+4. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u0627\u062a**: \u064a\u0648\u0636\u062d \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u062b \u062d\u062f\u062b \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0644\u062a\u0634\u063a\u064a\u0644 \u0625\u062c\u0631\u0627\u0621\u0627\u062a \u0645\u062a\u0627\u0628\u0639\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629. \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0633\u0628\u064a\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u060c \u0628\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0643\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0644 \u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u060c \u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062b \u0644\u0648\u062d\u0629 Trello \u0648\u0625\u0631\u0633\u0627\u0644 \u0631\u0633\u0627\u0644\u0629 Slack \u0648\u062d\u0641\u0638 \u0627\u0644\u0646\u062a\u0627\u0626\u062c. \u0625\u0646\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0631\u0627\u0626\u0639 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0646\u062a\u0627\u0626\u062c \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0646 \u062d\u062f\u062b \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f\u060c \u0645\u0645\u0627 \u064a\u062c\u0639\u0644\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u064a\u064b\u0627 \u0644\u0625\u062f\u0627\u0631\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0634\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0629 \u0648\u0623\u0646\u0638\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0634\u0639\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow)\n \n \u0645\u0646 \u062e\u0644\u0627\u0644 \u0627\u0633\u062a\u0643\u0634\u0627\u0641 \u0647\u0630\u0647 \u0627\u0644\u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629\u060c \u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646\u0643 \u0627\u0644\u062d\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0631\u0624\u0649 \u062d\u0648\u0644 \u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u0641\u0627\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0646 \u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642\u0627\u062a CrewAI \u0644\u062d\u0627\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u062a\u0646\u0648\u0639\u0629\u060c \u0645\u0646 \u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0643\u0631\u0631\u0629 \u0625\u0644\u0649 \u0625\u062f\u0627\u0631\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062e\u0637\u0648\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u062a\u062e\u0627\u0630 \u0627\u0644\u0642\u0631\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062f\u064a\u0646\u0627\u0645\u064a\u0643\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062a\u063a\u0630\u064a\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ar/examples/example.mdx b/docs/edge/ar/examples/example.mdx\nindex 0987e8dff5..6a5df55044 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ar/examples/example.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ar/examples/example.mdx\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"\u0627\u0644\u0631\u062f \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a\" icon=\"envelope\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow\">\n     \u0645\u0631\u0627\u0642\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0631\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0622\u0644\u064a.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Flow \u062a\u0642\u064a\u064a\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead_score_flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Flow \u062a\u0642\u064a\u064a\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow\">\n     \u062a\u0623\u0647\u064a\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646 \u0645\u0639 \u062a\u062f\u062e\u0644 \u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Flow \u0645\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u0627\u062a\" icon=\"calendar\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow\">\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062a\n \n <CardGroup cols={3}>\n-  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/crewai-langgraph\">\n+  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/CrewAI-LangGraph\">\n     \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0625\u0637\u0627\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644 LangGraph.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Azure OpenAI\" icon=\"cloud\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/azure_model\">\n@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## \u062f\u0641\u0627\u062a\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062d\u0638\u0627\u062a\n \n <CardGroup cols={2}>\n-  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n     Simple QA Crew + Flow.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"\u062c\u0645\u064a\u0639 \u062f\u0641\u0627\u062a\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062d\u0638\u0627\u062a\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"\u062c\u0645\u064a\u0639 \u062f\u0641\u0627\u062a\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062d\u0638\u0627\u062a\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     \u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629 \u062a\u0641\u0627\u0639\u0644\u064a\u0629 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0644\u0645 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062a\u062c\u0631\u064a\u0628.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/en/concepts/flows.mdx b/docs/edge/en/concepts/flows.mdx\nindex 8ba6aab52b..ec373889d8 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/concepts/flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/concepts/flows.mdx\n@@ -1041,13 +1041,13 @@ Plotting your flows is a powerful feature of CrewAI that enhances your ability t\n \n If you're interested in exploring additional examples of flows, we have a variety of recommendations in our examples repository. Here are four specific flow examples, each showcasing unique use cases to help you match your current problem type to a specific example:\n \n-1. **Email Auto Responder Flow**: This example demonstrates an infinite loop where a background job continually runs to automate email responses. It's a great use case for tasks that need to be performed repeatedly without manual intervention. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/email_auto_responder_flow)\n+1. **Email Auto Responder Flow**: This example demonstrates an infinite loop where a background job continually runs to automate email responses. It's a great use case for tasks that need to be performed repeatedly without manual intervention. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow)\n \n-2. **Lead Score Flow**: This flow showcases adding human-in-the-loop feedback and handling different conditional branches using the router. It's an excellent example of how to incorporate dynamic decision-making and human oversight into your workflows. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/lead-score-flow)\n+2. **Lead Score Flow**: This flow showcases adding human-in-the-loop feedback and handling different conditional branches using the router. It's an excellent example of how to incorporate dynamic decision-making and human oversight into your workflows. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow)\n \n-3. **Write a Book Flow**: This example excels at chaining multiple crews together, where the output of one crew is used by another. Specifically, one crew outlines an entire book, and another crew generates chapters based on the outline. Eventually, everything is connected to produce a complete book. This flow is perfect for complex, multi-step processes that require coordination between different tasks. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/write_a_book_with_flows)\n+3. **Write a Book Flow**: This example excels at chaining multiple crews together, where the output of one crew is used by another. Specifically, one crew outlines an entire book, and another crew generates chapters based on the outline. Eventually, everything is connected to produce a complete book. This flow is perfect for complex, multi-step processes that require coordination between different tasks. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/write_a_book_with_flows)\n \n-4. **Meeting Assistant Flow**: This flow demonstrates how to broadcast one event to trigger multiple follow-up actions. For instance, after a meeting is completed, the flow can update a Trello board, send a Slack message, and save the results. It's a great example of handling multiple outcomes from a single event, making it ideal for comprehensive task management and notification systems. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/meeting_assistant_flow)\n+4. **Meeting Assistant Flow**: This flow demonstrates how to broadcast one event to trigger multiple follow-up actions. For instance, after a meeting is completed, the flow can update a Trello board, send a Slack message, and save the results. It's a great example of handling multiple outcomes from a single event, making it ideal for comprehensive task management and notification systems. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow)\n \n By exploring these examples, you can gain insights into how to leverage CrewAI Flows for various use cases, from automating repetitive tasks to managing complex, multi-step processes with dynamic decision-making and human feedback.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/en/examples/example.mdx b/docs/edge/en/examples/example.mdx\nindex 37672cbfa3..b1b5f72c46 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/examples/example.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/examples/example.mdx\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"Email Auto Responder\" icon=\"envelope\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow\">\n     Automated email monitoring and replies.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Lead Score Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead_score_flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Lead Score Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow\">\n     Lead qualification with human\u2011in\u2011the\u2011loop.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Meeting Assistant Flow\" icon=\"calendar\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow\">\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## Integrations\n \n <CardGroup cols={3}>\n-  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/crewai-langgraph\">\n+  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/CrewAI-LangGraph\">\n     Integration with LangGraph framework.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Azure OpenAI\" icon=\"cloud\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/azure_model\">\n@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## Notebooks\n \n <CardGroup cols={2}>\n-  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n     Simple QA Crew + Flow.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"All Notebooks\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"All Notebooks\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     Interactive examples for learning and experimentation.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/concepts/flows.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/concepts/flows.mdx\nindex 3819b4ed74..e8c20f2f00 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/concepts/flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/concepts/flows.mdx\n@@ -1031,13 +1031,13 @@ flow\ub97c \uc2dc\uac01\ud654\ud558\uba74 \uc6cc\ud06c\ud50c\ub85c\uc758 \uad6c\uc870\ub97c \ub354\uc6b1 \uba85\ud655\ud558\uac8c \uc774\ud574\ud560\n \n \ucd94\uac00\uc801\uc778 flow \uc608\uc81c\ub97c \uc0b4\ud3b4\ubcf4\uace0 \uc2f6\uc73c\uc2dc\ub2e4\uba74, \uc800\ud76c examples \ub808\ud3ec\uc9c0\ud1a0\ub9ac\uc5d0\uc11c \ub2e4\uc591\ud55c \ucd94\ucc9c \uc608\uc81c\ub97c \ud655\uc778\ud558\uc2e4 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc544\ub798\ub294 \uac01\uac01 \uace0\uc720\ud55c \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uc0ac\ub840\ub97c \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc8fc\ub294 \ub124 \uac00\uc9c0 \uad6c\uccb4\uc801\uc778 flow \uc608\uc81c\ub85c, \ud604\uc7ac \ubb38\uc81c \uc720\ud615\uc5d0 \ub9de\ub294 \uc608\uc2dc\ub97c \ucc3e\ub294 \ub370 \ub3c4\uc6c0\uc774 \ub420 \uac83\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4:\n \n-1. **\uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc790\ub3d9 \uc751\ub2f5\uc790 Flow**: \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub294 \ubc31\uadf8\ub77c\uc6b4\ub4dc \uc791\uc5c5\uc774 \uacc4\uc18d \uc2e4\ud589\ub418\uba74\uc11c \uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc751\ub2f5\uc744 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ud558\ub294 \ubb34\ud55c \ub8e8\ud504\ub97c \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc218\ub3d9 \uac1c\uc785 \uc5c6\uc774 \ubc18\ubcf5\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \uc218\ud589\ud574\uc57c \ud558\ub294 \uc791\uc5c5\uc5d0 \uc801\ud569\ud55c \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uc0ac\ub840\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/email_auto_responder_flow)\n+1. **\uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc790\ub3d9 \uc751\ub2f5\uc790 Flow**: \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub294 \ubc31\uadf8\ub77c\uc6b4\ub4dc \uc791\uc5c5\uc774 \uacc4\uc18d \uc2e4\ud589\ub418\uba74\uc11c \uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc751\ub2f5\uc744 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ud558\ub294 \ubb34\ud55c \ub8e8\ud504\ub97c \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc218\ub3d9 \uac1c\uc785 \uc5c6\uc774 \ubc18\ubcf5\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \uc218\ud589\ud574\uc57c \ud558\ub294 \uc791\uc5c5\uc5d0 \uc801\ud569\ud55c \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uc0ac\ub840\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow)\n \n-2. **\ub9ac\ub4dc \uc810\uc218 Flow**: \uc774 flow \uc608\uc81c\ub294 human-in-the-loop \ud53c\ub4dc\ubc31\uc744 \ucd94\uac00\ud558\uace0 router\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud558\uc5ec \ub2e4\uc591\ud55c \uc870\uac74 \ubd84\uae30\ub97c \ucc98\ub9ac\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\ubc95\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc6cc\ud06c\ud50c\ub85c\uc6b0\uc5d0 \ub3d9\uc801 \uc758\uc0ac\uacb0\uc815\uacfc \uc778\uac04\uc758 \uad00\ub9ac\u00b7\uac10\ub3c5\uc744 \ud1b5\ud569\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\uc2dd\uc744 \ud655\uc778\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \ud6cc\ub96d\ud55c \uc608\uc2dc\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/lead-score-flow)\n+2. **\ub9ac\ub4dc \uc810\uc218 Flow**: \uc774 flow \uc608\uc81c\ub294 human-in-the-loop \ud53c\ub4dc\ubc31\uc744 \ucd94\uac00\ud558\uace0 router\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud558\uc5ec \ub2e4\uc591\ud55c \uc870\uac74 \ubd84\uae30\ub97c \ucc98\ub9ac\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\ubc95\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc6cc\ud06c\ud50c\ub85c\uc6b0\uc5d0 \ub3d9\uc801 \uc758\uc0ac\uacb0\uc815\uacfc \uc778\uac04\uc758 \uad00\ub9ac\u00b7\uac10\ub3c5\uc744 \ud1b5\ud569\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\uc2dd\uc744 \ud655\uc778\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \ud6cc\ub96d\ud55c \uc608\uc2dc\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow)\n \n-3. **\ucc45 \uc9d1\ud544 Flow**: \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub294 \uc5ec\ub7ec crew\ub97c \uc5f0\uc18d\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \uc5f0\uacb0\ud558\ub294 \ub370 \ud0c1\uc6d4\ud558\uba70, \ud55c crew\uc758 \ucd9c\ub825 \uacb0\uacfc\uac00 \ub2e4\ub978 crew\uc5d0 \uc758\ud574 \uc0ac\uc6a9\ub429\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uad6c\uccb4\uc801\uc73c\ub85c, \ud55c crew\uac00 \uc804\uccb4 \ucc45\uc758 \uac1c\uc694\ub97c \uc791\uc131\ud558\uace0, \ub2e4\ub978 crew\uac00 \uadf8 \uac1c\uc694\ub97c \ubc14\ud0d5\uc73c\ub85c \ucc55\ud130\ub97c \uc0dd\uc131\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uacb0\uad6d \ubaa8\ub4e0 \uac83\uc774 \uc5f0\uacb0\ub418\uc5b4 \uc644\uc131\ub41c \ucc45\uc774 \ub9cc\ub4e4\uc5b4\uc9d1\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc5ec\ub7ec \uc791\uc5c5 \uac04 \uc870\uc728\uc774 \ud544\uc694\ud55c \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c \ub2e4\ub2e8\uacc4 \ud504\ub85c\uc138\uc2a4\uc5d0 \uc801\ud569\ud55c flow\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/write_a_book_with_flows)\n+3. **\ucc45 \uc9d1\ud544 Flow**: \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub294 \uc5ec\ub7ec crew\ub97c \uc5f0\uc18d\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \uc5f0\uacb0\ud558\ub294 \ub370 \ud0c1\uc6d4\ud558\uba70, \ud55c crew\uc758 \ucd9c\ub825 \uacb0\uacfc\uac00 \ub2e4\ub978 crew\uc5d0 \uc758\ud574 \uc0ac\uc6a9\ub429\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uad6c\uccb4\uc801\uc73c\ub85c, \ud55c crew\uac00 \uc804\uccb4 \ucc45\uc758 \uac1c\uc694\ub97c \uc791\uc131\ud558\uace0, \ub2e4\ub978 crew\uac00 \uadf8 \uac1c\uc694\ub97c \ubc14\ud0d5\uc73c\ub85c \ucc55\ud130\ub97c \uc0dd\uc131\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uacb0\uad6d \ubaa8\ub4e0 \uac83\uc774 \uc5f0\uacb0\ub418\uc5b4 \uc644\uc131\ub41c \ucc45\uc774 \ub9cc\ub4e4\uc5b4\uc9d1\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc5ec\ub7ec \uc791\uc5c5 \uac04 \uc870\uc728\uc774 \ud544\uc694\ud55c \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c \ub2e4\ub2e8\uacc4 \ud504\ub85c\uc138\uc2a4\uc5d0 \uc801\ud569\ud55c flow\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/write_a_book_with_flows)\n \n-4. **\ubbf8\ud305 \uc5b4\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud134\ud2b8 Flow**: \uc774 flow\ub294 \ud558\ub098\uc758 \uc774\ubca4\ud2b8\uac00 \uc5ec\ub7ec \ud6c4\uc18d \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \ud2b8\ub9ac\uac70\ud558\ub3c4\ub85d \ube0c\ub85c\ub4dc\uce90\uc2a4\ud2b8\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\ubc95\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc608\ub97c \ub4e4\uc5b4, \ubbf8\ud305\uc774 \ub05d\ub09c \ud6c4 Trello \ubcf4\ub4dc\ub97c \uc5c5\ub370\uc774\ud2b8\ud558\uace0 Slack \uba54\uc2dc\uc9c0\ub97c \uc804\uc1a1\ud558\uba70 \uacb0\uacfc\ub97c \uc800\uc7a5\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4. \ud558\ub098\uc758 \uc774\ubca4\ud2b8\ub85c\ubd80\ud130 \uc5ec\ub7ec \uacb0\uacfc\ub97c \ucc98\ub9ac\ud558\ub294 \uc88b\uc740 \uc608\uc2dc\ub85c, \ud3ec\uad04\uc801\uc778 \uc791\uc5c5 \uad00\ub9ac \ubc0f \uc54c\ub9bc \uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c\uc5d0 \uc774\uc0c1\uc801\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/meeting_assistant_flow)\n+4. **\ubbf8\ud305 \uc5b4\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud134\ud2b8 Flow**: \uc774 flow\ub294 \ud558\ub098\uc758 \uc774\ubca4\ud2b8\uac00 \uc5ec\ub7ec \ud6c4\uc18d \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \ud2b8\ub9ac\uac70\ud558\ub3c4\ub85d \ube0c\ub85c\ub4dc\uce90\uc2a4\ud2b8\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\ubc95\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc608\ub97c \ub4e4\uc5b4, \ubbf8\ud305\uc774 \ub05d\ub09c \ud6c4 Trello \ubcf4\ub4dc\ub97c \uc5c5\ub370\uc774\ud2b8\ud558\uace0 Slack \uba54\uc2dc\uc9c0\ub97c \uc804\uc1a1\ud558\uba70 \uacb0\uacfc\ub97c \uc800\uc7a5\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4. \ud558\ub098\uc758 \uc774\ubca4\ud2b8\ub85c\ubd80\ud130 \uc5ec\ub7ec \uacb0\uacfc\ub97c \ucc98\ub9ac\ud558\ub294 \uc88b\uc740 \uc608\uc2dc\ub85c, \ud3ec\uad04\uc801\uc778 \uc791\uc5c5 \uad00\ub9ac \ubc0f \uc54c\ub9bc \uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c\uc5d0 \uc774\uc0c1\uc801\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow)\n \n \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub4e4\uc744 \ud1b5\ud574 \ubc18\ubcf5\ub418\ub294 \uc791\uc5c5 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ubd80\ud130 \ub3d9\uc801 \uc758\uc0ac\uacb0\uc815\uacfc \uc778\uac04 \ud53c\ub4dc\ubc31\uc774 \ud3ec\ud568\ub41c \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c \ub2e4\ub2e8\uacc4 \ud504\ub85c\uc138\uc2a4 \uad00\ub9ac\uc5d0 \uc774\ub974\uae30\uae4c\uc9c0 \ub2e4\uc591\ud55c \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uc0ac\ub840\uc5d0\uc11c CrewAI Flows\ub97c \uc5b4\ub5bb\uac8c \ud65c\uc6a9\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294\uc9c0\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \ud1b5\ucc30\ub825\uc744 \uc5bb\uc744 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/examples/cookbooks.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/examples/cookbooks.mdx\nindex 9b835cd1b1..af2c641c2a 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/examples/cookbooks.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/examples/cookbooks.mdx\n@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"Quickstarts \uc800\uc7a5\uc18c\" icon=\"bolt\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-quickstarts\">\n     \ud2b9\uc815 CrewAI \uae30\ub2a5\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc8fc\ub294 \ub370\ubaa8\uc640 \uc18c\uaddc\ubaa8 \ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"\uc608\uc2dc\uc758 \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81\" icon=\"book-open\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"\uc608\uc2dc\uc758 \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81\" icon=\"book-open\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     \uc2e4\uc2b5\uc744 \uc704\ud55c \uc778\ud130\ub799\ud2f0\ube0c \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/examples/example.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/examples/example.mdx\nindex 68dcccc5d5..f96eba936f 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/examples/example.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/examples/example.mdx\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"\uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc790\ub3d9 \uc751\ub2f5\" icon=\"envelope\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow\">\n     \uc774\uba54\uc77c \ubaa8\ub2c8\ud130\ub9c1\uacfc \uc790\ub3d9 \uc751\ub2f5.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"\ub9ac\ub4dc \uc810\uc218 Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead_score_flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"\ub9ac\ub4dc \uc810\uc218 Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow\">\n     \ud734\uba3c\u2011\uc778\u2011\ub354\u2011\ub8e8\ud504 \ub9ac\ub4dc \ud3c9\uac00.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"\ubbf8\ud305 \uc5b4\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud134\ud2b8 Flow\" icon=\"calendar\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow\">\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## \ud1b5\ud569 (Integrations)\n \n <CardGroup cols={3}>\n-  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/crewai-langgraph\">\n+  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/CrewAI-LangGraph\">\n     LangGraph \ud504\ub808\uc784\uc6cc\ud06c \uc5f0\ub3d9.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Azure OpenAI\" icon=\"cloud\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/azure_model\">\n@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81 (Notebooks)\n \n <CardGroup cols={2}>\n-  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n     Simple QA Crew + Flow.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"\ubaa8\ub4e0 \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"\ubaa8\ub4e0 \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     \ud559\uc2b5\uacfc \uc2e4\ud5d8\uc744 \uc704\ud55c \uc778\ud130\ub799\ud2f0\ube0c \uc608\uc2dc \ubaa8\uc74c.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/flows.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/flows.mdx\nindex aa4e3154fe..eb992d7746 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/concepts/flows.mdx\n@@ -1028,13 +1028,13 @@ A plotagem dos flows \u00e9 um recurso poderoso do CrewAI para aprimorar o design e\n \n Se voc\u00ea deseja explorar exemplos adicionais de flows, acompanhe alguns exemplos em nosso reposit\u00f3rio de exemplos. Aqui est\u00e3o quatro sugest\u00f5es espec\u00edficas de flows, cada uma demonstrando casos de uso distintos para voc\u00ea escolher conforme seu problema:\n \n-1. **Email Auto Responder Flow**: Este exemplo demonstra um loop infinito, onde um job de background roda continuamente automatizando respostas de email. \u00c9 ideal para tarefas rotineiras sem interven\u00e7\u00e3o manual. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/email_auto_responder_flow)\n+1. **Email Auto Responder Flow**: Este exemplo demonstra um loop infinito, onde um job de background roda continuamente automatizando respostas de email. \u00c9 ideal para tarefas rotineiras sem interven\u00e7\u00e3o manual. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow)\n \n-2. **Lead Score Flow**: Destaca como adicionar feedback humano e manipular diferentes ramos condicionais usando router. Um \u00f3timo aprendizado para workflows com decis\u00e3o din\u00e2mica e supervis\u00e3o humana. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/lead-score-flow)\n+2. **Lead Score Flow**: Destaca como adicionar feedback humano e manipular diferentes ramos condicionais usando router. Um \u00f3timo aprendizado para workflows com decis\u00e3o din\u00e2mica e supervis\u00e3o humana. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow)\n \n-3. **Write a Book Flow**: Exemplo ideal para encadear m\u00faltiplas crews, onde a sa\u00edda de uma \u00e9 usada por outra. Uma crew faz um sum\u00e1rio do livro inteiro, outra gera cap\u00edtulos... Tudo conectado para entregar um livro completo. Perfeito para processos longos e coordenados. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/write_a_book_with_flows)\n+3. **Write a Book Flow**: Exemplo ideal para encadear m\u00faltiplas crews, onde a sa\u00edda de uma \u00e9 usada por outra. Uma crew faz um sum\u00e1rio do livro inteiro, outra gera cap\u00edtulos... Tudo conectado para entregar um livro completo. Perfeito para processos longos e coordenados. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/write_a_book_with_flows)\n \n-4. **Meeting Assistant Flow**: Demonstra como transmitir um evento para desencadear m\u00faltiplas a\u00e7\u00f5es posteriores. Exemplo: ao finalizar uma reuni\u00e3o, atualizar um Trello, enviar mensagem no Slack e salvar resultados ao mesmo tempo. Indicado para gerenciamento completo de tarefas e notifica\u00e7\u00f5es. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/meeting_assistant_flow)\n+4. **Meeting Assistant Flow**: Demonstra como transmitir um evento para desencadear m\u00faltiplas a\u00e7\u00f5es posteriores. Exemplo: ao finalizar uma reuni\u00e3o, atualizar um Trello, enviar mensagem no Slack e salvar resultados ao mesmo tempo. Indicado para gerenciamento completo de tarefas e notifica\u00e7\u00f5es. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow)\n \n Explore esses exemplos para descobrir como aproveitar CrewAI Flows em diferentes contextos \u2013 desde automa\u00e7\u00e3o de tarefas repetitivas at\u00e9 o gerenciamento de processos din\u00e2micos com decis\u00f5es e feedback humano.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/examples/cookbooks.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/examples/cookbooks.mdx\nindex 7057621a19..b72f36d112 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/examples/cookbooks.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/examples/cookbooks.mdx\n@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"Reposit\u00f3rio de Quickstarts\" icon=\"bolt\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-quickstarts\">\n     Demos e projetos pequenos que mostram capacidades espec\u00edficas do CrewAI.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Notebooks nos Exemplos\" icon=\"book-open\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"Notebooks nos Exemplos\" icon=\"book-open\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     Notebooks interativos para aprendizado pr\u00e1tico.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/examples/example.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/examples/example.mdx\nindex 9e30069b31..bde6762da4 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/examples/example.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/examples/example.mdx\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"Email Auto Responder\" icon=\"envelope\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow\">\n     Monitoramento e respostas de e\u2011mail.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Lead Score Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead_score_flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Lead Score Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow\">\n     Qualifica\u00e7\u00e3o de leads com revis\u00e3o humana.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Meeting Assistant Flow\" icon=\"calendar\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow\">\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## Integra\u00e7\u00f5es\n \n <CardGroup cols={3}>\n-  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/crewai-langgraph\">\n+  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/CrewAI-LangGraph\">\n     Integra\u00e7\u00e3o com o framework LangGraph.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Azure OpenAI\" icon=\"cloud\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/azure_model\">\n@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## Notebooks\n \n <CardGroup cols={2}>\n-  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n     Simple QA Crew + Flow.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Todos os Notebooks\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"Todos os Notebooks\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     Exemplos interativos para aprendizado e experimenta\u00e7\u00e3o.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/concepts/flows.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/concepts/flows.mdx\nindex 6c4f9f51a1..c96ddce8d6 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/concepts/flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/concepts/flows.mdx\n@@ -1039,13 +1039,13 @@ crewai flow plot\n \n \u0625\u0630\u0627 \u0643\u0646\u062a \u0645\u0647\u062a\u0645\u064b\u0627 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u0643\u0634\u0627\u0641 \u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629 \u0625\u0636\u0627\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642\u0627\u062a\u060c \u0644\u062f\u064a\u0646\u0627 \u0645\u062c\u0645\u0648\u0639\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0646\u0648\u0639\u0629 \u0645\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0648\u0635\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0641\u064a \u0645\u0633\u062a\u0648\u062f\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629. \u0625\u0644\u064a\u0643 \u0623\u0631\u0628\u0639\u0629 \u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629 \u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u062d\u062f\u062f\u0629\u060c \u0643\u0644 \u0645\u0646\u0647\u0627 \u064a\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u062d\u0627\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u062f\u0629 \u0644\u0645\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f\u062a\u0643 \u0641\u064a \u0645\u0637\u0627\u0628\u0642\u0629 \u0646\u0648\u0639 \u0645\u0634\u0643\u0644\u062a\u0643 \u0627\u0644\u062d\u0627\u0644\u064a\u0629 \u0645\u0639 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0645\u062d\u062f\u062f:\n \n-1. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0627\u0644\u0631\u062f \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a**: \u064a\u0648\u0636\u062d \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u062d\u0644\u0642\u0629 \u0644\u0627 \u0646\u0647\u0627\u0626\u064a\u0629 \u062d\u064a\u062b \u062a\u0639\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0647\u0645\u0629 \u062e\u0644\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u0645\u0631\u0627\u0631 \u0644\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0631\u062f\u0648\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a. \u0625\u0646\u0647\u0627 \u062d\u0627\u0644\u0629 \u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0631\u0627\u0626\u0639\u0629 \u0644\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u062a\u062d\u062a\u0627\u062c \u0625\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0646\u0641\u064a\u0630 \u0628\u0634\u0643\u0644 \u0645\u062a\u0643\u0631\u0631 \u062f\u0648\u0646 \u062a\u062f\u062e\u0644 \u064a\u062f\u0648\u064a. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/email_auto_responder_flow)\n+1. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0627\u0644\u0631\u062f \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a**: \u064a\u0648\u0636\u062d \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u062d\u0644\u0642\u0629 \u0644\u0627 \u0646\u0647\u0627\u0626\u064a\u0629 \u062d\u064a\u062b \u062a\u0639\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0647\u0645\u0629 \u062e\u0644\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u0645\u0631\u0627\u0631 \u0644\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0631\u062f\u0648\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a. \u0625\u0646\u0647\u0627 \u062d\u0627\u0644\u0629 \u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0631\u0627\u0626\u0639\u0629 \u0644\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u062a\u062d\u062a\u0627\u062c \u0625\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0646\u0641\u064a\u0630 \u0628\u0634\u0643\u0644 \u0645\u062a\u0643\u0631\u0631 \u062f\u0648\u0646 \u062a\u062f\u062e\u0644 \u064a\u062f\u0648\u064a. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow)\n \n-2. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u062a\u0642\u064a\u064a\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646**: \u064a\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0625\u0636\u0627\u0641\u0629 \u062a\u063a\u0630\u064a\u0629 \u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639\u0629 \u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0641\u0631\u0648\u0639 \u0634\u0631\u0637\u064a\u0629 \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641\u0629 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0648\u062c\u0651\u0647. \u0625\u0646\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0645\u0645\u062a\u0627\u0632 \u0644\u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u062f\u0645\u062c \u0627\u062a\u062e\u0627\u0630 \u0627\u0644\u0642\u0631\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062f\u064a\u0646\u0627\u0645\u064a\u0643\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0631\u0642\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629 \u0641\u064a \u0633\u064a\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644\u0643. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/lead-score-flow)\n+2. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u062a\u0642\u064a\u064a\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646**: \u064a\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0625\u0636\u0627\u0641\u0629 \u062a\u063a\u0630\u064a\u0629 \u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639\u0629 \u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0641\u0631\u0648\u0639 \u0634\u0631\u0637\u064a\u0629 \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641\u0629 \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0648\u062c\u0651\u0647. \u0625\u0646\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0645\u0645\u062a\u0627\u0632 \u0644\u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u062f\u0645\u062c \u0627\u062a\u062e\u0627\u0630 \u0627\u0644\u0642\u0631\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062f\u064a\u0646\u0627\u0645\u064a\u0643\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0631\u0642\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629 \u0641\u064a \u0633\u064a\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644\u0643. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow)\n \n-3. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628**: \u064a\u062a\u0641\u0648\u0642 \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0641\u064a \u0631\u0628\u0637 \u0641\u0631\u0642 Crew \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0639\u064b\u0627\u060c \u062d\u064a\u062b \u062a\u064f\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645 \u0645\u062e\u0631\u062c\u0627\u062a \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0628\u0648\u0627\u0633\u0637\u0629 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0622\u062e\u0631. \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0648\u062c\u0647 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062f\u060c \u064a\u0642\u0648\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0628\u0648\u0636\u0639 \u0645\u062e\u0637\u0637 \u0644\u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628 \u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644\u060c \u0648\u064a\u0642\u0648\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0622\u062e\u0631 \u0628\u0625\u0646\u0634\u0627\u0621 \u0641\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0628\u0646\u0627\u0621\u064b \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062e\u0637\u0637. \u0641\u064a \u0627\u0644\u0646\u0647\u0627\u064a\u0629\u060c \u064a\u062a\u0645 \u0631\u0628\u0637 \u0643\u0644 \u0634\u064a\u0621 \u0644\u0625\u0646\u062a\u0627\u062c \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628 \u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644. \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062e\u0637\u0648\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u062a\u062a\u0637\u0644\u0628 \u062a\u0646\u0633\u064a\u0642\u064b\u0627 \u0628\u064a\u0646 \u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641\u0629. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/write_a_book_with_flows)\n+3. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628**: \u064a\u062a\u0641\u0648\u0642 \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0641\u064a \u0631\u0628\u0637 \u0641\u0631\u0642 Crew \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0639\u064b\u0627\u060c \u062d\u064a\u062b \u062a\u064f\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645 \u0645\u062e\u0631\u062c\u0627\u062a \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0628\u0648\u0627\u0633\u0637\u0629 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0622\u062e\u0631. \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0648\u062c\u0647 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062f\u060c \u064a\u0642\u0648\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0628\u0648\u0636\u0639 \u0645\u062e\u0637\u0637 \u0644\u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628 \u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644\u060c \u0648\u064a\u0642\u0648\u0645 \u0641\u0631\u064a\u0642 \u0622\u062e\u0631 \u0628\u0625\u0646\u0634\u0627\u0621 \u0641\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0628\u0646\u0627\u0621\u064b \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062e\u0637\u0637. \u0641\u064a \u0627\u0644\u0646\u0647\u0627\u064a\u0629\u060c \u064a\u062a\u0645 \u0631\u0628\u0637 \u0643\u0644 \u0634\u064a\u0621 \u0644\u0625\u0646\u062a\u0627\u062c \u0643\u062a\u0627\u0628 \u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644. \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062e\u0637\u0648\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u062a\u062a\u0637\u0644\u0628 \u062a\u0646\u0633\u064a\u0642\u064b\u0627 \u0628\u064a\u0646 \u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0644\u0641\u0629. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/write_a_book_with_flows)\n \n-4. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u0627\u062a**: \u064a\u0648\u0636\u062d \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u062b \u062d\u062f\u062b \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0644\u062a\u0634\u063a\u064a\u0644 \u0625\u062c\u0631\u0627\u0621\u0627\u062a \u0645\u062a\u0627\u0628\u0639\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629. \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0633\u0628\u064a\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u060c \u0628\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0643\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0644 \u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u060c \u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062b \u0644\u0648\u062d\u0629 Trello \u0648\u0625\u0631\u0633\u0627\u0644 \u0631\u0633\u0627\u0644\u0629 Slack \u0648\u062d\u0641\u0638 \u0627\u0644\u0646\u062a\u0627\u0626\u062c. \u0625\u0646\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0631\u0627\u0626\u0639 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0646\u062a\u0627\u0626\u062c \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0646 \u062d\u062f\u062b \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f\u060c \u0645\u0645\u0627 \u064a\u062c\u0639\u0644\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u064a\u064b\u0627 \u0644\u0625\u062f\u0627\u0631\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0634\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0629 \u0648\u0623\u0646\u0638\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0634\u0639\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/meeting_assistant_flow)\n+4. **\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0645\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u0627\u062a**: \u064a\u0648\u0636\u062d \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u062b \u062d\u062f\u062b \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f \u0644\u062a\u0634\u063a\u064a\u0644 \u0625\u062c\u0631\u0627\u0621\u0627\u062a \u0645\u062a\u0627\u0628\u0639\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629. \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0633\u0628\u064a\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u060c \u0628\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0643\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0644 \u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u060c \u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642 \u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062b \u0644\u0648\u062d\u0629 Trello \u0648\u0625\u0631\u0633\u0627\u0644 \u0631\u0633\u0627\u0644\u0629 Slack \u0648\u062d\u0641\u0638 \u0627\u0644\u0646\u062a\u0627\u0626\u062c. \u0625\u0646\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0631\u0627\u0626\u0639 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0646\u062a\u0627\u0626\u062c \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0646 \u062d\u062f\u062b \u0648\u0627\u062d\u062f\u060c \u0645\u0645\u0627 \u064a\u062c\u0639\u0644\u0647 \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644\u064a\u064b\u0627 \u0644\u0625\u062f\u0627\u0631\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0634\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0629 \u0648\u0623\u0646\u0638\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0634\u0639\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a. [\u0639\u0631\u0636 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow)\n \n \u0645\u0646 \u062e\u0644\u0627\u0644 \u0627\u0633\u062a\u0643\u0634\u0627\u0641 \u0647\u0630\u0647 \u0627\u0644\u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629\u060c \u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646\u0643 \u0627\u0644\u062d\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0631\u0624\u0649 \u062d\u0648\u0644 \u0643\u064a\u0641\u064a\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u0641\u0627\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u0646 \u062a\u062f\u0641\u0642\u0627\u062a CrewAI \u0644\u062d\u0627\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u062a\u0646\u0648\u0639\u0629\u060c \u0645\u0646 \u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0643\u0631\u0631\u0629 \u0625\u0644\u0649 \u0625\u062f\u0627\u0631\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629 \u0645\u062a\u0639\u062f\u062f\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062e\u0637\u0648\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u062a\u062e\u0627\u0630 \u0627\u0644\u0642\u0631\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u062f\u064a\u0646\u0627\u0645\u064a\u0643\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062a\u063a\u0630\u064a\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a\u0629.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/examples/example.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/examples/example.mdx\nindex 0987e8dff5..6a5df55044 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/examples/example.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/examples/example.mdx\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"\u0627\u0644\u0631\u062f \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a\" icon=\"envelope\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow\">\n     \u0645\u0631\u0627\u0642\u0628\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0631\u064a\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0631\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0622\u0644\u064a.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Flow \u062a\u0642\u064a\u064a\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead_score_flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Flow \u062a\u0642\u064a\u064a\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow\">\n     \u062a\u0623\u0647\u064a\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0646 \u0645\u0639 \u062a\u062f\u062e\u0644 \u0628\u0634\u0631\u064a.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Flow \u0645\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f \u0627\u0644\u0627\u062c\u062a\u0645\u0627\u0639\u0627\u062a\" icon=\"calendar\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow\">\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062a\n \n <CardGroup cols={3}>\n-  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/crewai-langgraph\">\n+  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/CrewAI-LangGraph\">\n     \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0625\u0637\u0627\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644 LangGraph.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Azure OpenAI\" icon=\"cloud\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/azure_model\">\n@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## \u062f\u0641\u0627\u062a\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062d\u0638\u0627\u062a\n \n <CardGroup cols={2}>\n-  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n     Simple QA Crew + Flow.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"\u062c\u0645\u064a\u0639 \u062f\u0641\u0627\u062a\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062d\u0638\u0627\u062a\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"\u062c\u0645\u064a\u0639 \u062f\u0641\u0627\u062a\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062d\u0638\u0627\u062a\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     \u0623\u0645\u062b\u0644\u0629 \u062a\u0641\u0627\u0639\u0644\u064a\u0629 \u0644\u0644\u062a\u0639\u0644\u0645 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062a\u062c\u0631\u064a\u0628.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/concepts/flows.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/concepts/flows.mdx\nindex 8ba6aab52b..ec373889d8 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/concepts/flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/concepts/flows.mdx\n@@ -1041,13 +1041,13 @@ Plotting your flows is a powerful feature of CrewAI that enhances your ability t\n \n If you're interested in exploring additional examples of flows, we have a variety of recommendations in our examples repository. Here are four specific flow examples, each showcasing unique use cases to help you match your current problem type to a specific example:\n \n-1. **Email Auto Responder Flow**: This example demonstrates an infinite loop where a background job continually runs to automate email responses. It's a great use case for tasks that need to be performed repeatedly without manual intervention. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/email_auto_responder_flow)\n+1. **Email Auto Responder Flow**: This example demonstrates an infinite loop where a background job continually runs to automate email responses. It's a great use case for tasks that need to be performed repeatedly without manual intervention. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow)\n \n-2. **Lead Score Flow**: This flow showcases adding human-in-the-loop feedback and handling different conditional branches using the router. It's an excellent example of how to incorporate dynamic decision-making and human oversight into your workflows. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/lead-score-flow)\n+2. **Lead Score Flow**: This flow showcases adding human-in-the-loop feedback and handling different conditional branches using the router. It's an excellent example of how to incorporate dynamic decision-making and human oversight into your workflows. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow)\n \n-3. **Write a Book Flow**: This example excels at chaining multiple crews together, where the output of one crew is used by another. Specifically, one crew outlines an entire book, and another crew generates chapters based on the outline. Eventually, everything is connected to produce a complete book. This flow is perfect for complex, multi-step processes that require coordination between different tasks. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/write_a_book_with_flows)\n+3. **Write a Book Flow**: This example excels at chaining multiple crews together, where the output of one crew is used by another. Specifically, one crew outlines an entire book, and another crew generates chapters based on the outline. Eventually, everything is connected to produce a complete book. This flow is perfect for complex, multi-step processes that require coordination between different tasks. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/write_a_book_with_flows)\n \n-4. **Meeting Assistant Flow**: This flow demonstrates how to broadcast one event to trigger multiple follow-up actions. For instance, after a meeting is completed, the flow can update a Trello board, send a Slack message, and save the results. It's a great example of handling multiple outcomes from a single event, making it ideal for comprehensive task management and notification systems. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/meeting_assistant_flow)\n+4. **Meeting Assistant Flow**: This flow demonstrates how to broadcast one event to trigger multiple follow-up actions. For instance, after a meeting is completed, the flow can update a Trello board, send a Slack message, and save the results. It's a great example of handling multiple outcomes from a single event, making it ideal for comprehensive task management and notification systems. [View Example](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow)\n \n By exploring these examples, you can gain insights into how to leverage CrewAI Flows for various use cases, from automating repetitive tasks to managing complex, multi-step processes with dynamic decision-making and human feedback.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/examples/example.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/examples/example.mdx\nindex 37672cbfa3..b1b5f72c46 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/examples/example.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/examples/example.mdx\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"Email Auto Responder\" icon=\"envelope\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow\">\n     Automated email monitoring and replies.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Lead Score Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead_score_flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Lead Score Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow\">\n     Lead qualification with human\u2011in\u2011the\u2011loop.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Meeting Assistant Flow\" icon=\"calendar\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow\">\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## Integrations\n \n <CardGroup cols={3}>\n-  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/crewai-langgraph\">\n+  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/CrewAI-LangGraph\">\n     Integration with LangGraph framework.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Azure OpenAI\" icon=\"cloud\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/azure_model\">\n@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## Notebooks\n \n <CardGroup cols={2}>\n-  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n     Simple QA Crew + Flow.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"All Notebooks\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"All Notebooks\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     Interactive examples for learning and experimentation.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/concepts/flows.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/concepts/flows.mdx\nindex 3819b4ed74..e8c20f2f00 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/concepts/flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/concepts/flows.mdx\n@@ -1031,13 +1031,13 @@ flow\ub97c \uc2dc\uac01\ud654\ud558\uba74 \uc6cc\ud06c\ud50c\ub85c\uc758 \uad6c\uc870\ub97c \ub354\uc6b1 \uba85\ud655\ud558\uac8c \uc774\ud574\ud560\n \n \ucd94\uac00\uc801\uc778 flow \uc608\uc81c\ub97c \uc0b4\ud3b4\ubcf4\uace0 \uc2f6\uc73c\uc2dc\ub2e4\uba74, \uc800\ud76c examples \ub808\ud3ec\uc9c0\ud1a0\ub9ac\uc5d0\uc11c \ub2e4\uc591\ud55c \ucd94\ucc9c \uc608\uc81c\ub97c \ud655\uc778\ud558\uc2e4 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc544\ub798\ub294 \uac01\uac01 \uace0\uc720\ud55c \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uc0ac\ub840\ub97c \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc8fc\ub294 \ub124 \uac00\uc9c0 \uad6c\uccb4\uc801\uc778 flow \uc608\uc81c\ub85c, \ud604\uc7ac \ubb38\uc81c \uc720\ud615\uc5d0 \ub9de\ub294 \uc608\uc2dc\ub97c \ucc3e\ub294 \ub370 \ub3c4\uc6c0\uc774 \ub420 \uac83\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4:\n \n-1. **\uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc790\ub3d9 \uc751\ub2f5\uc790 Flow**: \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub294 \ubc31\uadf8\ub77c\uc6b4\ub4dc \uc791\uc5c5\uc774 \uacc4\uc18d \uc2e4\ud589\ub418\uba74\uc11c \uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc751\ub2f5\uc744 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ud558\ub294 \ubb34\ud55c \ub8e8\ud504\ub97c \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc218\ub3d9 \uac1c\uc785 \uc5c6\uc774 \ubc18\ubcf5\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \uc218\ud589\ud574\uc57c \ud558\ub294 \uc791\uc5c5\uc5d0 \uc801\ud569\ud55c \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uc0ac\ub840\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/email_auto_responder_flow)\n+1. **\uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc790\ub3d9 \uc751\ub2f5\uc790 Flow**: \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub294 \ubc31\uadf8\ub77c\uc6b4\ub4dc \uc791\uc5c5\uc774 \uacc4\uc18d \uc2e4\ud589\ub418\uba74\uc11c \uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc751\ub2f5\uc744 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ud558\ub294 \ubb34\ud55c \ub8e8\ud504\ub97c \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc218\ub3d9 \uac1c\uc785 \uc5c6\uc774 \ubc18\ubcf5\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \uc218\ud589\ud574\uc57c \ud558\ub294 \uc791\uc5c5\uc5d0 \uc801\ud569\ud55c \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uc0ac\ub840\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow)\n \n-2. **\ub9ac\ub4dc \uc810\uc218 Flow**: \uc774 flow \uc608\uc81c\ub294 human-in-the-loop \ud53c\ub4dc\ubc31\uc744 \ucd94\uac00\ud558\uace0 router\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud558\uc5ec \ub2e4\uc591\ud55c \uc870\uac74 \ubd84\uae30\ub97c \ucc98\ub9ac\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\ubc95\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc6cc\ud06c\ud50c\ub85c\uc6b0\uc5d0 \ub3d9\uc801 \uc758\uc0ac\uacb0\uc815\uacfc \uc778\uac04\uc758 \uad00\ub9ac\u00b7\uac10\ub3c5\uc744 \ud1b5\ud569\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\uc2dd\uc744 \ud655\uc778\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \ud6cc\ub96d\ud55c \uc608\uc2dc\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/lead-score-flow)\n+2. **\ub9ac\ub4dc \uc810\uc218 Flow**: \uc774 flow \uc608\uc81c\ub294 human-in-the-loop \ud53c\ub4dc\ubc31\uc744 \ucd94\uac00\ud558\uace0 router\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud558\uc5ec \ub2e4\uc591\ud55c \uc870\uac74 \ubd84\uae30\ub97c \ucc98\ub9ac\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\ubc95\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc6cc\ud06c\ud50c\ub85c\uc6b0\uc5d0 \ub3d9\uc801 \uc758\uc0ac\uacb0\uc815\uacfc \uc778\uac04\uc758 \uad00\ub9ac\u00b7\uac10\ub3c5\uc744 \ud1b5\ud569\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\uc2dd\uc744 \ud655\uc778\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \ud6cc\ub96d\ud55c \uc608\uc2dc\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow)\n \n-3. **\ucc45 \uc9d1\ud544 Flow**: \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub294 \uc5ec\ub7ec crew\ub97c \uc5f0\uc18d\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \uc5f0\uacb0\ud558\ub294 \ub370 \ud0c1\uc6d4\ud558\uba70, \ud55c crew\uc758 \ucd9c\ub825 \uacb0\uacfc\uac00 \ub2e4\ub978 crew\uc5d0 \uc758\ud574 \uc0ac\uc6a9\ub429\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uad6c\uccb4\uc801\uc73c\ub85c, \ud55c crew\uac00 \uc804\uccb4 \ucc45\uc758 \uac1c\uc694\ub97c \uc791\uc131\ud558\uace0, \ub2e4\ub978 crew\uac00 \uadf8 \uac1c\uc694\ub97c \ubc14\ud0d5\uc73c\ub85c \ucc55\ud130\ub97c \uc0dd\uc131\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uacb0\uad6d \ubaa8\ub4e0 \uac83\uc774 \uc5f0\uacb0\ub418\uc5b4 \uc644\uc131\ub41c \ucc45\uc774 \ub9cc\ub4e4\uc5b4\uc9d1\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc5ec\ub7ec \uc791\uc5c5 \uac04 \uc870\uc728\uc774 \ud544\uc694\ud55c \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c \ub2e4\ub2e8\uacc4 \ud504\ub85c\uc138\uc2a4\uc5d0 \uc801\ud569\ud55c flow\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/write_a_book_with_flows)\n+3. **\ucc45 \uc9d1\ud544 Flow**: \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub294 \uc5ec\ub7ec crew\ub97c \uc5f0\uc18d\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \uc5f0\uacb0\ud558\ub294 \ub370 \ud0c1\uc6d4\ud558\uba70, \ud55c crew\uc758 \ucd9c\ub825 \uacb0\uacfc\uac00 \ub2e4\ub978 crew\uc5d0 \uc758\ud574 \uc0ac\uc6a9\ub429\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uad6c\uccb4\uc801\uc73c\ub85c, \ud55c crew\uac00 \uc804\uccb4 \ucc45\uc758 \uac1c\uc694\ub97c \uc791\uc131\ud558\uace0, \ub2e4\ub978 crew\uac00 \uadf8 \uac1c\uc694\ub97c \ubc14\ud0d5\uc73c\ub85c \ucc55\ud130\ub97c \uc0dd\uc131\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uacb0\uad6d \ubaa8\ub4e0 \uac83\uc774 \uc5f0\uacb0\ub418\uc5b4 \uc644\uc131\ub41c \ucc45\uc774 \ub9cc\ub4e4\uc5b4\uc9d1\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc5ec\ub7ec \uc791\uc5c5 \uac04 \uc870\uc728\uc774 \ud544\uc694\ud55c \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c \ub2e4\ub2e8\uacc4 \ud504\ub85c\uc138\uc2a4\uc5d0 \uc801\ud569\ud55c flow\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/write_a_book_with_flows)\n \n-4. **\ubbf8\ud305 \uc5b4\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud134\ud2b8 Flow**: \uc774 flow\ub294 \ud558\ub098\uc758 \uc774\ubca4\ud2b8\uac00 \uc5ec\ub7ec \ud6c4\uc18d \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \ud2b8\ub9ac\uac70\ud558\ub3c4\ub85d \ube0c\ub85c\ub4dc\uce90\uc2a4\ud2b8\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\ubc95\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc608\ub97c \ub4e4\uc5b4, \ubbf8\ud305\uc774 \ub05d\ub09c \ud6c4 Trello \ubcf4\ub4dc\ub97c \uc5c5\ub370\uc774\ud2b8\ud558\uace0 Slack \uba54\uc2dc\uc9c0\ub97c \uc804\uc1a1\ud558\uba70 \uacb0\uacfc\ub97c \uc800\uc7a5\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4. \ud558\ub098\uc758 \uc774\ubca4\ud2b8\ub85c\ubd80\ud130 \uc5ec\ub7ec \uacb0\uacfc\ub97c \ucc98\ub9ac\ud558\ub294 \uc88b\uc740 \uc608\uc2dc\ub85c, \ud3ec\uad04\uc801\uc778 \uc791\uc5c5 \uad00\ub9ac \ubc0f \uc54c\ub9bc \uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c\uc5d0 \uc774\uc0c1\uc801\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/meeting_assistant_flow)\n+4. **\ubbf8\ud305 \uc5b4\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud134\ud2b8 Flow**: \uc774 flow\ub294 \ud558\ub098\uc758 \uc774\ubca4\ud2b8\uac00 \uc5ec\ub7ec \ud6c4\uc18d \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \ud2b8\ub9ac\uac70\ud558\ub3c4\ub85d \ube0c\ub85c\ub4dc\uce90\uc2a4\ud2b8\ud558\ub294 \ubc29\ubc95\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc90d\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc608\ub97c \ub4e4\uc5b4, \ubbf8\ud305\uc774 \ub05d\ub09c \ud6c4 Trello \ubcf4\ub4dc\ub97c \uc5c5\ub370\uc774\ud2b8\ud558\uace0 Slack \uba54\uc2dc\uc9c0\ub97c \uc804\uc1a1\ud558\uba70 \uacb0\uacfc\ub97c \uc800\uc7a5\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4. \ud558\ub098\uc758 \uc774\ubca4\ud2b8\ub85c\ubd80\ud130 \uc5ec\ub7ec \uacb0\uacfc\ub97c \ucc98\ub9ac\ud558\ub294 \uc88b\uc740 \uc608\uc2dc\ub85c, \ud3ec\uad04\uc801\uc778 \uc791\uc5c5 \uad00\ub9ac \ubc0f \uc54c\ub9bc \uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c\uc5d0 \uc774\uc0c1\uc801\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. [\uc608\uc81c \ubcf4\uae30](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow)\n \n \uc774 \uc608\uc81c\ub4e4\uc744 \ud1b5\ud574 \ubc18\ubcf5\ub418\ub294 \uc791\uc5c5 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ubd80\ud130 \ub3d9\uc801 \uc758\uc0ac\uacb0\uc815\uacfc \uc778\uac04 \ud53c\ub4dc\ubc31\uc774 \ud3ec\ud568\ub41c \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c \ub2e4\ub2e8\uacc4 \ud504\ub85c\uc138\uc2a4 \uad00\ub9ac\uc5d0 \uc774\ub974\uae30\uae4c\uc9c0 \ub2e4\uc591\ud55c \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uc0ac\ub840\uc5d0\uc11c CrewAI Flows\ub97c \uc5b4\ub5bb\uac8c \ud65c\uc6a9\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294\uc9c0\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \ud1b5\ucc30\ub825\uc744 \uc5bb\uc744 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/examples/cookbooks.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/examples/cookbooks.mdx\nindex 9b835cd1b1..af2c641c2a 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/examples/cookbooks.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/examples/cookbooks.mdx\n@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"Quickstarts \uc800\uc7a5\uc18c\" icon=\"bolt\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-quickstarts\">\n     \ud2b9\uc815 CrewAI \uae30\ub2a5\uc744 \ubcf4\uc5ec\uc8fc\ub294 \ub370\ubaa8\uc640 \uc18c\uaddc\ubaa8 \ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"\uc608\uc2dc\uc758 \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81\" icon=\"book-open\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"\uc608\uc2dc\uc758 \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81\" icon=\"book-open\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     \uc2e4\uc2b5\uc744 \uc704\ud55c \uc778\ud130\ub799\ud2f0\ube0c \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/examples/example.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/examples/example.mdx\nindex 68dcccc5d5..f96eba936f 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/examples/example.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/examples/example.mdx\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"\uc774\uba54\uc77c \uc790\ub3d9 \uc751\ub2f5\" icon=\"envelope\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow\">\n     \uc774\uba54\uc77c \ubaa8\ub2c8\ud130\ub9c1\uacfc \uc790\ub3d9 \uc751\ub2f5.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"\ub9ac\ub4dc \uc810\uc218 Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead_score_flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"\ub9ac\ub4dc \uc810\uc218 Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow\">\n     \ud734\uba3c\u2011\uc778\u2011\ub354\u2011\ub8e8\ud504 \ub9ac\ub4dc \ud3c9\uac00.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"\ubbf8\ud305 \uc5b4\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud134\ud2b8 Flow\" icon=\"calendar\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow\">\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## \ud1b5\ud569 (Integrations)\n \n <CardGroup cols={3}>\n-  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/crewai-langgraph\">\n+  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/CrewAI-LangGraph\">\n     LangGraph \ud504\ub808\uc784\uc6cc\ud06c \uc5f0\ub3d9.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Azure OpenAI\" icon=\"cloud\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/azure_model\">\n@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81 (Notebooks)\n \n <CardGroup cols={2}>\n-  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n     Simple QA Crew + Flow.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"\ubaa8\ub4e0 \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"\ubaa8\ub4e0 \ub178\ud2b8\ubd81\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     \ud559\uc2b5\uacfc \uc2e4\ud5d8\uc744 \uc704\ud55c \uc778\ud130\ub799\ud2f0\ube0c \uc608\uc2dc \ubaa8\uc74c.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/concepts/flows.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/concepts/flows.mdx\nindex aa4e3154fe..eb992d7746 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/concepts/flows.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/concepts/flows.mdx\n@@ -1028,13 +1028,13 @@ A plotagem dos flows \u00e9 um recurso poderoso do CrewAI para aprimorar o design e\n \n Se voc\u00ea deseja explorar exemplos adicionais de flows, acompanhe alguns exemplos em nosso reposit\u00f3rio de exemplos. Aqui est\u00e3o quatro sugest\u00f5es espec\u00edficas de flows, cada uma demonstrando casos de uso distintos para voc\u00ea escolher conforme seu problema:\n \n-1. **Email Auto Responder Flow**: Este exemplo demonstra um loop infinito, onde um job de background roda continuamente automatizando respostas de email. \u00c9 ideal para tarefas rotineiras sem interven\u00e7\u00e3o manual. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/email_auto_responder_flow)\n+1. **Email Auto Responder Flow**: Este exemplo demonstra um loop infinito, onde um job de background roda continuamente automatizando respostas de email. \u00c9 ideal para tarefas rotineiras sem interven\u00e7\u00e3o manual. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow)\n \n-2. **Lead Score Flow**: Destaca como adicionar feedback humano e manipular diferentes ramos condicionais usando router. Um \u00f3timo aprendizado para workflows com decis\u00e3o din\u00e2mica e supervis\u00e3o humana. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/lead-score-flow)\n+2. **Lead Score Flow**: Destaca como adicionar feedback humano e manipular diferentes ramos condicionais usando router. Um \u00f3timo aprendizado para workflows com decis\u00e3o din\u00e2mica e supervis\u00e3o humana. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow)\n \n-3. **Write a Book Flow**: Exemplo ideal para encadear m\u00faltiplas crews, onde a sa\u00edda de uma \u00e9 usada por outra. Uma crew faz um sum\u00e1rio do livro inteiro, outra gera cap\u00edtulos... Tudo conectado para entregar um livro completo. Perfeito para processos longos e coordenados. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/write_a_book_with_flows)\n+3. **Write a Book Flow**: Exemplo ideal para encadear m\u00faltiplas crews, onde a sa\u00edda de uma \u00e9 usada por outra. Uma crew faz um sum\u00e1rio do livro inteiro, outra gera cap\u00edtulos... Tudo conectado para entregar um livro completo. Perfeito para processos longos e coordenados. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/write_a_book_with_flows)\n \n-4. **Meeting Assistant Flow**: Demonstra como transmitir um evento para desencadear m\u00faltiplas a\u00e7\u00f5es posteriores. Exemplo: ao finalizar uma reuni\u00e3o, atualizar um Trello, enviar mensagem no Slack e salvar resultados ao mesmo tempo. Indicado para gerenciamento completo de tarefas e notifica\u00e7\u00f5es. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/meeting_assistant_flow)\n+4. **Meeting Assistant Flow**: Demonstra como transmitir um evento para desencadear m\u00faltiplas a\u00e7\u00f5es posteriores. Exemplo: ao finalizar uma reuni\u00e3o, atualizar um Trello, enviar mensagem no Slack e salvar resultados ao mesmo tempo. Indicado para gerenciamento completo de tarefas e notifica\u00e7\u00f5es. [Ver Exemplo](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow)\n \n Explore esses exemplos para descobrir como aproveitar CrewAI Flows em diferentes contextos \u2013 desde automa\u00e7\u00e3o de tarefas repetitivas at\u00e9 o gerenciamento de processos din\u00e2micos com decis\u00f5es e feedback humano.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/examples/cookbooks.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/examples/cookbooks.mdx\nindex 7057621a19..b72f36d112 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/examples/cookbooks.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/examples/cookbooks.mdx\n@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"Reposit\u00f3rio de Quickstarts\" icon=\"bolt\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-quickstarts\">\n     Demos e projetos pequenos que mostram capacidades espec\u00edficas do CrewAI.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Notebooks nos Exemplos\" icon=\"book-open\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"Notebooks nos Exemplos\" icon=\"book-open\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     Notebooks interativos para aprendizado pr\u00e1tico.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/examples/example.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/examples/example.mdx\nindex 9e30069b31..bde6762da4 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/examples/example.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/examples/example.mdx\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n   <Card title=\"Email Auto Responder\" icon=\"envelope\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow\">\n     Monitoramento e respostas de e\u2011mail.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Lead Score Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead_score_flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Lead Score Flow\" icon=\"chart-line\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow\">\n     Qualifica\u00e7\u00e3o de leads com revis\u00e3o humana.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Meeting Assistant Flow\" icon=\"calendar\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow\">\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## Integra\u00e7\u00f5es\n \n <CardGroup cols={3}>\n-  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/crewai-langgraph\">\n+  <Card title=\"CrewAI \u2194 LangGraph\" icon=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/CrewAI-LangGraph\">\n     Integra\u00e7\u00e3o com o framework LangGraph.\n   </Card>\n   <Card title=\"Azure OpenAI\" icon=\"cloud\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/integrations/azure_model\">\n@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n ## Notebooks\n \n <CardGroup cols={2}>\n-  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n+  <Card title=\"Simple QA Crew + Flow\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks/Simple%20QA%20Crew%20%2B%20Flow\">\n     Simple QA Crew + Flow.\n   </Card>\n-  <Card title=\"Todos os Notebooks\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/Notebooks\">\n+  <Card title=\"Todos os Notebooks\" icon=\"book\" href=\"https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples/tree/main/notebooks\">\n     Exemplos interativos para aprendizado e experimenta\u00e7\u00e3o.\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>\n\\ No newline at end of file\n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "Docs: broken crewAI-examples links after the repo reorganization\nSeveral documentation pages link to `crewAIInc/crewAI-examples` paths that no longer exist, so the links return 404. The examples repo was reorganized in #277 (`Reorganize repo structure and upgrade to CrewAI 0.152.0`, 2025-08-12): flows moved under `flows/`, `lead_score_flow` was renamed to `lead-score-flow`, `crewai-langgraph` became `CrewAI-LangGraph`, and the `Notebooks` directory became lowercase `notebooks`.\n\nAffected pages (en/ko/pt-BR/ar, docs/edge and docs/v1.15.28):\n\n- `examples/example.mdx` ??Lead Score Flow card, CrewAI <-> LangGraph card, Simple QA Crew + Flow card, All Notebooks card\n- `concepts/flows.mdx` ??the four \"View Example\" links at the bottom\n- `examples/cookbooks.mdx` (ko/pt-BR only) ??Notebooks card\n\nBroken -> working mappings (verified against the live repo tree via the git trees API and HTTP 200 on each new URL):\n\n| Old path (404) | New path (200) |\n|---|---|\n| `tree/main/email_auto_responder_flow` | `tree/main/flows/email_auto_responder_flow` |\n| `tree/main/lead-score-flow` | `tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow` |\n| `tree/main/meeting_assistant_flow` | `tree/main/flows/meeting_assistant_flow` |\n| `tree/main/write_a_book_with_flows` | `tree/main/flows/write_a_book_with_flows` |\n| `tree/main/flows/lead_score_flow` | `tree/main/flows/lead-score-flow` |\n| `tree/main/integrations/crewai-langgraph` | `tree/main/integrations/CrewAI-LangGraph` |\n| `tree/main/Notebooks` | `tree/main/notebooks` |\n\nNote: the \"Content Creator Flow\" card links to `tree/main/flows/content_creator_flow`, which currently exists as a broken submodule in crewAI-examples (a gitlink committed without `.gitmodules`, so GitHub renders 404). That one needs to be fixed on the crewAI-examples side; the docs link cannot be corrected from here.\n\nHappy to open a PR with the URL fixes if that is welcome.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-22T07:20:00Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8369, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8369", "issue_numbers": ["8368"], "base_commit": "95de6ea1fbf5cf3a9074d4efd20073bed39559c1", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\nindex e3ebae7ae7..ecab6d596c 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\n@@ -119,6 +119,7 @@ def get_supported_content_types(provider: str, api: str | None = None) -> list[s\n from crewai.tasks.conditional_task import ConditionalTask\n from crewai.tasks.task_output import TaskOutput\n from crewai.tools.agent_tools.agent_tools import AgentTools\n+from crewai.tools.agent_tools.base_agent_tools import BaseAgentTool\n from crewai.tools.agent_tools.read_file_tool import ReadFileTool\n from crewai.tools.base_tool import BaseTool\n from crewai.tools.tool_failure import ToolFailurePolicy\n@@ -1533,7 +1534,11 @@ def _create_manager_agent(self) -> None:\n         if self.manager_agent is not None:\n             self.manager_agent.allow_delegation = True\n             manager = self.manager_agent\n-            if manager.tools is not None and len(manager.tools) > 0:\n+            # Delegation tools are the crew's own: a manager built from\n+            # manager_llm keeps them on the next kickoff, copy() or train().\n+            if manager.tools is not None and any(\n+                not isinstance(tool, BaseAgentTool) for tool in manager.tools\n+            ):\n                 self._logger.log(\n                     \"warning\",\n                     \"Manager agent should not have tools\",\n@@ -1868,7 +1873,9 @@ def _update_manager_tools(\n         self, task: Task, tools: list[BaseTool]\n     ) -> list[BaseTool]:\n         if self.manager_agent:\n-            if task.agent:\n+            # A previous run leaves the manager assigned to the task; that is\n+            # not a worker to delegate to.\n+            if task.agent and task.agent is not self.manager_agent:\n                 tools = self._inject_delegation_tools(tools, task.agent, [task.agent])\n             else:\n                 tools = self._inject_delegation_tools(\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\nindex 5d3c2e546d..1205fae83d 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\n@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@\n \"\"\"Test Agent creation and execution basic functionality.\"\"\"\n \n+import asyncio\n from io import StringIO\n import json\n import threading\n@@ -38,6 +39,7 @@\n from crewai.knowledge.knowledge import Knowledge\n from crewai.knowledge.source.string_knowledge_source import StringKnowledgeSource\n from crewai.llm import LLM\n+from crewai.llms.base_llm import BaseLLM\n from crewai.memory.unified_memory import Memory\n from crewai.process import Process\n from crewai.project import CrewBase, agent, before_kickoff, crew, task\n@@ -2911,6 +2913,61 @@ def testing_tool(first_number: int, second_number: int) -> int:\n         crew.kickoff()\n \n \n+class _ScriptedReActLLM(BaseLLM):\n+    def __init__(self, *replies: str) -> None:\n+        super().__init__(model=\"offline\")\n+        self.replies = replies\n+        self.calls = 0\n+\n+    def supports_function_calling(self) -> bool:\n+        return False\n+\n+    def call(self, messages: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> str:\n+        reply = self.replies[self.calls % len(self.replies)]\n+        self.calls += 1\n+        return reply\n+\n+    async def acall(self, messages: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> str:\n+        return self.call(messages, **kwargs)\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"async_entry\", [False, True], ids=[\"sync\", \"async\"])\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"manager\", [\"manager_llm\", \"manager_agent\"])\n+def test_hierarchical_crew_delegates_to_workers_on_every_kickoff(\n+    manager, async_entry\n+):\n+    delegate = json.dumps(\n+        {\"task\": \"Write a word\", \"context\": \"None\", \"coworker\": \"Writer\"}\n+    )\n+    manager_llm = _ScriptedReActLLM(\n+        f\"Thought: Delegate\\nAction: Delegate work to coworker\\nAction Input: {delegate}\",\n+        \"Thought: Done\\nFinal Answer: hello\",\n+    )\n+    worker_llm = _ScriptedReActLLM(\"Thought: Done\\nFinal Answer: hello\")\n+    writer = Agent(role=\"Writer\", goal=\"Write\", backstory=\"Writes\", llm=worker_llm)\n+    task = Task(description=\"Get a word\", expected_output=\"A word\")\n+    if manager == \"manager_llm\":\n+        crew = Crew(\n+            agents=[writer],\n+            tasks=[task],\n+            process=Process.hierarchical,\n+            manager_llm=manager_llm,\n+        )\n+    else:\n+        boss = Agent(role=\"Boss\", goal=\"Manage\", backstory=\"Manages\", llm=manager_llm)\n+        crew = Crew(\n+            agents=[writer],\n+            tasks=[task],\n+            process=Process.hierarchical,\n+            manager_agent=boss,\n+        )\n+\n+    for run in (1, 2):\n+        result = asyncio.run(crew.akickoff()) if async_entry else crew.kickoff()\n+        assert result.raw == \"hello\"\n+        assert worker_llm.calls == run\n+\n+\n @pytest.mark.vcr()\n def test_crew_train_success(researcher, writer, monkeypatch):\n     task = Task(\n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] Hierarchical crew fails on its second kickoff: manager_llm crashes, manager_agent delegates to itself\n### Description\n\nA hierarchical crew only works on its first `kickoff()`. Anything that runs the same crew again breaks: a second\n`kickoff()`/`akickoff()`, `copy().kickoff()` after a run, `kickoff_for_each()` after a run, and every\n`train(n_iterations > 1)` (it calls `kickoff()` repeatedly on one copy).\n\nWith `manager_llm`, the first run stores the manager it built, with its delegation tools, in `crew.manager_agent`.\nThe next run sees a manager that has tools and raises `Exception: Manager agent should not have tools`.\n\nWith `manager_agent`, the first run assigns the manager to each task without an agent. On the next run\n`_update_manager_tools` treats the manager as the task's worker, so the only coworker the manager can delegate\nto is itself and delegation silently stops working.\n\nThis was reported before for training (#2131) and in a flow (#1851); both were closed without a fix.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Build a hierarchical crew with one worker agent and `manager_llm=...` (or `manager_agent=...`).\n2. Run `crew.kickoff()` once. It works and the manager delegates to the worker.\n3. Run `crew.kickoff()` again on the same crew.\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nEvery run behaves like the first: no exception, and the manager can delegate to the crew's worker agents.\n\n### Screenshots/Code snippets\n\n```python\nimport json\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom crewai import Agent, Crew, Process, Task\nfrom crewai.llms.base_llm import BaseLLM\n\n\nclass ScriptedLLM(BaseLLM):\n    def __init__(self, *replies: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(model=\"offline\")\n        self.replies = replies\n        self.calls = 0\n\n    def supports_function_calling(self) -> bool:\n        return False\n\n    def call(self, messages: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> str:\n        reply = self.replies[self.calls % len(self.replies)]\n        self.calls += 1\n        return reply\n\n    async def acall(self, messages: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> str:\n        return self.call(messages, **kwargs)\n\n\ndelegate = json.dumps({\"task\": \"Write a word\", \"context\": \"None\", \"coworker\": \"Writer\"})\nmanager_llm = ScriptedLLM(\n    f\"Thought: Delegate\\nAction: Delegate work to coworker\\nAction Input: {delegate}\",\n    \"Thought: Done\\nFinal Answer: hello\",\n)\nworker_llm = ScriptedLLM(\"Thought: Done\\nFinal Answer: hello\")\nwriter = Agent(role=\"Writer\", goal=\"Write\", backstory=\"Writes\", llm=worker_llm)\ntask = Task(description=\"Get a word\", expected_output=\"A word\")\n\ncrew = Crew(agents=[writer], tasks=[task], process=Process.hierarchical, manager_llm=manager_llm)\nfor run in (1, 2):\n    print(run, crew.kickoff().raw, \"worker calls:\", worker_llm.calls)\n```\n\nOperating System: Other (specify in additional context)\nPython Version: 3.12\ncrewAI Version: 1.15.28 (main @ a8877f0cd)\ncrewAI Tools Version: N/A (not used in the repro)\nVirtual Environment: Venv\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS Monterey\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.12\n\n### crewAI Version\n\ncrewAI Version: 1.15.28 (main @ a8877f0cd)\n\n### crewAI Tools Version\n\n N/A (not used in the repro)\n\n### Virtual Environment\n\nVenv\n\n### Evidence\n\n```\n1 hello worker calls: 1\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  ...\nException: Manager agent should not have tools\n```\nWith `manager_agent=Agent(role=\"Boss\", ...)` instead of `manager_llm`, both runs return, but on run 2 the\ndelegation tool lists only \"Boss\" as a coworker, the worker is never called, and `worker calls` stays at 1.\n\n\n\n### Possible Solution\n\n\nIn `_create_manager_agent`, only reject tools that are not the crew's own delegation tools (`BaseAgentTool`).\nIn `_update_manager_tools`, don't treat the manager as the task's worker when it is the agent left on the task\nby the previous run.\n\n### Additional context\n\nmacOS 26. Reproduced on Python 3.13 with a uv-managed venv (3.13 is not in the version dropdown).\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-21T16:59:51Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8366, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8366", "issue_numbers": ["8365"], "base_commit": "5daf9cfc01b0d4306944be6799d1973bea223e6b", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\nindex fced02558b..e3ebae7ae7 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/crew.py\n@@ -85,6 +85,7 @@ def get_supported_content_types(provider: str, api: str | None = None) -> list[s\n from crewai.events.types.crew_events import (\n     CrewKickoffCompletedEvent,\n     CrewKickoffFailedEvent,\n+    CrewKickoffStartedEvent,\n     CrewTestCompletedEvent,\n     CrewTestFailedEvent,\n     CrewTestStartedEvent,\n@@ -2119,6 +2120,22 @@ def replay(self, task_id: str, inputs: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> CrewOutp\n         if replay_inputs:\n             self._interpolate_inputs(replay_inputs)\n \n+        # Mirror prepare_kickoff: replay's execution tail emits\n+        # CrewKickoffCompletedEvent(started_event_id=self._kickoff_event_id),\n+        # so a start event must scope it \u2014 otherwise the bus warns about an\n+        # unpaired ending event and the completion points at the original\n+        # kickoff's start id.\n+        started_event = CrewKickoffStartedEvent(\n+            crew_name=self.name, inputs=replay_inputs\n+        )\n+        self._kickoff_event_id = started_event.event_id\n+        future = crewai_event_bus.emit(self, started_event)\n+        if future is not None:\n+            try:\n+                future.result()\n+            except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001,S110\n+                pass\n+\n         if self.process == Process.hierarchical:\n             self._create_manager_agent()\n \n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\nindex 8cb9782397..5d3c2e546d 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_crew.py\n@@ -3084,6 +3084,72 @@ def test_replay_feature(researcher, writer):\n         assert mock_execute_task.call_count == 3\n \n \n+def test_replay_emits_paired_kickoff_events(researcher, writer):\n+    \"\"\"replay() must emit its own CrewKickoffStartedEvent before completing.\n+\n+    The execution tail of replay() emits CrewKickoffCompletedEvent(started_event_id\n+    = self._kickoff_event_id). Without a start event scoping the replay, the bus\n+    warns about an unpaired ending event and the completion points at the\n+    original kickoff's start id, corrupting event pairing for listeners.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    list_ideas = Task(\n+        description=\"Generate a list of 5 interesting ideas to explore for an article, where each bulletpoint is under 15 words.\",\n+        expected_output=\"Bullet point list of 5 important events. No additional commentary.\",\n+        agent=researcher,\n+    )\n+    write = Task(\n+        description=\"Write a sentence about the events\",\n+        expected_output=\"A sentence about the events\",\n+        agent=writer,\n+        context=[list_ideas],\n+    )\n+\n+    crew = Crew(\n+        agents=[researcher, writer],\n+        tasks=[list_ideas, write],\n+        process=Process.sequential,\n+    )\n+\n+    started_events: list[CrewKickoffStartedEvent] = []\n+\n+    def on_started(source, event: CrewKickoffStartedEvent):\n+        started_events.append(event)\n+\n+    crewai_event_bus.register_handler(CrewKickoffStartedEvent, on_started)\n+    try:\n+        with patch.object(Task, \"execute_sync\") as mock_execute_task:\n+            mock_execute_task.side_effect = [\n+                TaskOutput(\n+                    description=task.description,\n+                    raw=\"Mocked output\",\n+                    agent=\"Researcher\",\n+                    json_dict=None,\n+                    output_format=OutputFormat.RAW,\n+                    pydantic=None,\n+                    summary=\"Mocked output\",\n+                    messages=[],\n+                )\n+                for task in [list_ideas, write, write]\n+            ]\n+\n+            crew.kickoff()\n+            kickoff_start_ids = {event.event_id for event in started_events}\n+            assert kickoff_start_ids, \"kickoff() must emit CrewKickoffStartedEvent\"\n+\n+            crew.replay(str(write.id))\n+    finally:\n+        crewai_event_bus.off(CrewKickoffStartedEvent, on_started)\n+\n+    replay_starts = [\n+        event for event in started_events if event.event_id not in kickoff_start_ids\n+    ]\n+    assert replay_starts, \"replay() must emit its own CrewKickoffStartedEvent\"\n+    # The completion event is constructed with started_event_id=self._kickoff_event_id\n+    # (see _create_crew_output), so the pairing is correct exactly when the id\n+    # left behind points at the replay's own start event.\n+    assert crew._kickoff_event_id == replay_starts[-1].event_id\n+\n+\n def test_replay_rejects_changed_task_order(researcher):\n     \"\"\"Replay must not restore a saved output onto a different current task.\"\"\"\n     research = Task(\n", "problem_statement": "crew.replay() emits CrewKickoffCompletedEvent without a matching CrewKickoffStartedEvent\n## Description\n\n`crew.replay()` skips `prepare_kickoff` entirely, but its execution tail still emits a `CrewKickoffCompletedEvent` built with `started_event_id=self._kickoff_event_id` (`crew.py`, `_create_crew_output`). The only place a `CrewKickoffStartedEvent` is emitted is `prepare_kickoff` (`crews/utils.py`), which replay never calls.\n\nTwo user-visible consequences on every replay:\n\n1. The event bus warns:\n   ```\n   [CrewAIEventsBus] Warning: Ending event 'crew_kickoff_completed' emitted with empty scope stack. Missing starting event?\n   ```\n2. The replay's completion event points at the **original kickoff's** start event id \u2014 two completions reference one start, corrupting event pairing / trace causality for any listener (telemetry, tracing, custom observability).\n\n## Reproduction\n\nReproducible on current main with a 2-task crew using mocked `Task.execute_sync`: register listeners for both event types, `kickoff()`, then `replay(task_id)`:\n\n```\nevents during kickoff: start-count=1 completed-count=1\n--- calling crew.replay() ---\n[CrewAIEventsBus] Warning: Ending event 'crew_kickoff_completed' emitted with empty scope stack. Missing starting event?\nevents during replay: starts=0\nBUG: replay emitted NO CrewKickoffStartedEvent\nreplay completed.started_event_id == first kickoff's start id: True\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`replay()` emits its own `CrewKickoffStartedEvent` (with the replay inputs) before executing tasks, so the completion event pairs with a fresh start id \u2014 mirroring what `prepare_kickoff` does for `kickoff()`.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nIn `replay()`, after `_interpolate_inputs` and before task execution, emit `CrewKickoffStartedEvent(crew_name=self.name, inputs=replay_inputs)`, store its `event_id` in `self._kickoff_event_id`, and wait for the emit future like `prepare_kickoff` does.\n\nHappy to submit a PR with a regression test if the approach sounds right.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:22:37Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8363, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8363", "issue_numbers": ["8362"], "base_commit": "7a6d9d25cfaa4721e510fb32b4d4c31b91f01d45", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py\nindex 492faddf22..6f2d3d1c1f 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py\n@@ -1854,6 +1854,11 @@ def execute_tool_action(self) -> Literal[\"tool_completed\", \"tool_result_is_final\n                 function_calling_llm=self.function_calling_llm,\n                 crew=self.crew,\n             )\n+        except HookAborted:\n+            # A deliberate stop: the generic handler below would feed the\n+            # policy abort back to the LLM as a recoverable observation.\n+            raise\n+\n         except ToolExecutionFailedError:\n             # A deliberate stop: the generic handler below would feed it back\n             # to the LLM as a recoverable observation.\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/agents/test_react_tool_hook_contract.py b/lib/crewai/tests/agents/test_react_tool_hook_contract.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..278c6de598\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/agents/test_react_tool_hook_contract.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@\n+\"\"\"ReAct text-path tool hooks must retain aborts and use effective cache inputs.\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+from unittest.mock import patch\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from crewai.agents.agent_executor import AgentExecutor\n+from crewai.agents.cache.cache_handler import CacheHandler\n+from crewai.agents.parser import AgentAction\n+from crewai.agents.tools_handler import ToolsHandler\n+from crewai.events import crewai_event_bus\n+from crewai.hooks.dispatch import HookAborted, InterceptionPoint, clear_all, on\n+from crewai.tools import BaseTool\n+from crewai.tools.base_tool import to_langchain\n+\n+\n+class LookupTool(BaseTool):\n+    name: str = \"lookup\"\n+    description: str = \"Look up a value.\"\n+\n+    def _run(self, term: str = \"default\") -> str:\n+        return f\"value:{term}\"\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)\n+def clean_hooks():\n+    clear_all()\n+    yield\n+    crewai_event_bus.flush()\n+    clear_all()\n+\n+\n+def _react_text_executor() -> tuple[AgentExecutor, AgentAction]:\n+    \"\"\"Wire an executor for the ReAct text tool route (execute_tool_action).\"\"\"\n+    tool = LookupTool()\n+    structured = to_langchain([tool])\n+    handler = ToolsHandler(cache=CacheHandler())\n+    executor = AgentExecutor(\n+        tools=structured, original_tools=[tool], tools_handler=handler\n+    )\n+    action = AgentAction(\n+        thought=\"I should look this up\",\n+        tool=\"lookup\",\n+        tool_input='{\"term\": \"hello\"}',\n+        text=(\n+            \"Thought: I should look this up\\n\"\n+            'Action: lookup\\nAction Input: {\"term\": \"hello\"}'\n+        ),\n+    )\n+    executor.state.current_answer = action\n+    return executor, action\n+\n+\n+def test_post_tool_abort_reaches_caller_on_react_text_path():\n+    abort = HookAborted(\"policy denied\", source=\"test-policy\")\n+\n+    @on(InterceptionPoint.POST_TOOL_CALL)\n+    def deny(_context):\n+        raise abort\n+\n+    executor, action = _react_text_executor()\n+\n+    with pytest.raises(HookAborted) as exc:\n+        executor.execute_tool_action()\n+\n+    assert exc.value is abort\n+    # The abort must not be folded into a recoverable observation for the LLM.\n+    assert \"Error executing tool\" not in action.text\n+\n+\n+def test_plain_error_still_becomes_recovery_observation():\n+    \"\"\"Only deliberate aborts re-raise; plain errors stay recoverable.\"\"\"\n+    executor, action = _react_text_executor()\n+\n+    with patch(\n+        \"crewai.agents.agent_executor.execute_tool_and_check_finality\",\n+        side_effect=RuntimeError(\"boom\"),\n+    ):\n+        result = executor.execute_tool_action()\n+\n+    assert result == \"tool_completed\"\n+    assert \"Error executing tool: boom\" in action.text\n", "problem_statement": "ReAct text tool path swallows HookAborted from POST_TOOL_CALL hooks\n### Description\n\nWhen an agent runs on the ReAct text-based tool route (no native function calling), a `HookAborted` raised by a `POST_TOOL_CALL` policy hook is silently swallowed instead of terminating the run.\n\n`AgentExecutor.execute_tool_action` (`lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py`, ~line 1857) wraps `execute_tool_and_check_finality` in `try/except`. It correctly re-raises `ToolExecutionFailedError`, but the following `except Exception` also catches `HookAborted` (a subclass of `Exception`) and converts it into a recoverable observation:\n\n```\nObservation: Error executing tool: deny\n```\n\nThe agent then keeps iterating and can call the vetoed tool again.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom crewai.hooks import InterceptionPoint, on\nfrom crewai.hooks.dispatch import HookAborted\n\n@on(InterceptionPoint.POST_TOOL_CALL)\ndef deny(ctx):\n    raise HookAborted(\"deletion not allowed\")\n\nagent = Agent(role=..., goal=..., backstory=..., llm=<text-mode LLM>, tools=[...])\nagent.kickoff(\"delete the file\")   # abort never surfaces; LLM receives a tool-error observation\n```\n\n(With a native-function-calling LLM the same setup raises `HookAborted` out of `kickoff` as expected.)\n\n### Impact\n\n- The documented hook contract (`@on` docstring in `hooks/dispatch.py`: `raise HookAborted(\"deletion not allowed\")`) is broken on this path: a policy veto is downgraded to a tool error the LLM can retry around.\n- Guardrail hooks (blocking destructive tools, PII exfiltration, cost caps) do not stop the run when the model uses text tool calling.\n- Inconsistent behavior between the two tool-call modes for identical hook setups: the native path re-raises (`execute_native_tool`), the parallel todo executor re-raises, LiteAgent re-raises \u2014 only the ReAct text path swallows.\n\n`HookAborted` should be re-raised before the generic `except Exception`, mirroring the existing `ToolExecutionFailedError` passthrough in the same function.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:24:38Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8359, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8359", "issue_numbers": ["8358"], "base_commit": "a71be46d53b5d111a8c7819fd183e19677ed600f", "patch": "diff --git a/docs/edge/ar/observability/langtrace.mdx b/docs/edge/ar/observability/langtrace.mdx\nindex d07f3f35ee..3576f7a7f0 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ar/observability/langtrace.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ar/observability/langtrace.mdx\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ Langtrace \u0647\u0648 \u0623\u062f\u0627\u0629 \u0645\u0641\u062a\u0648\u062d\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u062e\u0627\u0631\u062c\u064a\u0629 \u062a\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f\u0643 \u0641\u064a\n \n <Steps>\n    <Step title=\"\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0633\u062c\u064a\u0644 \u0641\u064a Langtrace\">\n-      \u0633\u062c\u0651\u0644 \u0628\u0632\u064a\u0627\u0631\u0629 [https://langtrace.ai/signup](https://langtrace.ai/signup).\n+      \u0633\u062c\u0651\u0644 \u0628\u0632\u064a\u0627\u0631\u0629 [https://app.langtrace.ai/signup](https://app.langtrace.ai/signup).\n    </Step>\n    <Step title=\"\u0625\u0646\u0634\u0627\u0621 \u0645\u0634\u0631\u0648\u0639\">\n       \u0639\u064a\u0651\u0646 \u0646\u0648\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0634\u0631\u0648\u0639 \u0625\u0644\u0649 `CrewAI` \u0648\u0642\u0645 \u0628\u062a\u0648\u0644\u064a\u062f \u0645\u0641\u062a\u0627\u062d API.\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ar/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx b/docs/edge/ar/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\nindex 0899dbd9f0..be8b99b672 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ar/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ar/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n \u0639\u0632\u0651\u0632 \u0639\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0633\u062a\u0631\u062c\u0627\u0639 \u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0630\u0643\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0635\u0637\u0646\u0627\u0639\u064a \u0627\u0644\u062e\u0627\u0635\u0629 \u0628\u0643 \u0628\u0640:\n \n- - [\u0628\u0646\u064a\u0629 \u062a\u062d\u062a\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u062f\u0648\u0646 \u062e\u0627\u062f\u0645](https://docs.browserbase.com/under-the-hood) \u062a\u0648\u0641\u0631 \u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0648\u062b\u0648\u0642\u0629 \u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u0631\u0627\u062c \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0646 \u0648\u0627\u062c\u0647\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629\n- - [\u0648\u0636\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062e\u0641\u064a](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/stealth-mode) \u0645\u0639 \u062a\u0643\u062a\u064a\u0643\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0635\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0636\u0645\u0646\u0629 \u0648\u062d\u0644 CAPTCHA \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a\n- - [\u0645\u0635\u062d\u062d \u0627\u0644\u062c\u0644\u0633\u0627\u062a](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/sessions) \u0644\u0641\u062d\u0635 \u062c\u0644\u0633\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062c\u062f\u0648\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0632\u0645\u0646\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0634\u0628\u0643\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0633\u062c\u0644\u0627\u062a\n- - [\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0635\u062d\u064a\u062d \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0628\u0627\u0634\u0631](https://docs.browserbase.com/guides/session-debug-connection/browser-remote-control) \u0644\u062a\u0635\u062d\u064a\u062d \u0627\u0644\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0628\u0633\u0631\u0639\u0629\n+ - [\u0628\u0646\u064a\u0629 \u062a\u062d\u062a\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u062f\u0648\u0646 \u062e\u0627\u062f\u0645](https://docs.browserbase.com/welcome/what-is-browserbase) \u062a\u0648\u0641\u0631 \u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0648\u062b\u0648\u0642\u0629 \u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u0631\u0627\u062c \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0646 \u0648\u0627\u062c\u0647\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629\n+ - [\u0648\u0636\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062e\u0641\u064a](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/identity/overview) \u0645\u0639 \u062a\u0643\u062a\u064a\u0643\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0635\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0636\u0645\u0646\u0629 \u0648\u062d\u0644 CAPTCHA \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a\n+ - [\u0645\u0635\u062d\u062d \u0627\u0644\u062c\u0644\u0633\u0627\u062a](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/observability) \u0644\u0641\u062d\u0635 \u062c\u0644\u0633\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062c\u062f\u0648\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0632\u0645\u0646\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0634\u0628\u0643\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0633\u062c\u0644\u0627\u062a\n+ - [\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0635\u062d\u064a\u062d \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0628\u0627\u0634\u0631](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/session-live-view) \u0644\u062a\u0635\u062d\u064a\u062d \u0627\u0644\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0628\u0633\u0631\u0639\u0629\n \n ## \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062b\u0628\u064a\u062a\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/en/observability/langtrace.mdx b/docs/edge/en/observability/langtrace.mdx\nindex 8257f8eb7a..45f98de996 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/observability/langtrace.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/observability/langtrace.mdx\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ This integration allows you to log hyperparameters, monitor performance regressi\n \n <Steps>\n    <Step title=\"Sign up for Langtrace\">\n-      Sign up by visiting [https://langtrace.ai/signup](https://langtrace.ai/signup).\n+      Sign up by visiting [https://app.langtrace.ai/signup](https://app.langtrace.ai/signup).\n    </Step>\n    <Step title=\"Create a project\">\n       Set the project type to `CrewAI` and generate an API key.\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/en/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx b/docs/edge/en/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\nindex e53834d4bb..f445a005de 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n Power your AI data retrievals with:\n \n- - [Serverless Infrastructure](https://docs.browserbase.com/under-the-hood) providing reliable browsers to extract data from complex UIs\n- - [Stealth Mode](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/stealth-mode) with included fingerprinting tactics and automatic captcha solving\n- - [Session Debugger](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/sessions) to inspect your Browser Session with networks timeline and logs\n- - [Live Debug](https://docs.browserbase.com/guides/session-debug-connection/browser-remote-control) to quickly debug your automation\n+ - [Serverless Infrastructure](https://docs.browserbase.com/welcome/what-is-browserbase) providing reliable browsers to extract data from complex UIs\n+ - [Stealth Mode](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/identity/overview) with included fingerprinting tactics and automatic captcha solving\n+ - [Session Debugger](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/observability) to inspect your Browser Session with networks timeline and logs\n+ - [Live Debug](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/session-live-view) to quickly debug your automation\n \n ## Installation\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/observability/langtrace.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/observability/langtrace.mdx\nindex 05848d5868..47d9487fad 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/observability/langtrace.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/observability/langtrace.mdx\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ Langtrace\ub294 CrewAI\uc5d0 \uc9c1\uc811 \ub0b4\uc7a5\ub418\uc5b4 \uc788\uc9c0\ub294 \uc54a\uc9c0\ub9cc, CrewAI\uc640 \ud568\uaed8\n \n <Steps>\n    <Step title=\"Langtrace\uc5d0 \uac00\uc785\ud558\uae30\">\n-      [https://langtrace.ai/signup](https://langtrace.ai/signup)\uc5d0\uc11c \uac00\uc785\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n+      [https://app.langtrace.ai/signup](https://app.langtrace.ai/signup)\uc5d0\uc11c \uac00\uc785\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n    </Step>\n    <Step title=\"\ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8 \uc0dd\uc131\">\n       \ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8 \uc720\ud615\uc744 `CrewAI`\ub85c \uc124\uc815\ud558\uace0 API \ud0a4\ub97c \uc0dd\uc131\ud558\uc138\uc694.\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\nindex a2fdfecd36..8135b81f9b 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n AI \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc218\uc9d1\uc744 \ub2e4\uc74c\uacfc \uac19\uc774 \uac15\ud654\ud558\uc138\uc694:\n \n- - [\uc11c\ubc84\ub9ac\uc2a4 \uc778\ud504\ub77c\uc2a4\ud2b8\ub7ed\ucc98](https://docs.browserbase.com/under-the-hood)\ub97c \ud1b5\ud574 \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c UI\uc5d0\uc11c \ub370\uc774\ud130\ub97c \ucd94\ucd9c\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \uc2e0\ub8b0\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \ube0c\ub77c\uc6b0\uc800 \uc81c\uacf5\n- - [\uc2a4\ud154\uc2a4 \ubaa8\ub4dc](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/stealth-mode)\uc5d0\uc11c\ub294 \uc9c0\ubb38 \uc778\uc2dd \ud68c\ud53c \uae30\ubc95\uacfc \uc790\ub3d9 \ucea1\ucc28 \uc194\ub8e8\uc158\uc774 \ud3ec\ud568\ub418\uc5b4 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4\n- - [\uc138\uc158 \ub514\ubc84\uac70](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/sessions)\ub97c \ud1b5\ud574 \ub124\ud2b8\uc6cc\ud06c \ud0c0\uc784\ub77c\uc778\uacfc \ub85c\uadf8\ub85c Browser Session\uc744 \uc810\uac80\n- - [\ub77c\uc774\ube0c \ub514\ubc84\uadf8](https://docs.browserbase.com/guides/session-debug-connection/browser-remote-control)\ub85c \uc790\ub3d9\ud654 \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \uc2e0\uc18d\ud558\uac8c \ub514\ubc84\uae45\n+ - [\uc11c\ubc84\ub9ac\uc2a4 \uc778\ud504\ub77c\uc2a4\ud2b8\ub7ed\ucc98](https://docs.browserbase.com/welcome/what-is-browserbase)\ub97c \ud1b5\ud574 \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c UI\uc5d0\uc11c \ub370\uc774\ud130\ub97c \ucd94\ucd9c\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \uc2e0\ub8b0\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \ube0c\ub77c\uc6b0\uc800 \uc81c\uacf5\n+ - [\uc2a4\ud154\uc2a4 \ubaa8\ub4dc](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/identity/overview)\uc5d0\uc11c\ub294 \uc9c0\ubb38 \uc778\uc2dd \ud68c\ud53c \uae30\ubc95\uacfc \uc790\ub3d9 \ucea1\ucc28 \uc194\ub8e8\uc158\uc774 \ud3ec\ud568\ub418\uc5b4 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4\n+ - [\uc138\uc158 \ub514\ubc84\uac70](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/observability)\ub97c \ud1b5\ud574 \ub124\ud2b8\uc6cc\ud06c \ud0c0\uc784\ub77c\uc778\uacfc \ub85c\uadf8\ub85c Browser Session\uc744 \uc810\uac80\n+ - [\ub77c\uc774\ube0c \ub514\ubc84\uadf8](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/session-live-view)\ub85c \uc790\ub3d9\ud654 \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \uc2e0\uc18d\ud558\uac8c \ub514\ubc84\uae45\n \n ## \uc124\uce58\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/observability/langtrace.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/observability/langtrace.mdx\nindex 470c429338..2f0965ff7d 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/observability/langtrace.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/observability/langtrace.mdx\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ Essa integra\u00e7\u00e3o permite o registro de hiperpar\u00e2metros, o monitoramento de reg\n \n <Steps>\n    <Step title=\"Crie uma conta no Langtrace\">\n-      Cadastre-se acessando [https://langtrace.ai/signup](https://langtrace.ai/signup).\n+      Cadastre-se acessando [https://app.langtrace.ai/signup](https://app.langtrace.ai/signup).\n    </Step>\n    <Step title=\"Crie um projeto\">\n       Defina o tipo do projeto como `CrewAI` e gere uma chave de API.\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\nindex ef18a46475..7c8dce46f1 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n Potencialize suas buscas de dados para IA com:\n \n- - [Infraestrutura Serverless](https://docs.browserbase.com/under-the-hood) fornecendo navegadores confi\u00e1veis para extrair dados de interfaces complexas\n- - [Modo Stealth](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/stealth-mode) com t\u00e1ticas de fingerprinting e resolu\u00e7\u00e3o autom\u00e1tica de captcha inclu\u00eddas\n- - [Depurador de Sess\u00e3o](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/sessions) para inspecionar sua Sess\u00e3o do Navegador com linha do tempo de rede e logs\n- - [Depura\u00e7\u00e3o Ao Vivo](https://docs.browserbase.com/guides/session-debug-connection/browser-remote-control) para depurar rapidamente sua automa\u00e7\u00e3o\n+ - [Infraestrutura Serverless](https://docs.browserbase.com/welcome/what-is-browserbase) fornecendo navegadores confi\u00e1veis para extrair dados de interfaces complexas\n+ - [Modo Stealth](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/identity/overview) com t\u00e1ticas de fingerprinting e resolu\u00e7\u00e3o autom\u00e1tica de captcha inclu\u00eddas\n+ - [Depurador de Sess\u00e3o](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/observability) para inspecionar sua Sess\u00e3o do Navegador com linha do tempo de rede e logs\n+ - [Depura\u00e7\u00e3o Ao Vivo](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/session-live-view) para depurar rapidamente sua automa\u00e7\u00e3o\n \n ## Instala\u00e7\u00e3o\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/observability/langtrace.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/observability/langtrace.mdx\nindex d07f3f35ee..3576f7a7f0 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/observability/langtrace.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/observability/langtrace.mdx\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ Langtrace \u0647\u0648 \u0623\u062f\u0627\u0629 \u0645\u0641\u062a\u0648\u062d\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u062e\u0627\u0631\u062c\u064a\u0629 \u062a\u0633\u0627\u0639\u062f\u0643 \u0641\u064a\n \n <Steps>\n    <Step title=\"\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0633\u062c\u064a\u0644 \u0641\u064a Langtrace\">\n-      \u0633\u062c\u0651\u0644 \u0628\u0632\u064a\u0627\u0631\u0629 [https://langtrace.ai/signup](https://langtrace.ai/signup).\n+      \u0633\u062c\u0651\u0644 \u0628\u0632\u064a\u0627\u0631\u0629 [https://app.langtrace.ai/signup](https://app.langtrace.ai/signup).\n    </Step>\n    <Step title=\"\u0625\u0646\u0634\u0627\u0621 \u0645\u0634\u0631\u0648\u0639\">\n       \u0639\u064a\u0651\u0646 \u0646\u0648\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0634\u0631\u0648\u0639 \u0625\u0644\u0649 `CrewAI` \u0648\u0642\u0645 \u0628\u062a\u0648\u0644\u064a\u062f \u0645\u0641\u062a\u0627\u062d API.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\nindex 0899dbd9f0..be8b99b672 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n \u0639\u0632\u0651\u0632 \u0639\u0645\u0644\u064a\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0633\u062a\u0631\u062c\u0627\u0639 \u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0630\u0643\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0635\u0637\u0646\u0627\u0639\u064a \u0627\u0644\u062e\u0627\u0635\u0629 \u0628\u0643 \u0628\u0640:\n \n- - [\u0628\u0646\u064a\u0629 \u062a\u062d\u062a\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u062f\u0648\u0646 \u062e\u0627\u062f\u0645](https://docs.browserbase.com/under-the-hood) \u062a\u0648\u0641\u0631 \u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0648\u062b\u0648\u0642\u0629 \u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u0631\u0627\u062c \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0646 \u0648\u0627\u062c\u0647\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629\n- - [\u0648\u0636\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062e\u0641\u064a](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/stealth-mode) \u0645\u0639 \u062a\u0643\u062a\u064a\u0643\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0635\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0636\u0645\u0646\u0629 \u0648\u062d\u0644 CAPTCHA \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a\n- - [\u0645\u0635\u062d\u062d \u0627\u0644\u062c\u0644\u0633\u0627\u062a](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/sessions) \u0644\u0641\u062d\u0635 \u062c\u0644\u0633\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062c\u062f\u0648\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0632\u0645\u0646\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0634\u0628\u0643\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0633\u062c\u0644\u0627\u062a\n- - [\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0635\u062d\u064a\u062d \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0628\u0627\u0634\u0631](https://docs.browserbase.com/guides/session-debug-connection/browser-remote-control) \u0644\u062a\u0635\u062d\u064a\u062d \u0627\u0644\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0628\u0633\u0631\u0639\u0629\n+ - [\u0628\u0646\u064a\u0629 \u062a\u062d\u062a\u064a\u0629 \u0628\u062f\u0648\u0646 \u062e\u0627\u062f\u0645](https://docs.browserbase.com/welcome/what-is-browserbase) \u062a\u0648\u0641\u0631 \u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0648\u062b\u0648\u0642\u0629 \u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u0631\u0627\u062c \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0646 \u0648\u0627\u062c\u0647\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0642\u062f\u0629\n+ - [\u0648\u0636\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062e\u0641\u064a](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/identity/overview) \u0645\u0639 \u062a\u0643\u062a\u064a\u0643\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0628\u0635\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0636\u0645\u0646\u0629 \u0648\u062d\u0644 CAPTCHA \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0644\u0642\u0627\u0626\u064a\n+ - [\u0645\u0635\u062d\u062d \u0627\u0644\u062c\u0644\u0633\u0627\u062a](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/observability) \u0644\u0641\u062d\u0635 \u062c\u0644\u0633\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062c\u062f\u0648\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0632\u0645\u0646\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0634\u0628\u0643\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0633\u062c\u0644\u0627\u062a\n+ - [\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0635\u062d\u064a\u062d \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0628\u0627\u0634\u0631](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/session-live-view) \u0644\u062a\u0635\u062d\u064a\u062d \u0627\u0644\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0628\u0633\u0631\u0639\u0629\n \n ## \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062b\u0628\u064a\u062a\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/langtrace.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/langtrace.mdx\nindex 8257f8eb7a..45f98de996 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/langtrace.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/langtrace.mdx\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ This integration allows you to log hyperparameters, monitor performance regressi\n \n <Steps>\n    <Step title=\"Sign up for Langtrace\">\n-      Sign up by visiting [https://langtrace.ai/signup](https://langtrace.ai/signup).\n+      Sign up by visiting [https://app.langtrace.ai/signup](https://app.langtrace.ai/signup).\n    </Step>\n    <Step title=\"Create a project\">\n       Set the project type to `CrewAI` and generate an API key.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\nindex e53834d4bb..f445a005de 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n Power your AI data retrievals with:\n \n- - [Serverless Infrastructure](https://docs.browserbase.com/under-the-hood) providing reliable browsers to extract data from complex UIs\n- - [Stealth Mode](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/stealth-mode) with included fingerprinting tactics and automatic captcha solving\n- - [Session Debugger](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/sessions) to inspect your Browser Session with networks timeline and logs\n- - [Live Debug](https://docs.browserbase.com/guides/session-debug-connection/browser-remote-control) to quickly debug your automation\n+ - [Serverless Infrastructure](https://docs.browserbase.com/welcome/what-is-browserbase) providing reliable browsers to extract data from complex UIs\n+ - [Stealth Mode](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/identity/overview) with included fingerprinting tactics and automatic captcha solving\n+ - [Session Debugger](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/observability) to inspect your Browser Session with networks timeline and logs\n+ - [Live Debug](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/session-live-view) to quickly debug your automation\n \n ## Installation\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/observability/langtrace.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/observability/langtrace.mdx\nindex 05848d5868..47d9487fad 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/observability/langtrace.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/observability/langtrace.mdx\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ Langtrace\ub294 CrewAI\uc5d0 \uc9c1\uc811 \ub0b4\uc7a5\ub418\uc5b4 \uc788\uc9c0\ub294 \uc54a\uc9c0\ub9cc, CrewAI\uc640 \ud568\uaed8\n \n <Steps>\n    <Step title=\"Langtrace\uc5d0 \uac00\uc785\ud558\uae30\">\n-      [https://langtrace.ai/signup](https://langtrace.ai/signup)\uc5d0\uc11c \uac00\uc785\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n+      [https://app.langtrace.ai/signup](https://app.langtrace.ai/signup)\uc5d0\uc11c \uac00\uc785\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n    </Step>\n    <Step title=\"\ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8 \uc0dd\uc131\">\n       \ud504\ub85c\uc81d\ud2b8 \uc720\ud615\uc744 `CrewAI`\ub85c \uc124\uc815\ud558\uace0 API \ud0a4\ub97c \uc0dd\uc131\ud558\uc138\uc694.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\nindex a2fdfecd36..8135b81f9b 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n AI \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc218\uc9d1\uc744 \ub2e4\uc74c\uacfc \uac19\uc774 \uac15\ud654\ud558\uc138\uc694:\n \n- - [\uc11c\ubc84\ub9ac\uc2a4 \uc778\ud504\ub77c\uc2a4\ud2b8\ub7ed\ucc98](https://docs.browserbase.com/under-the-hood)\ub97c \ud1b5\ud574 \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c UI\uc5d0\uc11c \ub370\uc774\ud130\ub97c \ucd94\ucd9c\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \uc2e0\ub8b0\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \ube0c\ub77c\uc6b0\uc800 \uc81c\uacf5\n- - [\uc2a4\ud154\uc2a4 \ubaa8\ub4dc](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/stealth-mode)\uc5d0\uc11c\ub294 \uc9c0\ubb38 \uc778\uc2dd \ud68c\ud53c \uae30\ubc95\uacfc \uc790\ub3d9 \ucea1\ucc28 \uc194\ub8e8\uc158\uc774 \ud3ec\ud568\ub418\uc5b4 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4\n- - [\uc138\uc158 \ub514\ubc84\uac70](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/sessions)\ub97c \ud1b5\ud574 \ub124\ud2b8\uc6cc\ud06c \ud0c0\uc784\ub77c\uc778\uacfc \ub85c\uadf8\ub85c Browser Session\uc744 \uc810\uac80\n- - [\ub77c\uc774\ube0c \ub514\ubc84\uadf8](https://docs.browserbase.com/guides/session-debug-connection/browser-remote-control)\ub85c \uc790\ub3d9\ud654 \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \uc2e0\uc18d\ud558\uac8c \ub514\ubc84\uae45\n+ - [\uc11c\ubc84\ub9ac\uc2a4 \uc778\ud504\ub77c\uc2a4\ud2b8\ub7ed\ucc98](https://docs.browserbase.com/welcome/what-is-browserbase)\ub97c \ud1b5\ud574 \ubcf5\uc7a1\ud55c UI\uc5d0\uc11c \ub370\uc774\ud130\ub97c \ucd94\ucd9c\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \uc2e0\ub8b0\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub294 \ube0c\ub77c\uc6b0\uc800 \uc81c\uacf5\n+ - [\uc2a4\ud154\uc2a4 \ubaa8\ub4dc](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/identity/overview)\uc5d0\uc11c\ub294 \uc9c0\ubb38 \uc778\uc2dd \ud68c\ud53c \uae30\ubc95\uacfc \uc790\ub3d9 \ucea1\ucc28 \uc194\ub8e8\uc158\uc774 \ud3ec\ud568\ub418\uc5b4 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4\n+ - [\uc138\uc158 \ub514\ubc84\uac70](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/observability)\ub97c \ud1b5\ud574 \ub124\ud2b8\uc6cc\ud06c \ud0c0\uc784\ub77c\uc778\uacfc \ub85c\uadf8\ub85c Browser Session\uc744 \uc810\uac80\n+ - [\ub77c\uc774\ube0c \ub514\ubc84\uadf8](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/session-live-view)\ub85c \uc790\ub3d9\ud654 \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \uc2e0\uc18d\ud558\uac8c \ub514\ubc84\uae45\n \n ## \uc124\uce58\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/observability/langtrace.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/observability/langtrace.mdx\nindex 470c429338..2f0965ff7d 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/observability/langtrace.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/observability/langtrace.mdx\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ Essa integra\u00e7\u00e3o permite o registro de hiperpar\u00e2metros, o monitoramento de reg\n \n <Steps>\n    <Step title=\"Crie uma conta no Langtrace\">\n-      Cadastre-se acessando [https://langtrace.ai/signup](https://langtrace.ai/signup).\n+      Cadastre-se acessando [https://app.langtrace.ai/signup](https://app.langtrace.ai/signup).\n    </Step>\n    <Step title=\"Crie um projeto\">\n       Defina o tipo do projeto como `CrewAI` e gere uma chave de API.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\nindex ef18a46475..7c8dce46f1 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx\n@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n Potencialize suas buscas de dados para IA com:\n \n- - [Infraestrutura Serverless](https://docs.browserbase.com/under-the-hood) fornecendo navegadores confi\u00e1veis para extrair dados de interfaces complexas\n- - [Modo Stealth](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/stealth-mode) com t\u00e1ticas de fingerprinting e resolu\u00e7\u00e3o autom\u00e1tica de captcha inclu\u00eddas\n- - [Depurador de Sess\u00e3o](https://docs.browserbase.com/features/sessions) para inspecionar sua Sess\u00e3o do Navegador com linha do tempo de rede e logs\n- - [Depura\u00e7\u00e3o Ao Vivo](https://docs.browserbase.com/guides/session-debug-connection/browser-remote-control) para depurar rapidamente sua automa\u00e7\u00e3o\n+ - [Infraestrutura Serverless](https://docs.browserbase.com/welcome/what-is-browserbase) fornecendo navegadores confi\u00e1veis para extrair dados de interfaces complexas\n+ - [Modo Stealth](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/identity/overview) com t\u00e1ticas de fingerprinting e resolu\u00e7\u00e3o autom\u00e1tica de captcha inclu\u00eddas\n+ - [Depurador de Sess\u00e3o](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/observability) para inspecionar sua Sess\u00e3o do Navegador com linha do tempo de rede e logs\n+ - [Depura\u00e7\u00e3o Ao Vivo](https://docs.browserbase.com/platform/browser/observability/session-live-view) para depurar rapidamente sua automa\u00e7\u00e3o\n \n ## Instala\u00e7\u00e3o\n \n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "Dead and outdated links in browserbase load tool and langtrace guides\n## Description\n\nWhile auditing external links in the docs, I found broken/outdated links in two guides:\n\n### 1. `browserbaseloadtool.mdx` \u2014 Browserbase docs site restructured\n\nThe Browserbase documentation site has been restructured, and the links in the **Browserbase Load Tool** guide no longer point to the right pages:\n\n- `https://docs.browserbase.com/under-the-hood` \u2192 308 redirects to `/welcome/what-is-browserbase`\n- `https://docs.browserbase.com/features/stealth-mode` \u2192 308 redirects to `/platform/identity/overview`\n- `https://docs.browserbase.com/features/sessions` \u2192 308 redirects to `/platform/browser/core-features/session-metadata`, which is about tagging/querying sessions, **not** about the Session Debugger (network timeline and logs)\n- `https://docs.browserbase.com/guides/session-debug-connection/browser-remote-control` (Live Debug) \u2192 redirects to the unrelated session-metadata page; the Live Debug / browser remote control feature now lives at `/platform/browser/observability/session-live-view` (\"An interactive window to display or control a browser session\")\n\nEspecially the last two: readers looking for the **Session Debugger** or **Live Debug** land on a page about session metadata tags, so the links are effectively broken.\n\n### 2. `langtrace.mdx` \u2014 main site is down\n\n`https://langtrace.ai/signup` returns 404 (the whole `langtrace.ai` apex/www site is currently down). The signup page is still reachable at `https://app.langtrace.ai/signup` (the app subdomain is alive; `docs.langtrace.ai` also still works).\n\n## Affected files\n\nBoth `docs/edge` and `docs/v1.15.28` across `en`, `ko`, `pt-BR`, `ar`:\n\n- `docs/<version>/<lang>/tools/web-scraping/browserbaseloadtool.mdx`\n- `docs/<version>/<lang>/observability/langtrace.mdx`\n\nHappy to open a PR with the fixes.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-21T09:42:07Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8356, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8356", "issue_numbers": ["8355"], "base_commit": "5c154cd701fbe83ca2fe506849daed04c7d4c598", "patch": "diff --git a/docs/edge/ar/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx b/docs/edge/ar/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\nindex a900e78d31..9a055f63ab 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ar/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ar/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ print(result)\n   - **connection_data**: \u0642\u0627\u0645\u0648\u0633 \u064a\u062d\u062a\u0648\u064a \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0645\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0627\u062a\u0635\u0627\u0644 \u0644\u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a.\n   - **tables**: \u0642\u0627\u0626\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062c\u062f\u0627\u0648\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u0633\u064a\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645\u0647\u0627 \u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a. \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u062e\u062a\u064a\u0627\u0631\u064a \u0648\u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u062d\u0630\u0641\u0647 \u0625\u0630\u0627 \u0643\u0627\u0646\u062a \u062c\u0645\u064a\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062c\u062f\u0627\u0648\u0644 \u0641\u064a \u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0637\u0644\u0648\u0628\u0629.\n \n-\u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u062b\u0648\u0631 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0642\u0627\u0626\u0645\u0629 \u0645\u0635\u0627\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062f\u0639\u0648\u0645\u0629 \u0648\u0645\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u062a\u0635\u0627\u0644\u0647\u0627 [\u0647\u0646\u0627](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/data_sources).\n+\u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u062b\u0648\u0631 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0642\u0627\u0626\u0645\u0629 \u0645\u0635\u0627\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062f\u0639\u0648\u0645\u0629 \u0648\u0645\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u062a\u0635\u0627\u0644\u0647\u0627 [\u0647\u0646\u0627](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/anton_onboarding#connect-data-sources).\n \n ## \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0648\u0643\u064a\u0644\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ar/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx b/docs/edge/ar/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\nindex 3b5eb1aed7..19c27e53d3 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ar/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ar/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n@@ -137,4 +137,4 @@ extractor_tool = TavilyExtractorTool(\n - **\u0627\u0644\u0645\u0631\u0627\u0642\u0628\u0629**: \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u0631\u0627\u062c \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0646\u062a\u0638\u0645 \u0644\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0648\u0649 \u0644\u0627\u0643\u062a\u0634\u0627\u0641 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u063a\u064a\u064a\u0631\u0627\u062a\n - **\u062c\u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a**: \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u0631\u0627\u062c \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0646\u0647\u062c\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0644\u0648\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0646 \u0645\u0635\u0627\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0648\u064a\u0628\n \n-\u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639 [\u062a\u0648\u062b\u064a\u0642 Tavily API](https://docs.tavily.com/docs/tavily-api/python-sdk#extract) \u0644\u0644\u062d\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0645\u0639\u0644\u0648\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0641\u0635\u0644\u0629 \u062d\u0648\u0644 \u0647\u064a\u0643\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062c\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062e\u064a\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0627\u062d\u0629.\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+\u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639 [\u062a\u0648\u062b\u064a\u0642 Tavily API](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference#tavily-extract) \u0644\u0644\u062d\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0645\u0639\u0644\u0648\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0641\u0635\u0644\u0629 \u062d\u0648\u0644 \u0647\u064a\u0643\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062c\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062e\u064a\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0627\u062d\u0629.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ar/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx b/docs/edge/ar/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\nindex 338cc71051..87c96cdf69 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ar/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ar/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # \u0646\u0638\u0631\u0629 \u0639\u0627\u0645\u0629\n \n-\u062a\u062f\u0645\u062c \u0623\u062f\u0627\u0629 `StagehandTool` \u0625\u0637\u0627\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644 [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/get_started/introduction) \u0645\u0639 CrewAI\u060c \u0645\u0645\u0627 \u064a\u062a\u064a\u062d \u0644\u0644\u0648\u0643\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0641\u0627\u0639\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0648\u0627\u0642\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u062a\u0639\u0644\u064a\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0628\u0644\u063a\u0629 \u0637\u0628\u064a\u0639\u064a\u0629.\n+\u062a\u062f\u0645\u062c \u0623\u062f\u0627\u0629 `StagehandTool` \u0625\u0637\u0627\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644 [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/v4/first-steps/introduction) \u0645\u0639 CrewAI\u060c \u0645\u0645\u0627 \u064a\u062a\u064a\u062d \u0644\u0644\u0648\u0643\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0641\u0627\u0639\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0648\u0627\u0642\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u062a\u0639\u0644\u064a\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0628\u0644\u063a\u0629 \u0637\u0628\u064a\u0639\u064a\u0629.\n \n ## \u0646\u0638\u0631\u0629 \u0639\u0627\u0645\u0629\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/en/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx b/docs/edge/en/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\nindex 50c640a9d3..439ae46a16 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ The `AIMindTool` accepts the following parameters:\n   - **connection_data**: A dictionary containing the connection parameters for the datasource.\n   - **tables**: A list of tables that the data source will use. This is optional and can be omitted if all tables in the data source are to be used.\n \n-A list of supported data sources and their connection parameters can be found [here](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/data_sources).\n+A list of supported data sources and their connection parameters can be found [here](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/anton_onboarding#connect-data-sources).\n \n ## Agent Integration Example\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/en/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx b/docs/edge/en/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\nindex 1530d54a9a..045403468c 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n@@ -137,4 +137,4 @@ Common response elements include:\n - **Monitoring**: Regular extraction of content for change detection\n - **Data Collection**: Systematic extraction of information from web sources\n \n-Refer to the [Tavily API documentation](https://docs.tavily.com/docs/tavily-api/python-sdk#extract) for detailed information about the response structure and available options.\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+Refer to the [Tavily API documentation](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference#tavily-extract) for detailed information about the response structure and available options.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/en/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx b/docs/edge/en/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\nindex 442be59cbd..c616983775 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # Overview\n \n-The `StagehandTool` integrates the [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/get_started/introduction) framework with CrewAI, enabling agents to interact with websites and automate browser tasks using natural language instructions.\n+The `StagehandTool` integrates the [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/v4/first-steps/introduction) framework with CrewAI, enabling agents to interact with websites and automate browser tasks using natural language instructions.\n \n ## Overview\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\nindex 4f93af6565..2098922866 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ print(result)\n   - **connection_data**: \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc758 \uc5f0\uacb0 \ub9e4\uac1c\ubcc0\uc218\ub97c \ud3ec\ud568\ud558\ub294 \uc0ac\uc804\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n   - **tables**: \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc5d0\uc11c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud560 \ud14c\uc774\ube14 \ubaa9\ub85d\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc774 \ud56d\ubaa9\uc740 \uc120\ud0dd \uc0ac\ud56d\uc774\uba70, \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc758 \ubaa8\ub4e0 \ud14c\uc774\ube14\uc744 \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud560 \uacbd\uc6b0 \uc0dd\ub7b5\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \n-\uc9c0\uc6d0\ub418\ub294 \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc640 \uadf8 \uc5f0\uacb0 \ub9e4\uac1c\ubcc0\uc218 \ubaa9\ub85d\uc740 [\uc5ec\uae30](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/data_sources)\uc5d0\uc11c \ud655\uc778\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n+\uc9c0\uc6d0\ub418\ub294 \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc640 \uadf8 \uc5f0\uacb0 \ub9e4\uac1c\ubcc0\uc218 \ubaa9\ub85d\uc740 [\uc5ec\uae30](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/anton_onboarding#connect-data-sources)\uc5d0\uc11c \ud655\uc778\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \n ## \uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8 \ud1b5\ud569 \uc608\uc2dc\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\nindex 21211e9fde..a7de0b0330 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n@@ -137,4 +137,4 @@ extractor_tool = TavilyExtractorTool(\n - **\ubaa8\ub2c8\ud130\ub9c1**: \ubcc0\uacbd \uac10\uc9c0\ub97c \uc704\ud574 \uc815\uae30\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \ucf58\ud150\uce20 \ucd94\ucd9c\n - **\ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc218\uc9d1**: \uc6f9 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc5d0\uc11c \uc815\ubcf4\ub97c \uccb4\uacc4\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \ucd94\ucd9c\n \n-\uc751\ub2f5 \uad6c\uc870\uc640 \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uac00\ub2a5\ud55c \uc635\uc158\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \uc790\uc138\ud55c \uc815\ubcf4\ub294 [Tavily API \ubb38\uc11c](https://docs.tavily.com/docs/tavily-api/python-sdk#extract)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+\uc751\ub2f5 \uad6c\uc870\uc640 \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uac00\ub2a5\ud55c \uc635\uc158\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \uc790\uc138\ud55c \uc815\ubcf4\ub294 [Tavily API \ubb38\uc11c](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference#tavily-extract)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\nindex 2a7069e607..878bd7c19f 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # \uac1c\uc694\n \n-`StagehandTool`\uc740 [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/get_started/introduction) \ud504\ub808\uc784\uc6cc\ud06c\ub97c CrewAI\uc640 \ud1b5\ud569\ud558\uc5ec \uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8\uac00 \uc790\uc5f0\uc5b4 \uc9c0\uc2dc\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud574 \uc6f9\uc0ac\uc774\ud2b8\uc640 \uc0c1\ud638\uc791\uc6a9\ud558\uace0 \ube0c\ub77c\uc6b0\uc800 \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub3c4\ub85d \ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n+`StagehandTool`\uc740 [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/v4/first-steps/introduction) \ud504\ub808\uc784\uc6cc\ud06c\ub97c CrewAI\uc640 \ud1b5\ud569\ud558\uc5ec \uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8\uac00 \uc790\uc5f0\uc5b4 \uc9c0\uc2dc\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud574 \uc6f9\uc0ac\uc774\ud2b8\uc640 \uc0c1\ud638\uc791\uc6a9\ud558\uace0 \ube0c\ub77c\uc6b0\uc800 \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub3c4\ub85d \ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \n ## \uac1c\uc694\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\nindex 2ced339548..4c9cfb5abe 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ O `AIMindTool` aceita os seguintes par\u00e2metros:\n   - **connection_data**: Um dicion\u00e1rio contendo os par\u00e2metros de conex\u00e3o da fonte de dados.\n   - **tables**: Uma lista de tabelas que a fonte de dados ir\u00e1 utilizar. Isso \u00e9 opcional e pode ser omitido caso todas as tabelas da fonte de dados devam ser utilizadas.\n \n-Uma lista das fontes de dados suportadas e seus par\u00e2metros de conex\u00e3o pode ser encontrada [aqui](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/data_sources).\n+Uma lista das fontes de dados suportadas e seus par\u00e2metros de conex\u00e3o pode ser encontrada [aqui](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/anton_onboarding#connect-data-sources).\n \n ## Exemplo de Integra\u00e7\u00e3o com Agente\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\nindex 55030845cf..a8a65b55b4 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n@@ -137,4 +137,4 @@ Common response elements include:\n - **Monitoring**: Regular extraction of content for change detection\n - **Data Collection**: Systematic extraction of information from web sources\n \n-Refer to the [Tavily API documentation](https://docs.tavily.com/docs/tavily-api/python-sdk#extract) for detailed information about the response structure and available options.\n+Refer to the [Tavily API documentation](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference#tavily-extract) for detailed information about the response structure and available options.\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\nindex 724a853607..9fc2801e69 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # Vis\u00e3o Geral\n \n-A `StagehandTool` integra o framework [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/get_started/introduction) com o CrewAI, permitindo que agentes interajam com sites e automatizem tarefas no navegador utilizando instru\u00e7\u00f5es em linguagem natural.\n+A `StagehandTool` integra o framework [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/v4/first-steps/introduction) com o CrewAI, permitindo que agentes interajam com sites e automatizem tarefas no navegador utilizando instru\u00e7\u00f5es em linguagem natural.\n \n ## Vis\u00e3o Geral\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\nindex a900e78d31..9a055f63ab 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ print(result)\n   - **connection_data**: \u0642\u0627\u0645\u0648\u0633 \u064a\u062d\u062a\u0648\u064a \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0645\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0627\u062a\u0635\u0627\u0644 \u0644\u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a.\n   - **tables**: \u0642\u0627\u0626\u0645\u0629 \u0627\u0644\u062c\u062f\u0627\u0648\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u064a \u0633\u064a\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0645\u0647\u0627 \u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a. \u0647\u0630\u0627 \u0627\u062e\u062a\u064a\u0627\u0631\u064a \u0648\u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u062d\u0630\u0641\u0647 \u0625\u0630\u0627 \u0643\u0627\u0646\u062a \u062c\u0645\u064a\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u062c\u062f\u0627\u0648\u0644 \u0641\u064a \u0645\u0635\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0637\u0644\u0648\u0628\u0629.\n \n-\u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u062b\u0648\u0631 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0642\u0627\u0626\u0645\u0629 \u0645\u0635\u0627\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062f\u0639\u0648\u0645\u0629 \u0648\u0645\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u062a\u0635\u0627\u0644\u0647\u0627 [\u0647\u0646\u0627](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/data_sources).\n+\u064a\u0645\u0643\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0639\u062b\u0648\u0631 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0642\u0627\u0626\u0645\u0629 \u0645\u0635\u0627\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062f\u0639\u0648\u0645\u0629 \u0648\u0645\u0639\u0627\u0645\u0644\u0627\u062a \u0627\u062a\u0635\u0627\u0644\u0647\u0627 [\u0647\u0646\u0627](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/anton_onboarding#connect-data-sources).\n \n ## \u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0643\u0627\u0645\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0648\u0643\u064a\u0644\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\nindex 3b5eb1aed7..19c27e53d3 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n@@ -137,4 +137,4 @@ extractor_tool = TavilyExtractorTool(\n - **\u0627\u0644\u0645\u0631\u0627\u0642\u0628\u0629**: \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u0631\u0627\u062c \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0646\u062a\u0638\u0645 \u0644\u0644\u0645\u062d\u062a\u0648\u0649 \u0644\u0627\u0643\u062a\u0634\u0627\u0641 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u063a\u064a\u064a\u0631\u0627\u062a\n - **\u062c\u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u064a\u0627\u0646\u0627\u062a**: \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u0631\u0627\u062c \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0646\u0647\u062c\u064a \u0644\u0644\u0645\u0639\u0644\u0648\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0646 \u0645\u0635\u0627\u062f\u0631 \u0627\u0644\u0648\u064a\u0628\n \n-\u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639 [\u062a\u0648\u062b\u064a\u0642 Tavily API](https://docs.tavily.com/docs/tavily-api/python-sdk#extract) \u0644\u0644\u062d\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0645\u0639\u0644\u0648\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0641\u0635\u0644\u0629 \u062d\u0648\u0644 \u0647\u064a\u0643\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062c\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062e\u064a\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0627\u062d\u0629.\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+\u0631\u0627\u062c\u0639 [\u062a\u0648\u062b\u064a\u0642 Tavily API](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference#tavily-extract) \u0644\u0644\u062d\u0635\u0648\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u0649 \u0645\u0639\u0644\u0648\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0645\u0641\u0635\u0644\u0629 \u062d\u0648\u0644 \u0647\u064a\u0643\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062c\u0627\u0628\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062e\u064a\u0627\u0631\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0627\u062d\u0629.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\nindex 338cc71051..87c96cdf69 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ar/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # \u0646\u0638\u0631\u0629 \u0639\u0627\u0645\u0629\n \n-\u062a\u062f\u0645\u062c \u0623\u062f\u0627\u0629 `StagehandTool` \u0625\u0637\u0627\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644 [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/get_started/introduction) \u0645\u0639 CrewAI\u060c \u0645\u0645\u0627 \u064a\u062a\u064a\u062d \u0644\u0644\u0648\u0643\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0641\u0627\u0639\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0648\u0627\u0642\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u062a\u0639\u0644\u064a\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0628\u0644\u063a\u0629 \u0637\u0628\u064a\u0639\u064a\u0629.\n+\u062a\u062f\u0645\u062c \u0623\u062f\u0627\u0629 `StagehandTool` \u0625\u0637\u0627\u0631 \u0639\u0645\u0644 [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/v4/first-steps/introduction) \u0645\u0639 CrewAI\u060c \u0645\u0645\u0627 \u064a\u062a\u064a\u062d \u0644\u0644\u0648\u0643\u0644\u0627\u0621 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u0641\u0627\u0639\u0644 \u0645\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0648\u0627\u0642\u0639 \u0627\u0644\u0625\u0644\u0643\u062a\u0631\u0648\u0646\u064a\u0629 \u0648\u0623\u062a\u0645\u062a\u0629 \u0645\u0647\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u062a\u0635\u0641\u062d \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u062a\u0639\u0644\u064a\u0645\u0627\u062a \u0628\u0644\u063a\u0629 \u0637\u0628\u064a\u0639\u064a\u0629.\n \n ## \u0646\u0638\u0631\u0629 \u0639\u0627\u0645\u0629\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\nindex 50c640a9d3..439ae46a16 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ The `AIMindTool` accepts the following parameters:\n   - **connection_data**: A dictionary containing the connection parameters for the datasource.\n   - **tables**: A list of tables that the data source will use. This is optional and can be omitted if all tables in the data source are to be used.\n \n-A list of supported data sources and their connection parameters can be found [here](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/data_sources).\n+A list of supported data sources and their connection parameters can be found [here](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/anton_onboarding#connect-data-sources).\n \n ## Agent Integration Example\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\nindex 1530d54a9a..045403468c 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n@@ -137,4 +137,4 @@ Common response elements include:\n - **Monitoring**: Regular extraction of content for change detection\n - **Data Collection**: Systematic extraction of information from web sources\n \n-Refer to the [Tavily API documentation](https://docs.tavily.com/docs/tavily-api/python-sdk#extract) for detailed information about the response structure and available options.\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+Refer to the [Tavily API documentation](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference#tavily-extract) for detailed information about the response structure and available options.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\nindex 442be59cbd..c616983775 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # Overview\n \n-The `StagehandTool` integrates the [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/get_started/introduction) framework with CrewAI, enabling agents to interact with websites and automate browser tasks using natural language instructions.\n+The `StagehandTool` integrates the [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/v4/first-steps/introduction) framework with CrewAI, enabling agents to interact with websites and automate browser tasks using natural language instructions.\n \n ## Overview\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\nindex 4f93af6565..2098922866 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ print(result)\n   - **connection_data**: \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc758 \uc5f0\uacb0 \ub9e4\uac1c\ubcc0\uc218\ub97c \ud3ec\ud568\ud558\ub294 \uc0ac\uc804\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n   - **tables**: \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc5d0\uc11c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud560 \ud14c\uc774\ube14 \ubaa9\ub85d\uc785\ub2c8\ub2e4. \uc774 \ud56d\ubaa9\uc740 \uc120\ud0dd \uc0ac\ud56d\uc774\uba70, \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc758 \ubaa8\ub4e0 \ud14c\uc774\ube14\uc744 \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud560 \uacbd\uc6b0 \uc0dd\ub7b5\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \n-\uc9c0\uc6d0\ub418\ub294 \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc640 \uadf8 \uc5f0\uacb0 \ub9e4\uac1c\ubcc0\uc218 \ubaa9\ub85d\uc740 [\uc5ec\uae30](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/data_sources)\uc5d0\uc11c \ud655\uc778\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n+\uc9c0\uc6d0\ub418\ub294 \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc640 \uadf8 \uc5f0\uacb0 \ub9e4\uac1c\ubcc0\uc218 \ubaa9\ub85d\uc740 [\uc5ec\uae30](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/anton_onboarding#connect-data-sources)\uc5d0\uc11c \ud655\uc778\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\uc2b5\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \n ## \uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8 \ud1b5\ud569 \uc608\uc2dc\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\nindex 21211e9fde..a7de0b0330 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n@@ -137,4 +137,4 @@ extractor_tool = TavilyExtractorTool(\n - **\ubaa8\ub2c8\ud130\ub9c1**: \ubcc0\uacbd \uac10\uc9c0\ub97c \uc704\ud574 \uc815\uae30\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \ucf58\ud150\uce20 \ucd94\ucd9c\n - **\ub370\uc774\ud130 \uc218\uc9d1**: \uc6f9 \uc18c\uc2a4\uc5d0\uc11c \uc815\ubcf4\ub97c \uccb4\uacc4\uc801\uc73c\ub85c \ucd94\ucd9c\n \n-\uc751\ub2f5 \uad6c\uc870\uc640 \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uac00\ub2a5\ud55c \uc635\uc158\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \uc790\uc138\ud55c \uc815\ubcf4\ub294 [Tavily API \ubb38\uc11c](https://docs.tavily.com/docs/tavily-api/python-sdk#extract)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+\uc751\ub2f5 \uad6c\uc870\uc640 \uc0ac\uc6a9 \uac00\ub2a5\ud55c \uc635\uc158\uc5d0 \ub300\ud55c \uc790\uc138\ud55c \uc815\ubcf4\ub294 [Tavily API \ubb38\uc11c](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference#tavily-extract)\ub97c \ucc38\uace0\ud558\uc138\uc694.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\nindex 2a7069e607..878bd7c19f 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # \uac1c\uc694\n \n-`StagehandTool`\uc740 [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/get_started/introduction) \ud504\ub808\uc784\uc6cc\ud06c\ub97c CrewAI\uc640 \ud1b5\ud569\ud558\uc5ec \uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8\uac00 \uc790\uc5f0\uc5b4 \uc9c0\uc2dc\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud574 \uc6f9\uc0ac\uc774\ud2b8\uc640 \uc0c1\ud638\uc791\uc6a9\ud558\uace0 \ube0c\ub77c\uc6b0\uc800 \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub3c4\ub85d \ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n+`StagehandTool`\uc740 [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/v4/first-steps/introduction) \ud504\ub808\uc784\uc6cc\ud06c\ub97c CrewAI\uc640 \ud1b5\ud569\ud558\uc5ec \uc5d0\uc774\uc804\ud2b8\uac00 \uc790\uc5f0\uc5b4 \uc9c0\uc2dc\ub97c \uc0ac\uc6a9\ud574 \uc6f9\uc0ac\uc774\ud2b8\uc640 \uc0c1\ud638\uc791\uc6a9\ud558\uace0 \ube0c\ub77c\uc6b0\uc800 \uc791\uc5c5\uc744 \uc790\ub3d9\ud654\ud560 \uc218 \uc788\ub3c4\ub85d \ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \n ## \uac1c\uc694\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\nindex 2ced339548..4c9cfb5abe 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/ai-ml/aimindtool.mdx\n@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ O `AIMindTool` aceita os seguintes par\u00e2metros:\n   - **connection_data**: Um dicion\u00e1rio contendo os par\u00e2metros de conex\u00e3o da fonte de dados.\n   - **tables**: Uma lista de tabelas que a fonte de dados ir\u00e1 utilizar. Isso \u00e9 opcional e pode ser omitido caso todas as tabelas da fonte de dados devam ser utilizadas.\n \n-Uma lista das fontes de dados suportadas e seus par\u00e2metros de conex\u00e3o pode ser encontrada [aqui](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/data_sources).\n+Uma lista das fontes de dados suportadas e seus par\u00e2metros de conex\u00e3o pode ser encontrada [aqui](https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/anton_onboarding#connect-data-sources).\n \n ## Exemplo de Integra\u00e7\u00e3o com Agente\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\nindex 55030845cf..a8a65b55b4 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/search-research/tavilyextractortool.mdx\n@@ -137,4 +137,4 @@ Common response elements include:\n - **Monitoring**: Regular extraction of content for change detection\n - **Data Collection**: Systematic extraction of information from web sources\n \n-Refer to the [Tavily API documentation](https://docs.tavily.com/docs/tavily-api/python-sdk#extract) for detailed information about the response structure and available options.\n+Refer to the [Tavily API documentation](https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference#tavily-extract) for detailed information about the response structure and available options.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\nindex 724a853607..9fc2801e69 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/tools/web-scraping/stagehandtool.mdx\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # Vis\u00e3o Geral\n \n-A `StagehandTool` integra o framework [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/get_started/introduction) com o CrewAI, permitindo que agentes interajam com sites e automatizem tarefas no navegador utilizando instru\u00e7\u00f5es em linguagem natural.\n+A `StagehandTool` integra o framework [Stagehand](https://docs.stagehand.dev/v4/first-steps/introduction) com o CrewAI, permitindo que agentes interajam com sites e automatizem tarefas no navegador utilizando instru\u00e7\u00f5es em linguagem natural.\n \n ## Vis\u00e3o Geral\n \n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "Docs: dead external links in Stagehand / Tavily Extract / AI Mind tool guides\n## Problem\n\nThree tool guides link to external documentation URLs that now return 404:\n\n| Guide | Dead link | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `stagehandtool.mdx` | https://docs.stagehand.dev/get_started/introduction | 404 - docs restructured to versioned paths (`/v4/first-steps/...`) |\n| `tavilyextractortool.mdx` | https://docs.tavily.com/docs/tavily-api/python-sdk#extract | 404 - docs restructured to `/sdk/python/reference` |\n| `aimindtool.mdx` | https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/data_sources | 404 - docs restructured (data-source setup now covered in onboarding) |\n\nThese links appear in both `docs/edge/` and `docs/v1.15.28/` across the `en`, `ko`, `pt-BR` and `ar` locales (24 occurrences in total).\n\n## Verified replacements\n\n- Stagehand intro now lives at https://docs.stagehand.dev/v4/first-steps/introduction (the site root redirects exactly there)\n- Tavily Python SDK reference is https://docs.tavily.com/sdk/python/reference#tavily-extract (anchor `tavily-extract` exists on the page)\n- MDB data-source connection info is at https://docs.mdb.ai/docs/anton_onboarding#connect-data-sources (anchor `connect-data-sources` exists on the page)\n\nI've verified each new URL returns 200 and that the referenced anchors are present in the page HTML. Happy to open a PR with the replacements if that sounds good.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-21T09:03:05Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8348, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8348", "issue_numbers": ["8347"], "base_commit": "a8877f0cdfbca4fc4b95e3ce54aaa69aafca7688", "patch": "diff --git a/docs/edge/en/observability/galileo.mdx b/docs/edge/en/observability/galileo.mdx\nindex 241517ed22..4eb3325afe 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/observability/galileo.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/observability/galileo.mdx\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ how-to guide.\n \n > **Note** This tutorial assumes you have completed the [CrewAI quickstart](/en/quickstart).\n If you want a completed comprehensive example, see the Galileo\n-[CrewAI sdk-example repo](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crew-ai).\n+[CrewAI sdk-example repo](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crewAI).\n \n ### Step 1: Install dependencies\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/ko/observability/galileo.mdx b/docs/edge/ko/observability/galileo.mdx\nindex f82b825740..82d61737c4 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/ko/observability/galileo.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/ko/observability/galileo.mdx\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ AI \uc218\uba85\uc8fc\uae30 \uc804\ubc18\uc5d0 \uac78\uccd0 \ud22c\uba85\uc131\uacfc \uc9c0\uc18d\uc801\uc778 \uac1c\uc120\uc744 \uc81c\uacf5\ud569\n \n > **\ucc38\uace0**\uc774 \ud29c\ud1a0\ub9ac\uc5bc\uc5d0\uc11c\ub294 [CrewAI \ube60\ub978 \uc2dc\uc791](/ko/quickstart.mdx)\uc744 \uc644\ub8cc\ud588\ub2e4\uace0 \uac00\uc815\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \uc644\uc804\ud55c \ud3ec\uad04\uc801\uc778 \uc608\uc81c\ub97c \uc6d0\ud55c\ub2e4\uba74 Galileo\n-[CrewAI SDK \uc608\uc81c \uc800\uc7a5\uc18c](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crew-ai).\n+[CrewAI SDK \uc608\uc81c \uc800\uc7a5\uc18c](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crewAI).\n \n ### 1\ub2e8\uacc4: \uc885\uc18d\uc131 \uc124\uce58\n \ndiff --git a/docs/edge/pt-BR/observability/galileo.mdx b/docs/edge/pt-BR/observability/galileo.mdx\nindex 4296e35fb9..008d9d991a 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/pt-BR/observability/galileo.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/pt-BR/observability/galileo.mdx\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ guia pr\u00e1tico.\n \n > **Observa\u00e7\u00e3o**Este tutorial pressup\u00f5e que voc\u00ea concluiu o [CrewAI Quickstart](pt-BR/quickstart).\n Se voc\u00ea quiser um exemplo completo e abrangente, consulte o Galileo\n-[Reposit\u00f3rio de exemplo SDK da CrewAI](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crew-ai).\n+[Reposit\u00f3rio de exemplo SDK da CrewAI](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crewAI).\n \n ### Etapa 1: instalar depend\u00eancias\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/galileo.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/galileo.mdx\nindex 241517ed22..4eb3325afe 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/galileo.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/galileo.mdx\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ how-to guide.\n \n > **Note** This tutorial assumes you have completed the [CrewAI quickstart](/en/quickstart).\n If you want a completed comprehensive example, see the Galileo\n-[CrewAI sdk-example repo](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crew-ai).\n+[CrewAI sdk-example repo](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crewAI).\n \n ### Step 1: Install dependencies\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/observability/galileo.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/observability/galileo.mdx\nindex f82b825740..82d61737c4 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/ko/observability/galileo.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/ko/observability/galileo.mdx\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ AI \uc218\uba85\uc8fc\uae30 \uc804\ubc18\uc5d0 \uac78\uccd0 \ud22c\uba85\uc131\uacfc \uc9c0\uc18d\uc801\uc778 \uac1c\uc120\uc744 \uc81c\uacf5\ud569\n \n > **\ucc38\uace0**\uc774 \ud29c\ud1a0\ub9ac\uc5bc\uc5d0\uc11c\ub294 [CrewAI \ube60\ub978 \uc2dc\uc791](/ko/quickstart.mdx)\uc744 \uc644\ub8cc\ud588\ub2e4\uace0 \uac00\uc815\ud569\ub2c8\ub2e4.\n \uc644\uc804\ud55c \ud3ec\uad04\uc801\uc778 \uc608\uc81c\ub97c \uc6d0\ud55c\ub2e4\uba74 Galileo\n-[CrewAI SDK \uc608\uc81c \uc800\uc7a5\uc18c](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crew-ai).\n+[CrewAI SDK \uc608\uc81c \uc800\uc7a5\uc18c](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crewAI).\n \n ### 1\ub2e8\uacc4: \uc885\uc18d\uc131 \uc124\uce58\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/observability/galileo.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/observability/galileo.mdx\nindex 4296e35fb9..008d9d991a 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/observability/galileo.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/pt-BR/observability/galileo.mdx\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ guia pr\u00e1tico.\n \n > **Observa\u00e7\u00e3o**Este tutorial pressup\u00f5e que voc\u00ea concluiu o [CrewAI Quickstart](pt-BR/quickstart).\n Se voc\u00ea quiser um exemplo completo e abrangente, consulte o Galileo\n-[Reposit\u00f3rio de exemplo SDK da CrewAI](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crew-ai).\n+[Reposit\u00f3rio de exemplo SDK da CrewAI](https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crewAI).\n \n ### Etapa 1: instalar depend\u00eancias\n \n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "Dead repo link in observability guide (galileo.mdx)\n## What\n\nThe Galileo observability guide links to a directory that no longer exists in the `rungalileo/sdk-examples` repo:\n\n- `docs/edge/{en,ko,pt-BR}/observability/galileo.mdx` and `docs/v1.15.28/{en,ko,pt-BR}/observability/galileo.mdx` link to `https://github.com/rungalileo/sdk-examples/tree/main/python/agent/crew-ai`, which returns 404.\n\nThe example directory was renamed from `python/agent/crew-ai` to `python/agent/crewAI` (verified via the repo git tree API: the path now holds the `research_crew` CrewAI example project). The repo itself is alive (pushed 2026-07-08); only the directory casing changed.\n\n## Fix\n\nSix link replacements: `tree/main/python/agent/crew-ai` -> `tree/main/python/agent/crewAI` across the dev source (`docs/edge/`) and the current published version tree (`docs/v1.15.28/`), for all three language editions (en, ko, pt-BR). Older version snapshots left untouched as historical archives.\n\nThis is the same class of fix as #8310 (which updated dead repo links in `braintrust.mdx` / `arize-phoenix.mdx`); the `galileo.mdx` link was not part of that PR.\n\n## AI disclosure\n\nPer CONTRIBUTING.md this issue was prepared with AI assistance (agent-driven link verification); I cannot apply labels here - please add the `llm-generated` label.\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-21T07:30:24Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8310, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8310", "issue_numbers": ["8311"], "base_commit": "4f4573706ea4afee6c4da4c31cfb9622a4495ab7", "patch": "diff --git a/docs/edge/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx b/docs/edge/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx\nindex cdbe5b8224..d92f3cc601 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # Arize Phoenix Integration\n \n-This guide demonstrates how to integrate **Arize Phoenix** with **CrewAI** using OpenTelemetry via the [OpenInference](https://github.com/openinference/openinference) SDK. By the end of this guide, you will be able to trace your CrewAI agents and debug agent behavior.\n+This guide demonstrates how to integrate **Arize Phoenix** with **CrewAI** using OpenTelemetry via the [OpenInference](https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference) SDK. By the end of this guide, you will be able to trace your CrewAI agents and debug agent behavior.\n \n > **What is Arize Phoenix?** [Arize Phoenix](https://arize.com/phoenix/) is the open-source observability and evaluation option from [Arize AI](https://arize.com/?utm_source=crewai-docs&utm_medium=partner&utm_campaign=partner-docs&utm_content=observability-arize-phoenix). Use Phoenix when you want to run locally or self-host. Use [Arize AX](https://arize.com/products/ax/) for a managed cloud or enterprise self-hosted platform for production AI systems.\n \n@@ -152,4 +152,4 @@ Open your Phoenix project and navigate to the project you specified in the `proj\n - [Arize LLM evaluation guide](https://arize.com/resources/llm-evaluation/) - Methods and metrics for evaluating LLM applications.\n - [CrewAI Documentation](https://docs.crewai.com/) - Overview of the CrewAI framework.\n - [OpenTelemetry Docs](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/) - OpenTelemetry guide\n-- [OpenInference GitHub](https://github.com/openinference/openinference) - Source code for OpenInference SDK.\n+- [OpenInference GitHub](https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference) - Source code for OpenInference SDK.\ndiff --git a/docs/edge/en/observability/braintrust.mdx b/docs/edge/en/observability/braintrust.mdx\nindex 21ab52c852..c2ca9c5f31 100644\n--- a/docs/edge/en/observability/braintrust.mdx\n+++ b/docs/edge/en/observability/braintrust.mdx\n@@ -234,4 +234,4 @@ See the [Braintrust Eval SDK guide](https://www.braintrust.dev/docs/start/eval-s\n - [Braintrust Eval SDK](https://www.braintrust.dev/docs/start/eval-sdk) - Run experiments via the SDK\n - [CrewAI Documentation](https://docs.crewai.com/) - Overview of the CrewAI framework\n - [OpenTelemetry Docs](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/) - OpenTelemetry guide\n-- [Braintrust GitHub](https://github.com/braintrustdata/braintrust) - Source code for Braintrust SDK\n+- [Braintrust GitHub](https://github.com/braintrustdata/braintrust-sdk-python) - Source code for Braintrust SDK\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx\nindex cdbe5b8224..d92f3cc601 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ mode: \"wide\"\n \n # Arize Phoenix Integration\n \n-This guide demonstrates how to integrate **Arize Phoenix** with **CrewAI** using OpenTelemetry via the [OpenInference](https://github.com/openinference/openinference) SDK. By the end of this guide, you will be able to trace your CrewAI agents and debug agent behavior.\n+This guide demonstrates how to integrate **Arize Phoenix** with **CrewAI** using OpenTelemetry via the [OpenInference](https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference) SDK. By the end of this guide, you will be able to trace your CrewAI agents and debug agent behavior.\n \n > **What is Arize Phoenix?** [Arize Phoenix](https://arize.com/phoenix/) is the open-source observability and evaluation option from [Arize AI](https://arize.com/?utm_source=crewai-docs&utm_medium=partner&utm_campaign=partner-docs&utm_content=observability-arize-phoenix). Use Phoenix when you want to run locally or self-host. Use [Arize AX](https://arize.com/products/ax/) for a managed cloud or enterprise self-hosted platform for production AI systems.\n \n@@ -152,4 +152,4 @@ Open your Phoenix project and navigate to the project you specified in the `proj\n - [Arize LLM evaluation guide](https://arize.com/resources/llm-evaluation/) - Methods and metrics for evaluating LLM applications.\n - [CrewAI Documentation](https://docs.crewai.com/) - Overview of the CrewAI framework.\n - [OpenTelemetry Docs](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/) - OpenTelemetry guide\n-- [OpenInference GitHub](https://github.com/openinference/openinference) - Source code for OpenInference SDK.\n+- [OpenInference GitHub](https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference) - Source code for OpenInference SDK.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/braintrust.mdx b/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/braintrust.mdx\nindex 21ab52c852..c2ca9c5f31 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/braintrust.mdx\n+++ b/docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/braintrust.mdx\n@@ -234,4 +234,4 @@ See the [Braintrust Eval SDK guide](https://www.braintrust.dev/docs/start/eval-s\n - [Braintrust Eval SDK](https://www.braintrust.dev/docs/start/eval-sdk) - Run experiments via the SDK\n - [CrewAI Documentation](https://docs.crewai.com/) - Overview of the CrewAI framework\n - [OpenTelemetry Docs](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/) - OpenTelemetry guide\n-- [Braintrust GitHub](https://github.com/braintrustdata/braintrust) - Source code for Braintrust SDK\n+- [Braintrust GitHub](https://github.com/braintrustdata/braintrust-sdk-python) - Source code for Braintrust SDK\n", "test_patch": "", "problem_statement": "Dead repo links in observability guides (braintrust.mdx, arize-phoenix.mdx)\n## What\n\nTwo observability guides link to repositories that no longer exist:\n\n- `docs/edge/en/observability/braintrust.mdx` and `docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/braintrust.mdx` link to `braintrustdata/braintrust` (404). The current `braintrust` PyPI package (0.47.0) declares `braintrustdata/braintrust-sdk-python` as its source repo.\n- `docs/edge/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx` and `docs/v1.15.28/en/observability/arize-phoenix.mdx` link to `openinference/openinference` (404; the openinference org no longer hosts a repo of that name). The OpenInference PyPI packages declare `Arize-ai/openinference` as source; that repo is active (pushed 2026-10-20).\n\n## Fix\n\nReady in #8310 (6 link replacements across dev source + current version tree).\n\n## AI disclosure\n\nPer CONTRIBUTING.md this issue was prepared with AI assistance; I cannot apply labels here \u2014 please add the `llm-generated` label.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-20T12:08:07Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8308, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8308", "issue_numbers": ["8306"], "base_commit": "78cc9d9e9573442d1313348529e6378412edcbec", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py\nindex 0974ae7cc7..492faddf22 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py\n@@ -2844,8 +2844,10 @@ def _trigger_replan(self, reason: str) -> None:\n             if self.task:\n                 original_description = self.task.description\n                 self.task.description = enhanced_description\n-                output = planning_handler.handle_agent_reasoning()\n-                self.task.description = original_description\n+                try:\n+                    output = planning_handler.handle_agent_reasoning()\n+                finally:\n+                    self.task.description = original_description\n             else:\n                 # description is a read-only property \u2014 recreate with enhanced text\n                 input_text = getattr(self, \"_kickoff_input\", \"\")\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/agents/test_agent_executor.py b/lib/crewai/tests/agents/test_agent_executor.py\nindex e3ea8d89fb..6a42d9f593 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/agents/test_agent_executor.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/agents/test_agent_executor.py\n@@ -2988,6 +2988,22 @@ def test_generate_plan_does_not_mutate_task_description(self):\n             \"generate_plan should store plan in state, not task.description\"\n         )\n \n+    def test_failed_replan_restores_task_description(self):\n+        task = SimpleNamespace(description=\"What is the capital of France?\")\n+        executor = _build_executor(\n+            agent=SimpleNamespace(verbose=False),\n+            task=task,\n+        )\n+\n+        with patch(\"crewai.utilities.reasoning_handler.AgentReasoning\") as reasoning:\n+            reasoning.return_value.handle_agent_reasoning.side_effect = ValueError(\n+                \"planner failed\"\n+            )\n+            executor._trigger_replan(\"step 1 is blocked\")\n+\n+        assert task.description == \"What is the capital of France?\"\n+        assert executor.state.last_replan_reason == \"Replan failed: planner failed\"\n+\n \n # Todo Status Tracking\n \n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] Task description stays overwritten with the replan prompt when replanning fails\n### Description\n\nWhen an agent with planning enabled replans and the replan fails, the task's `description` is left permanently overwritten with the internal replan prompt.\n\n`AgentExecutor._trigger_replan` (`lib/crewai/src/crewai/agents/agent_executor.py`) temporarily swaps the task description to build the replan request, then restores it:\n\n```python\noriginal_description = self.task.description\nself.task.description = enhanced_description\noutput = planning_handler.handle_agent_reasoning()\nself.task.description = original_description\n```\n\nThe restore isn't in a `finally`, so any exception from `handle_agent_reasoning()` skips it. The broad `except Exception` below then swallows the error (logged only when `verbose=True`), and the run continues with the modified description. `HookAborted` is re-raised, but it skips the restore too.\n\nRealistic triggers are the planner model returning a plan that fails `ReasoningPlan` validation, or the planning LLM call raising (for a planner model without function calling).\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\nRun the script below. It forces the planner call to fail and then checks the task description.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`task.description` is restored to the original text whether or not the replan succeeds.\n\n### Screenshots/Code snippets\n\n```python\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\n\nfrom crewai import LLM, Agent, Task\nfrom crewai.agent.planning_config import PlanningConfig\nfrom crewai.agents.agent_executor import AgentExecutor\nfrom crewai.utilities.reasoning_handler import AgentReasoning\n\nllm = LLM(model=\"gpt-4o-mini\", api_key=\"sk-fake\")\nagent = Agent(\n    role=\"Researcher\",\n    goal=\"Answer\",\n    backstory=\"b\",\n    llm=llm,\n    planning_config=PlanningConfig(max_replans=2),\n)\ntask = Task(description=\"What is the capital of France?\", expected_output=\"A city.\", agent=agent)\nexecutor = AgentExecutor(agent=agent, llm=llm, task=task)\n\n# Stand-in for any planner failure: an API error, a malformed plan failing validation, ...\nwith patch.object(\n    AgentReasoning, \"handle_agent_reasoning\", side_effect=ValueError(\"planner failed\")\n):\n    executor._trigger_replan(\"step 1 is blocked\")\n\nprint(\"last_replan_reason:\", executor.state.last_replan_reason)\nprint(\"task.description unchanged:\", task.description == \"What is the capital of France?\")\nprint(\"task.description now:\", task.description[:200], \"...\")\n```\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.12\n\n### crewAI Version\n\n1.15.28 (main @ 65cdd70ac)\n\n### crewAI Tools Version\n\nN/A\n\n### Virtual Environment\n\nVenv\n\n### Evidence\n\nOutput of the script:\n\n```\nlast_replan_reason: Replan failed: planner failed\ntask.description unchanged: False\ntask.description now: What is the capital of France?\n\nIMPORTANT: Previous execution attempt did not fully succeed. Please create a revised plan that accounts for the following context from the previous attempt:\n...\n```\n\nI also reproduced this end to end without patching crewAI, with a full `Crew.kickoff()` against a fake OpenAI-compatible server. The first plan deadlocked, which triggered a replan, and the planner then returned a plan with `\"plan\": 123`, which fails `ReasoningPlan` validation. Results:\n\n- The task still completed successfully (`TaskCompletedEvent`, output `\"Paris\"`).\n- After two failed replans, `task.description` contained the `IMPORTANT: Previous execution attempt...` block **twice**.\n- `task.output.description` also contained the replan text.\n- Nothing was printed with the default `verbose=False`.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nRestore the description in a `finally`:\n\n```python\noriginal_description = self.task.description\nself.task.description = enhanced_description\ntry:\n    output = planning_handler.handle_agent_reasoning()\nfinally:\n    self.task.description = original_description\n```\n\nI'm happy to open a PR with this plus a regression test. The existing replan-failure test (`tests/hooks/test_hook_abort_propagation.py::test_a_denied_replan_does_not_keep_executing_the_stale_plan`) uses `task=None`, so it doesn't cover the swap-and-restore path.\n\n### Additional context\n\nFound while auditing silent fallbacks in the executor, with help from Claude Code (AI-assisted). Related area: #7678, which covers other message-handling issues in the same planning code.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-20T07:06:55Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8303, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8303", "issue_numbers": ["8302"], "base_commit": "c08008b62488e99b1775becd77f53a42f11215c3", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/storage/lancedb_storage.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/storage/lancedb_storage.py\nindex 23bfc354c0..c059abb40a 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/storage/lancedb_storage.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/memory/storage/lancedb_storage.py\n@@ -353,11 +353,12 @@ def update(self, record: MemoryRecord) -> None:\n             )\n         with store_lock(self._lock_name):\n             self._ensure_table()\n-            safe_id = _sql_str(str(record.id))\n-            self._do_write(\"delete\", f\"id = '{safe_id}'\")\n+            # Reject unserializable records before deleting the stored version.\n             row = self._record_to_row(record)\n             if row[\"vector\"] is None or len(row[\"vector\"]) != self._vector_dim:\n                 row[\"vector\"] = [0.0] * self._vector_dim\n+            safe_id = _sql_str(str(record.id))\n+            self._do_write(\"delete\", f\"id = '{safe_id}'\")\n             self._do_write(\"add\", [row])\n \n     def touch_records(self, record_ids: list[str]) -> None:\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/memory/test_lancedb_update.py b/lib/crewai/tests/memory/test_lancedb_update.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..8705df4c24\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/memory/test_lancedb_update.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@\n+\"\"\"Regression tests for preserving stored memories when an update is invalid.\"\"\"\n+\n+from datetime import datetime\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+from crewai.memory.storage.lancedb_storage import LanceDBStorage\n+from crewai.memory.types import MemoryRecord\n+import pytest\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    \"invalid_value\",\n+    [datetime(2026, 1, 1), {\"tag\"}],\n+    ids=[\"datetime\", \"set\"],\n+)\n+def test_update_serialization_failure_preserves_existing_record(\n+    tmp_path: Path, invalid_value: object\n+) -> None:\n+    storage = LanceDBStorage(path=tmp_path / \"memory\", vector_dim=2, compact_every=0)\n+    original = MemoryRecord(\n+        content=\"original content\",\n+        scope=\"/notes\",\n+        metadata={\"version\": 1},\n+        embedding=[1.0, 0.0],\n+    )\n+    storage.save([original])\n+    replacement = original.model_copy(\n+        update={\"content\": \"replacement content\", \"metadata\": {\"value\": invalid_value}}\n+    )\n+\n+    with pytest.raises(TypeError, match=\"not JSON serializable\"):\n+        storage.update(replacement)\n+\n+    assert storage.get_record(original.id) == original\n+    assert storage.count() == 1\n+\n+\n+def test_update_replaces_existing_record(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n+    storage = LanceDBStorage(path=tmp_path / \"memory\", vector_dim=2, compact_every=0)\n+    original = MemoryRecord(content=\"original content\", embedding=[1.0, 0.0])\n+    storage.save([original])\n+    replacement = original.model_copy(\n+        update={\"content\": \"replacement content\", \"metadata\": {\"version\": 2}}\n+    )\n+\n+    storage.update(replacement)\n+\n+    assert storage.get_record(original.id) == replacement\n+    assert storage.count() == 1\n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] Failed LanceDB memory updates delete the original record\n### Description\n\n`LanceDBStorage.update()` deletes the saved record before serializing its replacement. If the replacement metadata is not JSON serializable, the method raises `TypeError` after the delete has committed, permanently removing the original memory.\n\nThe public `Memory.update(..., metadata=...)` method delegates to this storage method. Rejecting invalid metadata is expected; losing the previously saved record is not.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Save a memory record in a local LanceDB store.\n2. Update the same ID with metadata containing a `datetime` or `set`.\n3. Catch the serialization error and retrieve the original ID.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe invalid update raises a serialization error and leaves the existing record unchanged.\n\n### Screenshots/Code snippets\n\n```python\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom tempfile import TemporaryDirectory\n\nfrom crewai.memory.storage.lancedb_storage import LanceDBStorage\nfrom crewai.memory.types import MemoryRecord\n\nwith TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n    storage = LanceDBStorage(path=directory, vector_dim=2, compact_every=0)\n    original = MemoryRecord(\n        content=\"Keep this memory\",\n        embedding=[1.0, 0.0],\n        metadata={\"version\": 1},\n    )\n    storage.save([original])\n    replacement = original.model_copy(\n        update={\"metadata\": {\"timestamp\": datetime(2026, 1, 1)}}\n    )\n\n    try:\n        storage.update(replacement)\n    except TypeError as error:\n        print(error)\n\n    print(\"Saved record:\", storage.get_record(original.id))\n    print(\"Record count:\", storage.count())\n```\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.10.20\n\n### crewAI Version\n\n1.15.28, main at `c6e500ab3730ccf3badb640c6e0170e5c6aa3882`\n\n### crewAI Tools Version\n\nNot used by the reproduction.\n\n### Virtual Environment\n\nVenv, installed with uv from the repository lockfile.\n\n### Evidence\n\nObserved before the fix with a real temporary LanceDB database:\n\n```text\nObject of type datetime is not JSON serializable\nSaved record: None\nRecord count: 0\n```\n\nRegression tests with both `datetime` and `set` metadata fail because `get_record()` returns `None`. No LLM or embedding service is needed. Local test startup disables telemetry and stubs the unrelated authentication-token lookup.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nSerialize the replacement row and prepare its vector before deleting the stored record. This preserves the original when row serialization fails while retaining the existing serialization error.\n\n\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-20T02:29:09Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8300, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8300", "issue_numbers": ["8299"], "base_commit": "5e9be90db036caf020d8fd314a6730bb716fd068", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/mcp/client.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/mcp/client.py\nindex b84165fb52..b68d67cc69 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/mcp/client.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/mcp/client.py\n@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@\n     MCPToolExecutionFailedEvent,\n     MCPToolExecutionStartedEvent,\n )\n+from crewai.mcp.content import content_blocks_to_text\n from crewai.mcp.exceptions import (\n     MCPConnectionError,\n     error_for_status,\n@@ -621,12 +622,7 @@ async def _call_tool_impl(\n         is_error = getattr(result, \"isError\", False) or False\n \n         if hasattr(result, \"content\") and result.content:\n-            if isinstance(result.content, list) and len(result.content) > 0:\n-                content_item = result.content[0]\n-                if hasattr(content_item, \"text\"):\n-                    return _MCPToolResult(str(content_item.text), is_error)\n-                return _MCPToolResult(str(content_item), is_error)\n-            return _MCPToolResult(str(result.content), is_error)\n+            return _MCPToolResult(content_blocks_to_text(result.content), is_error)\n \n         return _MCPToolResult(str(result), is_error)\n \ndiff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/mcp/content.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/mcp/content.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..e728b8efea\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/mcp/content.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@\n+\"\"\"Flatten MCP tool result content into the text an agent sees.\"\"\"\n+\n+from typing import Any\n+\n+\n+def content_blocks_to_text(content: Any) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Join every block of an MCP ``CallToolResult.content`` into one string.\n+\n+    Text blocks and embedded text resources keep their text, one block per\n+    line. Image, audio, blob and link blocks become short typed placeholders\n+    such as ``[image: image/png]``; their base64 ``data`` and ``blob`` fields\n+    are not copied into the result.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        content: The ``content`` list of a ``CallToolResult``.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        The text of all blocks joined with newlines.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    from mcp.types import (\n+        AudioContent,\n+        EmbeddedResource,\n+        ImageContent,\n+        ResourceLink,\n+        TextContent,\n+        TextResourceContents,\n+    )\n+\n+    if not isinstance(content, list):\n+        return str(content)\n+\n+    parts: list[str] = []\n+    for block in content:\n+        if isinstance(block, TextContent):\n+            parts.append(block.text)\n+        elif isinstance(block, EmbeddedResource):\n+            resource = block.resource\n+            if isinstance(resource, TextResourceContents):\n+                parts.append(resource.text)\n+            else:\n+                parts.append(f\"[{block.type}: {resource.uri}]\")\n+        elif isinstance(block, ResourceLink):\n+            parts.append(f\"[{block.type}: {block.uri}]\")\n+        elif isinstance(block, (ImageContent, AudioContent)):\n+            parts.append(f\"[{block.type}: {block.mimeType}]\")\n+        else:\n+            parts.append(str(block))\n+    return \"\\n\".join(parts)\ndiff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_native_tool.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_native_tool.py\nindex d2ffae9f59..a9c5c39841 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_native_tool.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_native_tool.py\n@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@\n import contextvars\n from typing import Any\n \n+from crewai.mcp.content import content_blocks_to_text\n from crewai.tools import BaseTool\n from crewai.tools.tool_failure import ToolFailure, ToolFailureReason\n \n@@ -153,11 +154,6 @@ def _extract_content(result: Any) -> str:\n             return result\n \n         if hasattr(result, \"content\") and result.content:\n-            if isinstance(result.content, list) and len(result.content) > 0:\n-                content_item = result.content[0]\n-                if hasattr(content_item, \"text\"):\n-                    return str(content_item.text)\n-                return str(content_item)\n-            return str(result.content)\n+            return content_blocks_to_text(result.content)\n \n         return str(result)\ndiff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_tool_wrapper.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_tool_wrapper.py\nindex 87867b4651..a0254c41f0 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_tool_wrapper.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_tool_wrapper.py\n@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@\n from collections.abc import Callable, Coroutine\n from typing import Any\n \n+from crewai.mcp.content import content_blocks_to_text\n from crewai.tools import BaseTool\n \n \n@@ -163,7 +164,6 @@ async def _execute_tool(self, **kwargs: Any) -> str:\n         \"\"\"Execute the actual MCP tool call.\"\"\"\n         from mcp import ClientSession\n         from mcp.client.streamable_http import streamablehttp_client\n-        from mcp.types import TextContent\n \n         server_url = self.mcp_server_params[\"url\"]\n \n@@ -180,10 +180,7 @@ async def _do_mcp_call() -> str:\n                         )\n \n                         if result.content:\n-                            content_item = result.content[0]\n-                            if isinstance(content_item, TextContent):\n-                                return content_item.text\n-                            return str(content_item)\n+                            return content_blocks_to_text(result.content)\n                         return str(result)\n \n             return await asyncio.wait_for(\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/mcp/test_tool_result_content.py b/lib/crewai/tests/mcp/test_tool_result_content.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..ead3bbc70f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/mcp/test_tool_result_content.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@\n+\"\"\"MCP tool results must reach the agent with every content block.\"\"\"\n+\n+import asyncio\n+from contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n+from typing import Any\n+from unittest.mock import AsyncMock, MagicMock, patch\n+\n+import mcp.types as mcp_types\n+import pytest\n+\n+from crewai.mcp.client import MCPClient\n+from crewai.mcp.content import content_blocks_to_text\n+from crewai.tools.mcp_native_tool import MCPNativeTool\n+from crewai.tools.mcp_tool_wrapper import MCPToolWrapper\n+\n+\n+THREE_TEXT_BLOCKS = mcp_types.CallToolResult(\n+    content=[\n+        mcp_types.TextContent(type=\"text\", text=text)\n+        for text in (\"first\", \"second\", \"third\")\n+    ]\n+)\n+\n+MIXED_BLOCKS = mcp_types.CallToolResult(\n+    content=[\n+        mcp_types.TextContent(type=\"text\", text=\"chart below\"),\n+        mcp_types.ImageContent(type=\"image\", data=\"iVBORw0KGgo=\", mimeType=\"image/png\"),\n+        mcp_types.EmbeddedResource(\n+            type=\"resource\",\n+            resource=mcp_types.BlobResourceContents(\n+                uri=\"file:///report.pdf\", blob=\"JVBERi0=\", mimeType=\"application/pdf\"\n+            ),\n+        ),\n+    ]\n+)\n+\n+\n+def _via_client(result: mcp_types.CallToolResult) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"MCPClient, which feeds MCPNativeTool on the MCPServerConfig path.\"\"\"\n+    client = MCPClient(MagicMock())\n+    client._session = MagicMock(call_tool=AsyncMock(return_value=result))\n+    return asyncio.run(client._call_tool_impl(\"search\", {})).content\n+\n+\n+def _via_tool_wrapper(result: mcp_types.CallToolResult) -> Any:\n+    \"\"\"MCPToolWrapper, used for plain https:// MCP server URLs.\"\"\"\n+\n+    @asynccontextmanager\n+    async def fake_streamablehttp_client(*_args: Any, **_kwargs: Any) -> Any:\n+        yield (None, None, None)\n+\n+    session = MagicMock(\n+        initialize=AsyncMock(), call_tool=AsyncMock(return_value=result)\n+    )\n+    session.__aenter__ = AsyncMock(return_value=session)\n+    session.__aexit__ = AsyncMock(return_value=False)\n+    tool = MCPToolWrapper(\n+        mcp_server_params={\"url\": \"https://mcp.example.test/mcp\"},\n+        tool_name=\"search\",\n+        tool_schema={\"description\": \"search\"},\n+        server_name=\"demo\",\n+    )\n+    with (\n+        patch(\n+            \"mcp.client.streamable_http.streamablehttp_client\",\n+            fake_streamablehttp_client,\n+        ),\n+        patch(\"mcp.ClientSession\", return_value=session),\n+    ):\n+        return tool.run()\n+\n+\n+CALL_PATHS = pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    \"call_tool\",\n+    [_via_client, _via_tool_wrapper, MCPNativeTool._extract_content],\n+    ids=[\"mcp_client\", \"tool_wrapper\", \"native_tool_extract\"],\n+)\n+\n+\n+@CALL_PATHS\n+def test_every_text_block_reaches_the_agent(call_tool: Any) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"All text blocks are kept, in order, not just the first one.\"\"\"\n+    assert call_tool(THREE_TEXT_BLOCKS) == \"first\\nsecond\\nthird\"\n+\n+\n+@CALL_PATHS\n+def test_non_text_blocks_become_placeholders(call_tool: Any) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Image and blob blocks become placeholders without their base64 data.\"\"\"\n+    assert call_tool(MIXED_BLOCKS) == (\n+        \"chart below\\n[image: image/png]\\n[resource: file:///report.pdf]\"\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def test_remaining_block_types() -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Audio and resource links get placeholders; embedded text is kept.\"\"\"\n+    blocks = [\n+        mcp_types.AudioContent(type=\"audio\", data=\"UklGRg==\", mimeType=\"audio/wav\"),\n+        mcp_types.ResourceLink(\n+            type=\"resource_link\", uri=\"file:///notes.md\", name=\"notes\"\n+        ),\n+        mcp_types.EmbeddedResource(\n+            type=\"resource\",\n+            resource=mcp_types.TextResourceContents(\n+                uri=\"file:///inline.txt\", text=\"inline text\"\n+            ),\n+        ),\n+    ]\n+    assert content_blocks_to_text(blocks) == (\n+        \"[audio: audio/wav]\\n[resource_link: file:///notes.md]\\ninline text\"\n+    )\n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] MCP tools pass only the first content block of a tool result to the agent\n### Description\n\nWhen an MCP tool returns more than one content block, CrewAI hands only `result.content[0]` to the agent and drops the rest. If the first block is not text (an image, say), the agent gets the pydantic repr of that block, base64 data included, and the text after it is lost.\n\nThe same first-block logic exists in three places on main (c6e500ab):\n\n- `MCPClient._call_tool_impl` ([client.py#L623-L629](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/c6e500ab3730ccf3badb640c6e0170e5c6aa3882/lib/crewai/src/crewai/mcp/client.py#L623-L629)). This is the path for `mcps=[MCPServerStdio(...) / MCPServerHTTP(...) / MCPServerSSE(...)]` and AMP references, through `MCPNativeTool`.\n- `MCPToolWrapper._execute_tool` ([mcp_tool_wrapper.py#L182-L187](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/c6e500ab3730ccf3badb640c6e0170e5c6aa3882/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_tool_wrapper.py#L182-L187)). This is the path for plain `mcps=[\"https://...\"]` URLs.\n- `MCPNativeTool._extract_content` ([mcp_native_tool.py#L150-L163](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/c6e500ab3730ccf3badb640c6e0170e5c6aa3882/lib/crewai/src/crewai/tools/mcp_native_tool.py#L150-L163)). Today this is only a fallback, because `MCPClient` already returns a string, but it has the same logic.\n\n`MCPServerAdapter` in crewai-tools already keeps every text block ([mcp_adapter.py#L61-L74](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/c6e500ab3730ccf3badb640c6e0170e5c6aa3882/lib/crewai-tools/src/crewai_tools/adapters/mcp_adapter.py#L61-L74)), which suggests that dropping blocks in the native paths is not intended.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Save this MCP server as `server.py`:\n\n```python\nimport logging\n\nfrom mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP\nfrom mcp.types import ImageContent, TextContent\n\nlogging.disable(logging.INFO)\nserver = FastMCP(\"demo\")\n\n\n@server.tool(structured_output=False)\ndef three_blocks() -> list[TextContent]:\n    \"\"\"Return three text blocks.\"\"\"\n    return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=t) for t in (\"first\", \"second\", \"third\")]\n\n\n@server.tool(structured_output=False)\ndef chart() -> list[ImageContent | TextContent]:\n    \"\"\"Return an image followed by its caption.\"\"\"\n    return [\n        ImageContent(type=\"image\", data=\"iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAA\", mimeType=\"image/png\"),\n        TextContent(type=\"text\", text=\"Revenue grew 12% in Q3.\"),\n    ]\n\n\nserver.run()\n```\n\n2. Save this next to it as `repro.py`:\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nfrom crewai import Agent\nfrom crewai.mcp import MCPServerStdio\n\nserver = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), \"server.py\")\nagent = Agent(\n    role=\"r\",\n    goal=\"g\",\n    backstory=\"b\",\n    llm=\"gpt-4o-mini\",  # never called; tools are resolved and run directly\n    mcps=[MCPServerStdio(command=sys.executable, args=[server])],\n)\nfor tool in agent.get_mcp_tools(agent.mcps):\n    print(f\"RESULT {tool.original_tool_name}: {tool.run()!r}\")\n```\n\n3. Run `python repro.py | grep RESULT`. No API key or network access is needed.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe agent sees every text block, in order. A non-text block should not hide the text around it and should not put base64 data into the prompt; a short marker such as `[image: image/png]` is enough.\n\n### Screenshots/Code snippets\n\n`MCPClient._call_tool_impl` on main:\n\n```python\nif hasattr(result, \"content\") and result.content:\n    if isinstance(result.content, list) and len(result.content) > 0:\n        content_item = result.content[0]\n        if hasattr(content_item, \"text\"):\n            return _MCPToolResult(str(content_item.text), is_error)\n        return _MCPToolResult(str(content_item), is_error)\n    return _MCPToolResult(str(result.content), is_error)\n```\n\n`MCPToolWrapper._execute_tool` and `MCPNativeTool._extract_content` repeat the same `result.content[0]` pattern.\n\n### Operating System\n\nOther (specify in additional context)\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.10\n\n### crewAI Version\n\n1.15.28 (main at c6e500ab)\n\n### crewAI Tools Version\n\n1.15.28\n\n### Virtual Environment\n\nVenv\n\n### Evidence\n\nOutput of `repro.py` on main (c6e500ab) with mcp 1.30.0, the same on Python 3.10.19 and 3.13.16:\n\n```text\nRESULT three_blocks: 'first'\nRESULT chart: \"type='image' data='iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAA' mimeType='image/png' annotations=None meta=None\"\n```\n\n`second` and `third` never reach the agent. For `chart`, the agent gets the image repr with its base64 data, and the caption is gone.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nOne small helper used by all three call sites: join text blocks (and embedded text resources) with newlines, and render image, audio, blob and link blocks as a short typed placeholder such as `[image: image/png]` or `[resource: file:///report.pdf]`. A result with a single text block stays exactly as it is today.\n\nA PR with this fix and regression tests for each call site follows and links this issue.\n\n### Additional context\n\n- OS: macOS 27.0.1 (not in the dropdown).\n- #5226 tried to fix the `MCPClient` copy in April. It was closed unmerged on 2026-09-17 with the `needs-issue` label because it had no linked issue; the change itself was never reviewed. It also left the other two copies alone.\n- Open PRs touching the same files: #7643 (isError on the `MCPToolWrapper` path, edits the same lines in `_execute_tool`), #6744 (MCPClient connection and retry changes, does not touch `_call_tool_impl`), #7448 and #7756 (event-loop handling, no overlap with result flattening).\n- AI disclosure: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5) found the bug, ran the reproduction above and wrote this report. I reviewed the draft, and Claude Code filed it on my behalf. Please add the `llm-generated` label; I don't have permission to add labels.\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-20T00:39:08Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8297, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8297", "issue_numbers": ["8296"], "base_commit": "add3f7bf1e439d692eb45397aef653bd287ca708", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/cli/src/crewai_cli/input_prompt.py b/lib/cli/src/crewai_cli/input_prompt.py\nindex a91fdee7ed..49c4831ff0 100644\n--- a/lib/cli/src/crewai_cli/input_prompt.py\n+++ b/lib/cli/src/crewai_cli/input_prompt.py\n@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@\n from __future__ import annotations\n \n from collections.abc import Callable, Iterable\n+from contextlib import redirect_stdout\n import difflib\n import json\n import sys\n@@ -76,9 +77,12 @@ def prompt_for_inputs(\n     for name in names:\n         if describe is not None and (hint := describe(name)):\n             click.secho(f\"  {hint}\", dim=True, err=True)\n-        raw = click.prompt(\n-            click.style(f\"  {name}\", fg=\"cyan\"),\n-            prompt_suffix=click.style(\" > \", fg=\"bright_white\"),\n-        )\n+        # Click's Windows readline path writes the last prompt character to stdout.\n+        with redirect_stdout(sys.stderr):\n+            raw = click.prompt(\n+                click.style(f\"  {name}\", fg=\"cyan\"),\n+                prompt_suffix=click.style(\" > \", fg=\"bright_white\"),\n+                err=True,\n+            )\n         collected[name] = coerce(name, raw) if coerce is not None else raw\n     return collected\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/cli/tests/test_input_prompt.py b/lib/cli/tests/test_input_prompt.py\nindex 22bb334a90..2f2787c86e 100644\n--- a/lib/cli/tests/test_input_prompt.py\n+++ b/lib/cli/tests/test_input_prompt.py\n@@ -2,6 +2,11 @@\n \n from __future__ import annotations\n \n+import json\n+import os\n+import subprocess\n+import sys\n+\n import pytest\n \n from crewai_cli.input_prompt import (\n@@ -36,7 +41,9 @@ def test_parse_inputs_json_rejects_non_object(capsys):\n \n \n def test_closest_name_suggests_near_miss():\n-    assert closest_name(\"prospect_emai\", [\"prospect_email\", \"topic\"]) == \"prospect_email\"\n+    assert (\n+        closest_name(\"prospect_emai\", [\"prospect_email\", \"topic\"]) == \"prospect_email\"\n+    )\n \n \n def test_closest_name_returns_none_when_nothing_close():\n@@ -80,3 +87,51 @@ def test_prompt_for_inputs_keeps_raw_string_without_coerce(monkeypatch):\n     )\n \n     assert result == {\"topic\": \"AI\"}\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    (\"names\", \"input_text\", \"expected\"),\n+    [\n+        ([\"topic\"], \"AI\\n\", {\"topic\": \"AI\"}),\n+        ([\"count\", \"topic\"], \"42\\n\u7814\u7a76\\n\", {\"count\": 42, \"topic\": \"\u7814\u7a76\"}),\n+        ([\"topic\"], \"\", None),\n+    ],\n+    ids=[\"single-input\", \"multiple-inputs\", \"abort\"],\n+)\n+def test_prompt_for_inputs_keeps_prompt_chrome_on_stderr(\n+    names: list[str], input_text: str, expected: dict[str, str | int] | None\n+) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Real Click prompts must leave stdout available for serialized results.\"\"\"\n+    script = (\n+        \"import json\\n\"\n+        \"import click\\n\"\n+        \"from crewai_cli.input_prompt import prompt_for_inputs\\n\"\n+        f\"names = {names!r}\\n\"\n+        \"try:\\n\"\n+        \"    result = prompt_for_inputs(\\n\"\n+        \"        names, title='Runtime inputs', subtitle='Required values',\\n\"\n+        \"        describe=lambda name: f'Value for {name}',\\n\"\n+        \"        coerce=lambda name, raw: int(raw) if name == 'count' else raw,\\n\"\n+        \"    )\\n\"\n+        \"except click.Abort:\\n\"\n+        \"    result = None\\n\"\n+        \"print(json.dumps(result, ensure_ascii=False))\\n\"\n+    )\n+    result = subprocess.run(\n+        [sys.executable, \"-c\", script],\n+        input=input_text,\n+        capture_output=True,\n+        text=True,\n+        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n+        env={**os.environ, \"PYTHONIOENCODING\": \"utf-8\"},\n+        check=False,\n+        timeout=20,\n+    )\n+\n+    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr\n+    assert result.stdout == json.dumps(expected, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\"\n+    assert \"Runtime inputs\" in result.stderr\n+    assert \"Required values\" in result.stderr\n+    for name in names:\n+        assert f\"Value for {name}\" in result.stderr\n+        assert f\"{name} > \" in result.stderr\n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] Runtime input prompts contaminate stdout reserved for run results\n## Description\n\nThe shared `crewai_cli.input_prompt.prompt_for_inputs` helper documents that prompt chrome goes to stderr, leaving stdout for the run result. Its title, subtitle and description use `err=True`, but its `click.prompt` call does not. The field prompt and ANSI suffix appear on stdout before the result, so a consumer cannot parse the serialized output even when the process succeeds.\n\nThis was found by source inspection and reproduced offline on `main@c6e500ab3730ccf3badb640c6e0170e5c6aa3882`; it is not a reported production incident. JSON crew and declarative-flow input resolution both use this helper. This report concerns that helper's I/O contract, not a claim that every output from the complete `crewai run` command is JSON.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\nRun against an installed checkout:\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\n\nscript = (\n    \"import json; from crewai_cli.input_prompt import prompt_for_inputs; \"\n    \"print(json.dumps(prompt_for_inputs(['topic'], \"\n    \"title='Crew inputs', subtitle='Required values')))\"\n)\nresult = subprocess.run(\n    [sys.executable, \"-c\", script],\n    input=\"AI\\n\",\n    capture_output=True,\n    text=True,\n    check=False,\n)\nprint(result.returncode)\nprint(repr(result.stdout))\nprint(repr(result.stderr))\njson.loads(result.stdout)\n```\n\nNo model, API key, network service or project is required.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nThe return value remains `{\"topic\": \"AI\"}`. All prompt text is written to stderr; the wrapper's stdout is exactly `{\"topic\": \"AI\"}\\n` and remains usable after normal input or an input abort.\n\n## Screenshots/Code snippets\n\nObserved on Windows with Click 8.4.2:\n\n```text\nexit: 0\nstdout: '  topic > \\x1b[0m{\"topic\": \"AI\"}\\n'\nstderr: '\\n  Crew inputs\\n  Required values\\n'\nJSON consumer rejects stdout: Expecting value: line 1 column 3 (char 2)\n```\n\n## Operating System\n\nNative Windows; the exact Windows product edition is not claimed.\n\n## Python Version\n\n3.12.8\n\n## crewAI Version\n\ncrewai-cli 1.15.28, editable current-main checkout at the SHA above; Click 8.4.2.\n\n## crewAI Tools Version\n\nNot involved in this reproduction.\n\n## Virtual Environment\n\nuv venv using current lockfile dependencies, synchronized with `uv sync --locked --package crewai --group dev --python <Python-3.12.8>`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThree real-subprocess regressions for one field, multiple fields with coercion/non-ASCII input, and EOF abort yield **3 failed, 8 passed** on the unchanged production file. Existing tests replace `click.prompt` and therefore do not observe its real stream behavior.\n\n## Possible Solution\n\nRoute the Click prompt to stderr. On Windows, `err=True` alone is insufficient with the tested Click version: `_readline_prompt` writes the last prompt character through `input()` on stdout. A short `redirect_stdout(sys.stderr)` context around only the `click.prompt` call handles that path and restores the caller's stdout on return or exception. Coercion and subsequent result output remain outside the context. This is a process-wide redirection scoped to synchronous input collection, not a thread-local logging mechanism.\n\n## Additional context\n\nAll-state PR and Issue searches for `prompt_for_inputs`/`input_prompt` and stderr/stdout did not identify a matching fix when prepared. Merged PR #6466 introduced the current shared helper; its implementation also lacks the stderr routing on the field prompt.\n\nAI assistance: Codex checked related work, reproduced the behavior, prepared a focused patch and tests, and ran local checks. Please apply the required `llm-generated` label; this external account cannot add repository labels.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-20T00:07:32Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8282, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8282", "issue_numbers": ["8233"], "base_commit": "b523e6124f145010a881ff68e74764bcab338789", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/llms/providers/anthropic/completion.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/llms/providers/anthropic/completion.py\nindex a3d8d78333..8c582db946 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/llms/providers/anthropic/completion.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/llms/providers/anthropic/completion.py\n@@ -625,7 +625,8 @@ def _prepare_completion_params(\n             system_message: Extracted system message\n             tools: Tool definitions\n             available_functions: Available functions for tool calling. When provided\n-                with a single tool, tool_choice is automatically set to force tool use.\n+                with a single tool, tool_choice is \"auto\" so the model may call\n+                that tool or answer in text.\n \n         Returns:\n             Parameters dictionary for Anthropic API\n@@ -652,8 +653,7 @@ def _prepare_completion_params(\n \n             # When tool_search is enabled and there are 2+ regular tools,\n             # inject the search tool and mark regular tools with defer_loading.\n-            # With only 1 tool there's nothing to search \u2014 skip tool search\n-            # entirely so the normal forced tool_choice optimisation still works.\n+            # With only 1 tool there's nothing to search, so skip tool search.\n             regular_tools = [\n                 t\n                 for t in converted_tools\n@@ -664,10 +664,11 @@ def _prepare_completion_params(\n \n             params[\"tools\"] = converted_tools\n \n+            # available_functions means the tool can be executed, not that the\n+            # model must call it. Named tool_choice is also rejected by newer\n+            # Claude models (Sonnet 5.5, Opus 5.5, Fable 5.1, Mythos 5.1).\n             if available_functions and len(regular_tools) == 1:\n-                tool_name = regular_tools[0].get(\"name\")\n-                if tool_name and tool_name in available_functions:\n-                    params[\"tool_choice\"] = {\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": tool_name}\n+                params[\"tool_choice\"] = {\"type\": \"auto\"}\n \n         if self.thinking:\n             if isinstance(self.thinking, AnthropicThinkingConfig):\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/llms/anthropic/test_anthropic.py b/lib/crewai/tests/llms/anthropic/test_anthropic.py\nindex 059627ba9d..8fce270660 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/llms/anthropic/test_anthropic.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/llms/anthropic/test_anthropic.py\n@@ -1470,9 +1470,9 @@ def test_tool_search_passthrough_preserves_tool_search_type():\n     assert \"input_schema\" in converted[1]\n \n \n-def test_tool_search_single_tool_skips_search_and_forces_choice():\n-    \"\"\"With only 1 tool, tool_search is skipped (nothing to search) and the\n-    normal forced tool_choice optimisation still applies.\"\"\"\n+def test_tool_search_single_tool_skips_search_and_uses_auto_choice():\n+    \"\"\"With only 1 tool, tool_search is skipped (nothing to search) and\n+    tool_choice stays auto.\"\"\"\n     llm = LLM(model=\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5\", tool_search=True)\n \n     crewai_tools = [\n@@ -1500,9 +1500,8 @@ def test_tool_search_single_tool_skips_search_and_forces_choice():\n         available_functions={\"test_tool\": lambda q: \"result\"},\n     )\n \n-    # Single tool \u2014 tool_search skipped, tool_choice forced as normal\n-    assert \"tool_choice\" in params\n-    assert params[\"tool_choice\"][\"name\"] == \"test_tool\"\n+    # Single tool \u2014 tool_search skipped, model chooses whether to call it\n+    assert params[\"tool_choice\"] == {\"type\": \"auto\"}\n \n     # No tool search tool should be injected\n     tool_types = [t.get(\"type\", \"\") for t in params[\"tools\"]]\n@@ -1513,6 +1512,39 @@ def test_tool_search_single_tool_skips_search_and_forces_choice():\n     assert \"defer_loading\" not in params[\"tools\"][0]\n \n \n+def test_single_tool_with_available_functions_uses_auto_choice():\n+    \"\"\"One executable tool is offered, not forced.\n+\n+    Newer Claude models reject tool_choice {\"type\": \"tool\"}. Auto lets the\n+    model call the tool or answer in text.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    llm = LLM(model=\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5\")\n+    tool = {\n+        \"type\": \"function\",\n+        \"function\": {\n+            \"name\": \"get_weather\",\n+            \"description\": \"Get the weather for a city.\",\n+            \"parameters\": {\n+                \"type\": \"object\",\n+                \"properties\": {\"city\": {\"type\": \"string\"}},\n+                \"required\": [\"city\"],\n+            },\n+        },\n+    }\n+    formatted_messages, system_message = llm._format_messages_for_anthropic(\n+        [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What's the weather in Paris?\"}]\n+    )\n+    params = llm._prepare_completion_params(\n+        formatted_messages,\n+        system_message,\n+        [tool],\n+        available_functions={\"get_weather\": lambda city: \"sunny\"},\n+    )\n+\n+    assert params[\"tool_choice\"] == {\"type\": \"auto\"}\n+    assert [t[\"name\"] for t in params[\"tools\"]] == [\"get_weather\"]\n+\n+\n def test_tool_search_via_llm_class():\n     \"\"\"Verify tool_search param passes through LLM class correctly.\"\"\"\n     from crewai.llms.providers.anthropic.completion import (\n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] Claude Sonnet 5.5 / Opus 5.5 on native Anthropic provider will return 400 when one tool is passed with available_functions\n### Description\n\nWith exactly one tool and using the available_functions parameter, AnthropicCompletion._prepare_completion_params sets tool_choice: {\"type\": \"tool\"}. This was fine for older models such as Claude Sonnet 5 and below but Claude Sonnet 5.5, Opus 5.5, Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1 will reject that with a error stating `400 tool_choice: type \"tool\" and \"any\" are not supported for this model` as shown on the [claude docs](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/migration-guide#forced-tool-use ). This will break the crewai chat on any message that is invoked through crewai with this configuration by making the agent reasoning step fail its tool call and fall back to text. The Bedrock counterpart is #7725 / #7726.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Install crewAI 1.15.28 with the Anthropic extra (crewai[anthropic]) and set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.\n2. Call the native Anthropic provider with just one tool and the `available_functions` parameter:\n\n```\nfrom crewai import LLM\n\nllm = LLM(model=\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5\")\nweather_tool = {\n    \"type\": \"function\",\n    \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"get_weather\",\n        \"description\": \"Get the weather for a city.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\"city\": {\"type\": \"string\"}},\n            \"required\": [\"city\"],\n        },\n    },\n}\nllm.call(\n    \"What's the weather in Paris?\",\n    tools=[weather_tool],\n    available_functions={\"get_weather\": lambda city: \"sunny\"},\n)\n```\n\nThe call will raise a 400 error. The same will happen with anthropic/claude-opus-5-5, and on every message in crewai chat with those models.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe call succeeds on Sonnet 5.5 and Opus 5.5, as it does on claude-sonnet-5: the model either calls get_weather or answers in text.\n\n### Screenshots/Code snippets\n\nThe following usage:\n\n```\nfrom crewai import LLM\n\nllm = LLM(model=\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5\")\nweather_tool = {\n    \"type\": \"function\",\n    \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"get_weather\",\n        \"description\": \"Get the weather for a city.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\"city\": {\"type\": \"string\"}},\n            \"required\": [\"city\"],\n        },\n    },\n}\nllm.call(\n    \"What's the weather in Paris?\",\n    tools=[weather_tool],\n    available_functions={\"get_weather\": lambda city: \"sunny\"},\n)\n```\n\nwill invoke the tool forcing code: https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/main/lib/crewai/src/crewai/llms/providers/anthropic/completion.py#L667-L670\n\n```\nif available_functions and len(regular_tools) == 1:\n  tool_name = regular_tools[0].get(\"name\")\n  if tool_name and tool_name in available_functions:\n    params[\"tool_choice\"] = {\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": tool_name}\n```\n\n### Operating System\n\nUbuntu 20.04\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.10\n\n### crewAI Version\n\n1.15.28\n\n### crewAI Tools Version\n\n1.15.28\n\n### Virtual Environment\n\nVenv\n\n### Evidence\n\ndon\u2019t have Anthropic API access to capture the live response, so here is the request crewAI builds. Running the repro script on crewAI 1.15.27 with anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 (dummy key):\n```\ncrewai 1.15.27, anthropic <version>\nmodel: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5\ntool_choice sent by crewAI: {'type': 'tool', 'name': 'get_weather'}\n```\nSonnet 5.5 / Opus 5.5 reject this with 400 invalid_request_error: tool_choice: type \"tool\" and \"any\" are not supported for this model. That\u2019s the same error #7726 recorded live on Bedrock for these models. The repro script is attached; with a real ANTHROPIC_API_KEY it shows the 400 directly.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nI believe we should be skipping the forced tool_choice on models that reject/ do not support it. This makes the API\u2019s default to auto apply. We keep the other (older) model with the current forced behaviour. The existing _supports_native_structured_outputs already maintains a deny list so we can do the same.\n\n### Additional context\n\nNone\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-19T15:59:08Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8278, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8278", "issue_numbers": ["8276"], "base_commit": "0b84f8e18b45c3f22e101c28c3d4e9852bdfcccd", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai-tools/src/crewai_tools/rag/loaders/json_loader.py b/lib/crewai-tools/src/crewai_tools/rag/loaders/json_loader.py\nindex 41c019f3ed..8d8c98f694 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai-tools/src/crewai_tools/rag/loaders/json_loader.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai-tools/src/crewai_tools/rag/loaders/json_loader.py\n@@ -33,12 +33,18 @@ def _parse_json(self, content: str, source_ref: str) -> LoaderResult:\n             data = json.loads(content)\n             if isinstance(data, dict):\n                 text = \"\\n\".join(\n-                    f\"{k}: {json.dumps(v, indent=0)}\" for k, v in data.items()\n+                    f\"{k}: {json.dumps(v, indent=0, ensure_ascii=False)}\"\n+                    for k, v in data.items()\n                 )\n             elif isinstance(data, list):\n-                text = \"\\n\".join(json.dumps(item, indent=0) for item in data)\n+                text = \"\\n\".join(\n+                    json.dumps(item, indent=0, ensure_ascii=False) for item in data\n+                )\n             else:\n-                text = json.dumps(data, indent=0)\n+                text = json.dumps(data, indent=0, ensure_ascii=False)\n+\n+            # Keep lone surrogates escaped without replacing readable Unicode.\n+            text = text.encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"backslashreplace\").decode(\"utf-8\")\n \n             metadata = {\n                 \"format\": \"json\",\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai-tools/tests/rag/test_json_loader_bom.py b/lib/crewai-tools/tests/rag/test_json_loader_bom.py\nindex 0802d9ce23..419a3bf3f7 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai-tools/tests/rag/test_json_loader_bom.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai-tools/tests/rag/test_json_loader_bom.py\n@@ -34,6 +34,6 @@ def test_json_loader_preserves_internal_bom_and_malformed_fallback(\n     \"\"\"Only a leading BOM is removed; content and malformed fallback stay intact.\"\"\"\n     internal = _load(tmp_path, b'{\"value\":\"a\\xef\\xbb\\xbf b\"}')\n     malformed = _load(tmp_path, b\"\\xef\\xbb\\xbf{invalid json}\")\n-    assert \"a\\\\ufeff b\" in internal.content\n+    assert \"a\\ufeff b\" in internal.content\n     assert \"parse_error\" in malformed.metadata\n     assert malformed.content == \"{invalid json}\"\ndiff --git a/lib/crewai-tools/tests/rag/test_json_loader_unicode.py b/lib/crewai-tools/tests/rag/test_json_loader_unicode.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..5d65e165d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/lib/crewai-tools/tests/rag/test_json_loader_unicode.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@\n+import pytest\n+\n+from crewai_tools.rag.loaders.json_loader import JSONLoader\n+from crewai_tools.rag.source_content import SourceContent\n+\n+\n+def test_json_loader_keeps_non_ascii_text_readable() -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Object values keep readable Unicode characters.\"\"\"\n+    raw = '{\"city\": \"M\u00e1laga\", \"note\": \"\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\"}'\n+\n+    result = JSONLoader().load(SourceContent(raw))\n+\n+    assert \"M\u00e1laga\" in result.content\n+    assert \"\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\" in result.content\n+    assert \"\\\\u\" not in result.content\n+\n+\n+def test_json_loader_list_keeps_non_ascii_text_readable() -> None:\n+    \"\"\"List items keep readable Unicode characters.\"\"\"\n+    result = JSONLoader().load(SourceContent('[\"caf\u00e9\", \"na\u00efve\"]'))\n+\n+    assert \"caf\u00e9\" in result.content\n+    assert \"\\\\u\" not in result.content\n+\n+\n+def test_json_loader_scalar_keeps_non_ascii_text_readable() -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Scalar strings keep readable Unicode characters.\"\"\"\n+    result = JSONLoader().load(SourceContent('\"M\u00e1laga\"'))\n+\n+    assert result.content == '\"M\u00e1laga\"'\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"surrogate\", [r\"\\ud800\", r\"\\udfff\"])\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"shape\", [\"object\", \"list\", \"scalar\"])\n+def test_json_loader_lone_surrogate_stays_escaped(surrogate: str, shape: str) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Lone surrogate escapes remain ingestible without losing their value.\"\"\"\n+    value = '\"caf\u00e9 ' + surrogate + '\"'\n+    raw = {\n+        \"object\": '{\"value\": ' + value + '}',\n+        \"list\": '[' + value + ']',\n+        \"scalar\": value,\n+    }[shape]\n+\n+    result = JSONLoader().load(SourceContent(raw))\n+\n+    assert surrogate in result.content\n+    assert \"caf\u00e9\" in result.content\n+    assert result.content.encode(\"utf-8\")\n+    assert result.doc_id\n+\n+\n+def test_json_loader_paired_surrogate_keeps_emoji_readable() -> None:\n+    \"\"\"A valid surrogate pair is rendered as its Unicode character.\"\"\"\n+    result = JSONLoader().load(SourceContent(r'\"\\ud83d\\ude00\"'))\n+\n+    assert result.content == '\"\ud83d\ude00\"'\n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] JSONLoader escapes non-ASCII text when rendering JSON documents\n### Description\n\nJSONLoader renders parsed JSON back into text with `json.dumps` and its default `ensure_ascii=True`. Any non-ASCII text in the source JSON (names, places, non-English content) is escaped into its `\\uXXXX` ASCII form, and that escaped text is what ends up in the document content that gets embedded and passed to the model. The JSON itself stores the characters fine; they are only lost in the rendered text.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Create `data.json` with non-ASCII content:\n\n```json\n{\"name\": \"caf\u00e9\", \"city\": \"M\u00fcnchen\"}\n```\n\n2. Load it:\n\n```python\nfrom crewai_tools.rag.loaders.json_loader import JSONLoader\nfrom crewai_tools.rag.source_content import SourceContent\n\nresult = JSONLoader().load(SourceContent(\"data.json\"))\nprint(result.content)\n```\n\n3. In the rendered content, `\u00e9` and `\u00fc` come out as their four-digit `\\uXXXX` escape sequences instead of the readable characters.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe rendered text keeps the original characters (`caf\u00e9`, `M\u00fcnchen`). `json.dumps(..., ensure_ascii=False)` is still valid JSON text, but it preserves the characters for embedding and retrieval. The same escaping happens for top-level lists and scalars, which all go through `json.dumps` with the same default.\n\n### Screenshots/Code snippets\n\nSee the snippet above.\n\n### Operating System\n\nUbuntu 24.04\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.13\n\n### crewAI Version\n\n1.15.28\n\n### crewAI Tools Version\n\n1.15.28\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nPass `ensure_ascii=False` in the three `json.dumps` calls in `crewai_tools/rag/loaders/json_loader.py`. Happy to open a PR with regression tests.\n\nDisclosure: investigated and drafted with an AI assistant, reviewed and submitted by me. The contributing guide asks for the `llm-generated` label; GitHub does not let me apply labels from my account, so a maintainer may need to add it.\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-19T14:43:47Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8272, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8272", "issue_numbers": ["8139"], "base_commit": "c358daab14fc5e6b6192365848c6e0d208d7524d", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/persistence/sqlite.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/persistence/sqlite.py\nindex dc45af5927..45a1db6728 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/persistence/sqlite.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/persistence/sqlite.py\n@@ -246,6 +246,42 @@ def load_state(self, flow_uuid: str) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n             return result if isinstance(result, dict) else None\n         return None\n \n+    def load_state_from_history(\n+        self, flow_uuid: str, record_id: int\n+    ) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n+        \"\"\"Load one historical state saved for a given flow UUID.\n+\n+        Args:\n+            flow_uuid: Unique identifier for the flow instance\n+            record_id: Row id of the saved state in the flow_states table.\n+                This is not the flow's ``state.id``.\n+\n+        Returns:\n+            The stored state as a dictionary, or None if the flow has no\n+            state with that row id. Like load_state, a stored state that is\n+            not a JSON object also returns None.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        with (\n+            closing(\n+                sqlite3.connect(self.db_path, timeout=_SQLITE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\n+            ) as conn,\n+            conn,\n+        ):\n+            cursor = conn.execute(\n+                \"\"\"\n+            SELECT state_json\n+            FROM flow_states\n+            WHERE id = ? AND flow_uuid = ?\n+            \"\"\",\n+                (record_id, flow_uuid),\n+            )\n+            row = cursor.fetchone()\n+\n+        if row:\n+            result = json.loads(row[0])\n+            return result if isinstance(result, dict) else None\n+        return None\n+\n     def save_pending_feedback(\n         self,\n         flow_uuid: str,\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_persistence.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_persistence.py\nindex 22f146c6f7..287806267f 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_persistence.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_persistence.py\n@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@\n \"\"\"Test flow state persistence functionality.\"\"\"\n \n+from contextlib import closing\n import os\n+import sqlite3\n from typing import Dict, List\n \n import pytest\n@@ -638,3 +640,82 @@ def count_up(self):\n     saved_state = persistence.load_state(flow.state.id)\n     assert saved_state is not None\n     assert saved_state[\"counter\"] == 1\n+\n+\n+def _flow_state_row_ids(db_path: str, flow_uuid: str) -> list[int]:\n+    \"\"\"Return the flow_states row ids saved for a flow, oldest first.\"\"\"\n+    with closing(sqlite3.connect(db_path)) as conn:\n+        rows = conn.execute(\n+            \"SELECT id FROM flow_states WHERE flow_uuid = ? ORDER BY id\",\n+            (flow_uuid,),\n+        ).fetchall()\n+    return [row[0] for row in rows]\n+\n+\n+def test_load_state_from_history_returns_exact_nested_state(tmp_path):\n+    \"\"\"Test that a historical row returns its own stored state, not the latest.\"\"\"\n+    db_path = os.path.join(tmp_path, \"test_flows.db\")\n+    persistence = SQLiteFlowPersistence(db_path)\n+    first = {\n+        \"id\": \"flow-1\",\n+        \"step\": 1,\n+        \"nested\": {\"items\": [{\"name\": \"a\", \"tags\": [\"x\", \"y\"]}], \"meta\": {\"ok\": True}},\n+    }\n+    persistence.save_state(\"flow-1\", \"first_step\", first)\n+    persistence.save_state(\"flow-1\", \"second_step\", {\"id\": \"flow-1\", \"step\": 2})\n+    persistence.save_state(\"flow-1\", \"third_step\", {\"id\": \"flow-1\", \"step\": 3})\n+\n+    first_row_id = _flow_state_row_ids(db_path, \"flow-1\")[0]\n+\n+    assert persistence.load_state_from_history(\"flow-1\", first_row_id) == first\n+\n+\n+def test_load_state_from_history_returns_none_for_missing_record(tmp_path):\n+    \"\"\"Test that a missing row id or an unknown flow UUID returns None.\"\"\"\n+    db_path = os.path.join(tmp_path, \"test_flows.db\")\n+    persistence = SQLiteFlowPersistence(db_path)\n+    persistence.save_state(\"flow-1\", \"first_step\", {\"id\": \"flow-1\", \"step\": 1})\n+\n+    row_id = _flow_state_row_ids(db_path, \"flow-1\")[0]\n+\n+    assert persistence.load_state_from_history(\"flow-1\", row_id + 1) is None\n+    assert persistence.load_state_from_history(\"unknown-flow\", row_id) is None\n+\n+\n+def test_load_state_from_history_never_returns_another_flows_row(tmp_path):\n+    \"\"\"Test that a row id only resolves under the flow UUID that saved it.\"\"\"\n+    db_path = os.path.join(tmp_path, \"test_flows.db\")\n+    persistence = SQLiteFlowPersistence(db_path)\n+    persistence.save_state(\"flow-a\", \"step\", {\"id\": \"flow-a\", \"value\": \"a1\"})\n+    persistence.save_state(\"flow-b\", \"step\", {\"id\": \"flow-b\", \"value\": \"b1\"})\n+    persistence.save_state(\"flow-a\", \"step\", {\"id\": \"flow-a\", \"value\": \"a2\"})\n+\n+    a_ids = _flow_state_row_ids(db_path, \"flow-a\")\n+    b_ids = _flow_state_row_ids(db_path, \"flow-b\")\n+\n+    assert persistence.load_state_from_history(\"flow-a\", a_ids[0]) == {\n+        \"id\": \"flow-a\",\n+        \"value\": \"a1\",\n+    }\n+    assert persistence.load_state_from_history(\"flow-b\", b_ids[0]) == {\n+        \"id\": \"flow-b\",\n+        \"value\": \"b1\",\n+    }\n+    assert persistence.load_state_from_history(\"flow-b\", a_ids[0]) is None\n+    assert persistence.load_state_from_history(\"flow-a\", b_ids[0]) is None\n+\n+\n+def test_load_state_still_returns_latest_after_history_lookup(tmp_path):\n+    \"\"\"Test that looking up an older row leaves load_state on the latest state.\"\"\"\n+    db_path = os.path.join(tmp_path, \"test_flows.db\")\n+    persistence = SQLiteFlowPersistence(db_path)\n+    persistence.save_state(\"flow-1\", \"first_step\", {\"id\": \"flow-1\", \"step\": 1})\n+    persistence.save_state(\"flow-1\", \"second_step\", {\"id\": \"flow-1\", \"step\": 2})\n+\n+    first_row_id = _flow_state_row_ids(db_path, \"flow-1\")[0]\n+\n+    assert persistence.load_state_from_history(\"flow-1\", first_row_id) == {\n+        \"id\": \"flow-1\",\n+        \"step\": 1,\n+    }\n+    assert persistence.load_state(\"flow-1\") == {\"id\": \"flow-1\", \"step\": 2}\n", "problem_statement": "[FEATURE] Add exact historical Flow state lookup scoped to its UUID\n## Python PR scope\n\nAdd a read-only method to retrieve one historical state row by its stable row ID and Flow UUID, alongside the history listing API.\n\n**Difficulty:** easy. **Allocation index:** #8118. **Project:** #8121.\n\n## Cohort allocation\n\nThis ticket is reserved for maintainer-coordinated allocation to the Stanford semester collaboration. Please wait for @lorenzejay to confirm an assignee before implementing. A comment expresses interest; it does not establish ownership. Public `good first issue` / `help wanted` discovery labels will be considered after cohort allocation.\n\nGitHub usernames have not yet been supplied, so no individual assignment is implied.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A row belonging to another Flow UUID must not be returned.\n- [ ] Return None for a missing record, and preserve the stored JSON state for a matching record.\n- [ ] Test nested state data, missing IDs, multiple flows, and latest-state API regression.\n- [ ] Use existing JSON decoding conventions and bound SQL parameters.\n- [ ] Do not change the active Flow state or add a historical resume API.\n\n## Dependencies and coordination\n\n- Depends on #8138.\n\n## Starting points\n\n- [lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/persistence/sqlite.py](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/main/lib/crewai/src/crewai/flow/persistence/sqlite.py)\n- [lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_persistence.py](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/main/lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_persistence.py)\n\n## Submission\n\nThe contributor implements this scope and submits one focused PR linked to this open issue. Include full Python annotations, behavioral tests, and relevant quality checks. No paid API calls are required for the tests. Preserve existing APIs outside the scoped feature. For newly found defects, reproduce them and check active issues/PRs before fixing them. Docs edits, when needed, belong under `docs/edge/` and must sync ar, ko, pt-BR per `DOCS_TRANSLATIONS.md`. Follow [.github/CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md). Issue prepared with AI assistance.\n", "hints_text": "I would like to take up this as a part of the Stanford collaboration. \n@lorenzejay A quick question about the dependency on #8138: it's still unassigned with no PR, so the history listing API doesn't exist on main yet. Should I implement the lookup independently now, or wait for #8138? And should the lookup return the plain state dict like `load_state`, or the same typed history record that #8138 will introduce?\n@lorenzejay Since #8253 now covers #8138, here is how I plan to tackle this one. Its history record carries only metadata, so this lookup fills in the state for a listed row.\n\n- Add `SQLiteFlowPersistence.load_state_from_history(flow_uuid, record_id)`, returning `dict[str, Any] | None` like `load_state`.\n- Match on both the row id and the flow UUID with bound parameters, so a row from another flow is never returned. Missing rows and non-dict JSON return None, as in `load_state`.\n- Build it on main independently of #8253 and rebase if that merges first.\n- Keep it SQLite-only, with no base-class hook and no read-only module-level variant for #8140. Those can follow once #8253 settles.\n- Tests in `test_flow_persistence.py` for nested state, missing ids, multiple flows and `load_state` regression. No docs changes.\n\nI plan to draft PR along these lines, but please let me know if you'd prefer otherwise.", "created_at": "2026-10-19T07:14:08Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8269, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8269", "issue_numbers": ["8268"], "base_commit": "ecddbf2af7255c67f65853a24a7d661274b4102f", "patch": "diff --git a/lib/cli/src/crewai_cli/checkpoint_cli.py b/lib/cli/src/crewai_cli/checkpoint_cli.py\nindex 16a6a30562..a9ce23dec4 100644\n--- a/lib/cli/src/crewai_cli/checkpoint_cli.py\n+++ b/lib/cli/src/crewai_cli/checkpoint_cli.py\n@@ -239,7 +239,7 @@ def _entity_summary(entities: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> str:\n \n \n def _list_json(location: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n-    pattern = os.path.join(location, \"**\", \"*.json\")\n+    pattern = os.path.join(glob.escape(location), \"**\", \"*.json\")\n     results = []\n     for path in sorted(\n         glob.glob(pattern, recursive=True), key=os.path.getmtime, reverse=True\n@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@ def _list_json(location: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n \n \n def _info_json_latest(location: str) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n-    pattern = os.path.join(location, \"**\", \"*.json\")\n+    pattern = os.path.join(glob.escape(location), \"**\", \"*.json\")\n     files = sorted(\n         glob.glob(pattern, recursive=True), key=os.path.getmtime, reverse=True\n     )\n@@ -456,7 +456,7 @@ def _resolve_checkpoint(\n             from crewai.state.provider.json_provider import JsonProvider\n \n             _json_provider: JsonProvider = JsonProvider()\n-            pattern: str = os.path.join(location, \"**\", \"*.json\")\n+            pattern: str = os.path.join(glob.escape(location), \"**\", \"*.json\")\n             all_files: list[str] = glob.glob(pattern, recursive=True)\n             matches: list[str] = [\n                 f for f in all_files if checkpoint_id in _json_provider.extract_id(f)\n@@ -647,7 +647,7 @@ def _parse_duration(value: str) -> timedelta:\n \n \n def _prune_json(location: str, keep: int | None, older_than: timedelta | None) -> int:\n-    pattern: str = os.path.join(location, \"**\", \"*.json\")\n+    pattern: str = os.path.join(glob.escape(location), \"**\", \"*.json\")\n     files: list[str] = sorted(\n         glob.glob(pattern, recursive=True), key=os.path.getmtime, reverse=True\n     )\n@@ -725,7 +725,7 @@ def prune_checkpoints(\n     elif os.path.isdir(location):\n         if dry_run:\n             files: list[str] = glob.glob(\n-                os.path.join(location, \"**\", \"*.json\"), recursive=True\n+                os.path.join(glob.escape(location), \"**\", \"*.json\"), recursive=True\n             )\n             click.echo(f\"Would prune from {len(files)} checkpoint(s) in {location}\")\n             return\ndiff --git a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/state/provider/json_provider.py b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/state/provider/json_provider.py\nindex 93556f0e3f..c81851fcba 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/src/crewai/state/provider/json_provider.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/src/crewai/state/provider/json_provider.py\n@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@ def prune(self, location: str, max_keep: int, *, branch: str = \"main\") -> int:\n         \"\"\"Remove oldest checkpoint files beyond *max_keep* on a branch.\"\"\"\n         _safe_branch(location, branch)\n         branch_dir = os.path.join(location, branch)\n-        pattern = os.path.join(branch_dir, \"*.json\")\n+        pattern = os.path.join(glob.escape(branch_dir), \"*.json\")\n         files = sorted(glob.glob(pattern), key=os.path.getmtime)\n         removed = 0\n         for path in files if max_keep == 0 else files[:-max_keep]:\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_checkpoint.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_checkpoint.py\nindex 8bd43e3e79..dae9768c92 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/test_checkpoint.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_checkpoint.py\n@@ -120,6 +120,34 @@ def test_unknown_source(self) -> None:\n \n \n class TestPrune:\n+    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+        (\"directory\", \"branch\"),\n+        [(\"checkpoints[1]\", \"main\"), (\"checkpoints\", \"run[1]\"), (\"checkpoints\", \"fork/run[1]\")],\n+    )\n+    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"max_keep\", [0, 1])\n+    def test_prune_treats_directory_and_branch_as_literal_paths(\n+        self, tmp_path: Path, directory: str, branch: str, max_keep: int\n+    ) -> None:\n+        provider = JsonProvider()\n+        location = str(tmp_path / directory)\n+        paths = []\n+        for i in range(2):\n+            path = Path(provider.checkpoint(\"{}\", location, branch=branch))\n+            os.utime(path, (i + 1, i + 1))\n+            paths.append(path)\n+        # As a glob pattern, \"[1]\" matches \"1\", so this path must not be pruned\n+        other_path = Path(\n+            provider.checkpoint(\n+                \"{}\",\n+                str(tmp_path / directory.replace(\"[1]\", \"1\")),\n+                branch=branch.replace(\"[1]\", \"1\"),\n+            )\n+        )\n+\n+        assert provider.prune(location, max_keep=max_keep, branch=branch) == 2 - max_keep\n+        assert [path for path in paths if path.exists()] == (paths[-1:] if max_keep else [])\n+        assert other_path.exists()\n+\n     def test_prune_keeps_newest(self) -> None:\n         with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n             branch_dir = os.path.join(d, \"main\")\ndiff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_checkpoint_cli.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_checkpoint_cli.py\nindex 5007ba5579..764816362d 100644\n--- a/lib/crewai/tests/test_checkpoint_cli.py\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_checkpoint_cli.py\n@@ -169,6 +169,24 @@ def test_json_not_found(self) -> None:\n             _write_json_checkpoint(d)\n             assert _resolve_checkpoint(d, \"nonexistent\") is None\n \n+    def test_json_location_with_glob_characters(self) -> None:\n+        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n+            location = os.path.join(d, \"runs[1]\")\n+            path = _write_json_checkpoint(\n+                location, name=\"20260101T000000_aaaa1111_p-none.json\"\n+            )\n+            # As a glob pattern, \"runs[1]\" matches this directory instead\n+            _write_json_checkpoint(\n+                os.path.join(d, \"runs1\"), name=\"20260102T000000_bbbb2222_p-none.json\"\n+            )\n+            assert [item[\"path\"] for item in _list_json(location)] == [path]\n+            meta = _resolve_checkpoint(location, None)\n+            assert meta is not None\n+            assert meta[\"path\"] == path\n+            meta = _resolve_checkpoint(location, \"aaaa1111\")\n+            assert meta is not None\n+            assert meta[\"path\"] == path\n+\n     def test_sqlite_latest(self) -> None:\n         with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n             db_path = os.path.join(d, \"test.db\")\n@@ -355,6 +373,28 @@ def test_removes_empty_branch_dirs(self) -> None:\n             _prune_json(d, keep=None, older_than=timedelta(days=1))\n             assert not os.path.exists(os.path.join(d, \"feature\"))\n \n+    def test_location_with_glob_characters(\n+        self, capsys: pytest.CaptureFixture[str]\n+    ) -> None:\n+        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n+            location = os.path.join(d, \"runs[1]\")\n+            path = _write_json_checkpoint(\n+                location, name=\"20260101T000000_aaaa1111_p-none.json\"\n+            )\n+            # As a glob pattern, \"runs[1]\" matches this directory instead\n+            others = [\n+                _write_json_checkpoint(\n+                    os.path.join(d, \"runs1\"),\n+                    name=f\"2026010{i + 2}T000000_bbbb{i}222_p-none.json\",\n+                )\n+                for i in range(2)\n+            ]\n+            prune_checkpoints(location, keep=0, older_than=None, dry_run=True)\n+            assert \"Would prune from 1 checkpoint(s)\" in capsys.readouterr().out\n+            assert _prune_json(location, keep=0, older_than=None) == 1\n+            assert not os.path.exists(path)\n+            assert all(os.path.exists(other) for other in others)\n+\n \n class TestPruneSqlite:\n     def test_keep_n(self) -> None:\n", "problem_statement": "[BUG] Checkpoint paths with glob characters prune and list the wrong checkpoints\n### Description\n\n`JsonProvider.prune()` and the checkpoint CLI build a glob pattern from the checkpoint location (and branch) without escaping it. When the path contains glob characters such as `[1]`, the pattern matches a different directory. For the branch `run[1]`, `prune()` deletes the checkpoints of `run1` and keeps the ones of `run[1]`. `crewai checkpoint list`, `info` and `prune` read the wrong directory in the same way.\n\n`prune()` also runs automatically after each checkpoint when `CheckpointConfig.max_checkpoints` is set.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Save a checkpoint on the branch `run[1]` and one on the branch `run1` with `JsonProvider`.\n2. Prune the branch `run[1]` with `max_keep=0`.\n3. Check which checkpoint still exists.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe checkpoint on `run[1]` is removed and the checkpoint on `run1` is kept.\n\n### Screenshots/Code snippets\n\n```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tempfile import TemporaryDirectory\n\nfrom crewai.state.provider.json_provider import JsonProvider\n\nprovider = JsonProvider()\nwith TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n    requested = Path(provider.checkpoint(\"{}\", directory, branch=\"run[1]\"))\n    neighbor = Path(provider.checkpoint(\"{}\", directory, branch=\"run1\"))\n    provider.prune(directory, max_keep=0, branch=\"run[1]\")\n    print(\"requested exists:\", requested.exists())\n    print(\"neighbor exists:\", neighbor.exists())\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\nrequested exists: True\nneighbor exists: False\n```\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS 26.3\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.13\n\n### crewAI Version\n\n1.15.28 (main at 40bb2d3)\n\n### crewAI Tools Version\n\nNot used.\n\n### Virtual Environment\n\nVenv (uv)\n\n### Evidence\n\nThe snippet above shows that the checkpoint on `run[1]` is kept and the checkpoint on `run1` is deleted.\n\nThe CLI has the same problem. With a directory `runs[1]` that has 1 checkpoint next to a directory `runs1` that has 2 checkpoints:\n\n```\n$ crewai checkpoint list runs[1]\nFound 2 checkpoint(s) in runs[1]\n$ crewai checkpoint --location runs[1] prune --keep 0\nPruned 2 checkpoint(s) from runs[1]\n```\n\nAfter this, the checkpoint in `runs[1]` still exists and the 2 checkpoints in `runs1` are deleted.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nEscape the directory part with `glob.escape()` before adding the file pattern, for example in `JsonProvider.prune()`:\n\n```python\npattern = os.path.join(glob.escape(branch_dir), \"*.json\")\n```\n\nThe five `os.path.join(location, \"**\", \"*.json\")` patterns in `crewai_cli/checkpoint_cli.py` need the same change. I have a fix with tests and can open a PR.\n\n### Additional context\n\nThis issue was prepared with AI assistance. I can't add labels, so could a maintainer please add `llm-generated`?\n\n\n", "hints_text": "", "created_at": "2026-10-19T00:15:46Z"}
{"repo": "crewAIInc/crewAI", "pull_number": 8230, "instance_id": "crewAIInc__crewAI-8230", "issue_numbers": ["8124"], "base_commit": "9c24fda7f48875a362762f444d7f2ea62618a3b2", "patch": "diff --git a/scripts/jev_evaluation_runner.py b/scripts/jev_evaluation_runner.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..c5ba02d9f7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/scripts/jev_evaluation_runner.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,602 @@\n+# ruff: noqa: T201\n+\"\"\"Offline evaluation of Jev routing (Choice) and guardrail (Noul) decisions.\n+\n+Usage:\n+    uv run python scripts/jev_evaluation_runner.py examples.jsonl \\\\\n+        --min-confidence 0.7 --noul-threshold 0.8 [--route billing --route tech]\n+\n+The dataset is a .jsonl file (one record per line; blank lines are skipped) or\n+a .json array, read as UTF-8 with an optional BOM. Malformed JSON, unknown\n+fields, and missing or duplicate ids are reported with the line or index:\n+\n+    {\"id\": \"r1\", \"kind\": \"route\", \"state\": \"Refund for order 1234\", \"expected_route\": \"billing\", \"decision\": {\"choice\": \"billing\", \"confidence\": 0.91, \"probabilities\": {\"billing\": 0.95, \"tech\": 0.05}}}\n+    {\"id\": \"g1\", \"kind\": \"guardrail\", \"state\": \"Paris is the capital of France.\", \"expected\": \"accept\", \"decision\": {\"noul\": 0.97}}\n+\n+Route records have expected_route; guardrail records have expected (\"accept\"\n+or \"reject\"). Both can have an error (a recorded failure) and metadata (model,\n+usage, latency_ms). The report is printed as JSON.\n+\n+A record fails if it has a recorded error, no decision, or a malformed decision\n+(a missing field, or a value that isn't a finite number in [0, 1]); a route\n+also fails if its choice isn't a known route (every expected_route in the\n+dataset, or the --route values). Failed records are never counted as correct or\n+accepted. Routes with confidence >= min_confidence are decided (correct or\n+incorrect), lower ones abstain; guardrails with noul >= noul_threshold are\n+accepted, lower ones rejected. Choice confidence and Noul probability are never\n+converted into each other.\n+\n+- routing accuracy / coverage / abstention_rate: correct / decided / abstained\n+  over all route records.\n+- guardrail false_accept_rate / false_reject_rate: accepted / rejected over\n+  decided records expected to be rejected / accepted.\n+- usage, latency: token sums and mean latency_ms over only the records that\n+  report them.\n+\n+A rate is null when its denominator is 0. These are decision-quality metrics,\n+not a replay of a runtime guardrail: a guardrail that rejects when the answer\n+is missing or the call fails would count those cases as rejections, while here\n+they are failed and left out of the false-accept and false-reject rates.\n+\n+Live collection is opt-in and needs your own TypeSafe client, which you close:\n+\n+    with TypeSafeClient(api_key=\"...\") as client:\n+        records = collect_live_decisions(\n+            load_dataset(\"unlabeled.jsonl\"),\n+            client=client,\n+            route_instructions=\"Which team should handle this ticket?\",\n+            route_criteria={\"billing\": \"Payments\", \"tech\": \"Bugs and outages\"},\n+            guardrail_instructions=\"Is this statement true?\",\n+        )\n+\n+It times each call, stores client errors on the record (which then fails), and\n+fails an answer whose type doesn't match the question. The type is not stored,\n+so recorded decisions are checked by their fields only.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import argparse\n+from collections import Counter\n+from collections.abc import Collection, Mapping, Sequence\n+import json\n+from pathlib import Path\n+import time\n+from typing import Annotated, Any, Literal, Protocol\n+\n+from pydantic import (\n+    BaseModel,\n+    ConfigDict,\n+    Field,\n+    TypeAdapter,\n+    ValidationError,\n+)\n+\n+\n+Probability = Annotated[float, Field(ge=0.0, le=1.0, allow_inf_nan=False)]\n+_THRESHOLD: TypeAdapter[float] = TypeAdapter(\n+    Probability, config=ConfigDict(strict=True)\n+)\n+\n+ROUTE_QUESTION = \"route\"\n+GUARDRAIL_QUESTION = \"guardrail\"\n+\n+\n+class ChoiceDecision(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"A Jev Choice answer, mirroring the SDK's ``ChoiceAnswer`` fields.\"\"\"\n+\n+    model_config = ConfigDict(strict=True, extra=\"ignore\")\n+\n+    choice: str\n+    confidence: Probability\n+    probabilities: dict[str, Probability]\n+\n+\n+class NoulDecision(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"A Jev Noul answer: the probability that the question is true.\"\"\"\n+\n+    model_config = ConfigDict(strict=True, extra=\"ignore\")\n+\n+    noul: Probability\n+\n+\n+class TokenUsage(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"Token counts as reported by the SDK; ``None`` means not reported.\"\"\"\n+\n+    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\")\n+\n+    input_tokens: int | None = Field(default=None, ge=0)\n+    output_tokens: int | None = Field(default=None, ge=0)\n+\n+\n+class DecisionMetadata(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"Request metadata kept only when it was actually recorded.\"\"\"\n+\n+    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\")\n+\n+    model: str | None = None\n+    usage: TokenUsage | None = None\n+    latency_ms: float | None = Field(default=None, ge=0.0, allow_inf_nan=False)\n+\n+\n+class _BaseRecord(BaseModel):\n+    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\")\n+\n+    id: str = Field(min_length=1)\n+    state: Any\n+    decision: dict[str, Any] | None = None\n+    error: str | None = None\n+    metadata: DecisionMetadata | None = None\n+\n+\n+class RouteRecord(_BaseRecord):\n+    \"\"\"A labeled routing example with an optional recorded Choice decision.\"\"\"\n+\n+    kind: Literal[\"route\"]\n+    expected_route: str = Field(min_length=1)\n+\n+\n+class GuardrailRecord(_BaseRecord):\n+    \"\"\"A labeled guardrail example with an optional recorded Noul decision.\"\"\"\n+\n+    kind: Literal[\"guardrail\"]\n+    expected: Literal[\"accept\", \"reject\"]\n+\n+\n+EvaluationRecord = Annotated[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord, Field(discriminator=\"kind\")]\n+_RECORD_ADAPTER: TypeAdapter[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord] = TypeAdapter(\n+    EvaluationRecord\n+)\n+\n+Outcome = Literal[\"correct\", \"incorrect\", \"abstained\", \"accepted\", \"rejected\", \"failed\"]\n+\n+\n+class RecordOutcome(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"How a single record was classified, and why.\"\"\"\n+\n+    id: str\n+    kind: Literal[\"route\", \"guardrail\"]\n+    outcome: Outcome\n+    reason: str\n+\n+\n+class RoutingReport(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"Routing counts and rates; every rate is over all routing records.\"\"\"\n+\n+    total: int\n+    decided: int\n+    abstained: int\n+    failed: int\n+    correct: int\n+    accuracy: float | None\n+    coverage: float | None\n+    abstention_rate: float | None\n+\n+\n+class GuardrailReport(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"Guardrail counts; error rates are over decided records only.\"\"\"\n+\n+    total: int\n+    decided: int\n+    failed: int\n+    accepted: int\n+    rejected: int\n+    false_accepts: int\n+    false_accept_denominator: int\n+    false_accept_rate: float | None\n+    false_rejects: int\n+    false_reject_denominator: int\n+    false_reject_rate: float | None\n+\n+\n+class UsageSummary(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"Token totals over the records that reported each count.\"\"\"\n+\n+    input_tokens: int\n+    input_token_records: int\n+    output_tokens: int\n+    output_token_records: int\n+\n+\n+class LatencySummary(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"Mean latency over records with a measured latency.\"\"\"\n+\n+    count: int\n+    mean_ms: float | None\n+\n+\n+class EvaluationReport(BaseModel):\n+    \"\"\"Full evaluation result.\"\"\"\n+\n+    routing: RoutingReport\n+    guardrail: GuardrailReport\n+    usage: UsageSummary\n+    latency: LatencySummary\n+    outcomes: list[RecordOutcome]\n+\n+\n+class SystemOneClient(Protocol):\n+    \"\"\"The part of the TypeSafe client used for live collection.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def system_one(\n+        self, state: Any, questions: Mapping[str, Any], *, model: str | None = None\n+    ) -> Any:\n+        \"\"\"Answer the named questions about ``state``.\"\"\"\n+        ...\n+\n+\n+def load_dataset(path: str | Path) -> list[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord]:\n+    \"\"\"Load and validate records from a ``.jsonl`` or ``.json`` file.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        path: A ``.jsonl`` file (one record per line; blank lines are skipped)\n+            or a ``.json`` file containing an array of records.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        The validated records, in file order.\n+\n+    Raises:\n+        ValueError: If the file or any record is malformed.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    path = Path(path)\n+    text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n+    if path.suffix == \".jsonl\":\n+        items = _parse_jsonl(text)\n+    elif path.suffix == \".json\":\n+        try:\n+            data = json.loads(text)\n+        except ValueError as e:\n+            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid JSON: {e}\") from e\n+        if not isinstance(data, list):\n+            raise ValueError(\"A .json dataset must be an array of records\")\n+        items = [(f\"index {i}\", item) for i, item in enumerate(data)]\n+    else:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported dataset extension: {path.suffix!r}\")\n+\n+    records: list[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord] = []\n+    seen: set[str] = set()\n+    for location, item in items:\n+        try:\n+            record = _RECORD_ADAPTER.validate_python(item)\n+        except ValidationError as e:\n+            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid record at {location}: {e}\") from e\n+        if record.id in seen:\n+            raise ValueError(f\"Duplicate record id {record.id!r} at {location}\")\n+        seen.add(record.id)\n+        records.append(record)\n+    return records\n+\n+\n+def evaluate(\n+    records: Sequence[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord],\n+    *,\n+    min_confidence: float,\n+    noul_threshold: float,\n+    routes: Collection[str] | None = None,\n+) -> EvaluationReport:\n+    \"\"\"Classify every record and compute routing and guardrail metrics.\n+\n+    Both thresholds are inclusive: a Choice confidence equal to\n+    ``min_confidence`` is decided, and a Noul probability equal to\n+    ``noul_threshold`` is accepted.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        records: Records to evaluate.\n+        min_confidence: Minimum Choice confidence for a route to be decided.\n+        noul_threshold: Minimum Noul probability for an output to be accepted.\n+        routes: Known route labels. Defaults to every ``expected_route``.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        Counts, rates, usage, latency, and a per-record outcome with its reason.\n+\n+    Raises:\n+        ValueError: If a threshold is not a finite number in [0, 1].\n+    \"\"\"\n+    _validate_threshold(\"min_confidence\", min_confidence)\n+    _validate_threshold(\"noul_threshold\", noul_threshold)\n+    route_records = [r for r in records if isinstance(r, RouteRecord)]\n+    known_routes = (\n+        set(routes) if routes is not None else {r.expected_route for r in route_records}\n+    )\n+\n+    outcomes: list[RecordOutcome] = []\n+    false_accepts = false_rejects = fa_denominator = fr_denominator = 0\n+    for record in records:\n+        if isinstance(record, RouteRecord):\n+            outcome, reason = _classify_route(record, known_routes, min_confidence)\n+        else:\n+            outcome, reason = _classify_guardrail(record, noul_threshold)\n+            if outcome != \"failed\" and record.expected == \"reject\":\n+                fa_denominator += 1\n+                if outcome == \"accepted\":\n+                    false_accepts += 1\n+            elif outcome != \"failed\":\n+                fr_denominator += 1\n+                if outcome == \"rejected\":\n+                    false_rejects += 1\n+        outcomes.append(\n+            RecordOutcome(\n+                id=record.id, kind=record.kind, outcome=outcome, reason=reason\n+            )\n+        )\n+\n+    route_counts = Counter(o.outcome for o in outcomes if o.kind == \"route\")\n+    guard_counts = Counter(o.outcome for o in outcomes if o.kind == \"guardrail\")\n+    route_total = len(route_records)\n+    route_decided = route_counts[\"correct\"] + route_counts[\"incorrect\"]\n+    guard_total = len(records) - route_total\n+    return EvaluationReport(\n+        routing=RoutingReport(\n+            total=route_total,\n+            decided=route_decided,\n+            abstained=route_counts[\"abstained\"],\n+            failed=route_counts[\"failed\"],\n+            correct=route_counts[\"correct\"],\n+            accuracy=_rate(route_counts[\"correct\"], route_total),\n+            coverage=_rate(route_decided, route_total),\n+            abstention_rate=_rate(route_counts[\"abstained\"], route_total),\n+        ),\n+        guardrail=GuardrailReport(\n+            total=guard_total,\n+            decided=guard_total - guard_counts[\"failed\"],\n+            failed=guard_counts[\"failed\"],\n+            accepted=guard_counts[\"accepted\"],\n+            rejected=guard_counts[\"rejected\"],\n+            false_accepts=false_accepts,\n+            false_accept_denominator=fa_denominator,\n+            false_accept_rate=_rate(false_accepts, fa_denominator),\n+            false_rejects=false_rejects,\n+            false_reject_denominator=fr_denominator,\n+            false_reject_rate=_rate(false_rejects, fr_denominator),\n+        ),\n+        usage=_summarize_usage(records),\n+        latency=_summarize_latency(records),\n+        outcomes=outcomes,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def collect_live_decisions(\n+    records: Sequence[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord],\n+    *,\n+    client: SystemOneClient,\n+    route_instructions: str,\n+    route_criteria: Mapping[str, str],\n+    guardrail_instructions: str,\n+    model: str | None = None,\n+) -> list[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord]:\n+    \"\"\"Ask Jev for each record that has no recorded decision or error.\n+\n+    Opt-in: the caller supplies a client built with their own credentials,\n+    and remains responsible for closing it. Client errors are recorded on the\n+    record (which then evaluates as failed) instead of stopping the run.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        records: Records to complete; those with a decision or error are kept as is.\n+        client: A TypeSafe client, or any object with a compatible ``system_one``.\n+        route_instructions: Instructions for the Choice question on route records.\n+        route_criteria: Route labels mapped to their descriptions.\n+        guardrail_instructions: Instructions for the Noul question on guardrail records.\n+        model: Optional Jev model name passed to the client.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        The records with decisions, latency, and usage filled in where collected.\n+\n+    Raises:\n+        ValueError: If instructions are blank or ``route_criteria`` is empty.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if not route_instructions.strip() or not guardrail_instructions.strip():\n+        raise ValueError(\"route_instructions and guardrail_instructions are required\")\n+    if not route_criteria:\n+        raise ValueError(\"route_criteria must not be empty\")\n+\n+    collected: list[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord] = []\n+    for record in records:\n+        if record.decision is not None or record.error is not None:\n+            collected.append(record)\n+            continue\n+        if isinstance(record, RouteRecord):\n+            name = ROUTE_QUESTION\n+            question: dict[str, Any] = {\n+                \"type\": \"choice\",\n+                \"instructions\": route_instructions,\n+                \"criteria\": dict(route_criteria),\n+            }\n+        else:\n+            name = GUARDRAIL_QUESTION\n+            question = {\"type\": \"noul\", \"instructions\": guardrail_instructions}\n+        collected.append(_query(record, client, name, question, model))\n+    return collected\n+\n+\n+def _query(\n+    record: RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord,\n+    client: SystemOneClient,\n+    name: str,\n+    question: dict[str, Any],\n+    model: str | None,\n+) -> RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord:\n+    start = time.perf_counter()\n+    try:\n+        response = client.system_one(record.state, {name: question}, model=model)\n+    except Exception as e:\n+        return record.model_copy(update={\"error\": f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\"})\n+    latency_ms = (time.perf_counter() - start) * 1000\n+\n+    usage = getattr(response, \"usage\", None)\n+    response_model = getattr(response, \"model\", None)\n+    metadata = DecisionMetadata(\n+        model=response_model if isinstance(response_model, str) else None,\n+        latency_ms=latency_ms,\n+    )\n+    if usage is not None:\n+        try:\n+            metadata.usage = TokenUsage.model_validate(usage, from_attributes=True)\n+        except ValidationError as e:\n+            first = e.errors()[0]\n+            location = \".\".join(str(part) for part in first[\"loc\"]) or \"usage\"\n+            return record.model_copy(\n+                update={\n+                    \"error\": f\"invalid usage: {location}: {first['msg']}\",\n+                    \"metadata\": metadata,\n+                }\n+            )\n+    answers = getattr(response, \"answers\", None)\n+    answer = answers.get(name) if isinstance(answers, Mapping) else None\n+    if answer is None:\n+        return record.model_copy(\n+            update={\"error\": f\"no answer returned for {name!r}\", \"metadata\": metadata}\n+        )\n+    answer_type = getattr(answer, \"type\", None)\n+    if answer_type is not None and answer_type != question[\"type\"]:\n+        return record.model_copy(\n+            update={\n+                \"error\": f\"expected a {question['type']!r} answer for {name!r},\"\n+                f\" got {answer_type!r}\",\n+                \"metadata\": metadata,\n+            }\n+        )\n+    if isinstance(record, RouteRecord):\n+        probabilities = getattr(answer, \"probabilities\", None)\n+        if probabilities is None:\n+            probabilities = {}\n+        elif isinstance(probabilities, Mapping):\n+            probabilities = dict(probabilities)\n+        decision = {\n+            \"choice\": getattr(answer, \"choice\", None),\n+            \"confidence\": getattr(answer, \"confidence\", None),\n+            \"probabilities\": probabilities,\n+        }\n+    else:\n+        decision = {\"noul\": getattr(answer, \"noul\", None)}\n+    return record.model_copy(update={\"decision\": decision, \"metadata\": metadata})\n+\n+\n+def _parse_decision(\n+    record: RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord,\n+    model: type[ChoiceDecision] | type[NoulDecision],\n+) -> tuple[ChoiceDecision | NoulDecision | None, str]:\n+    \"\"\"Return the validated decision, or ``None`` and the failure reason.\"\"\"\n+    if record.error is not None:\n+        return None, f\"recorded error: {record.error}\"\n+    if record.decision is None:\n+        return None, \"missing decision\"\n+    try:\n+        return model.model_validate(record.decision), \"\"\n+    except ValidationError as e:\n+        first = e.errors()[0]\n+        location = \".\".join(str(part) for part in first[\"loc\"]) or \"decision\"\n+        return None, f\"invalid {model.__name__}: {location}: {first['msg']}\"\n+\n+\n+def _classify_route(\n+    record: RouteRecord, known_routes: set[str], min_confidence: float\n+) -> tuple[Outcome, str]:\n+    decision, reason = _parse_decision(record, ChoiceDecision)\n+    if not isinstance(decision, ChoiceDecision):\n+        return \"failed\", reason\n+    if decision.choice not in known_routes:\n+        return \"failed\", f\"choice {decision.choice!r} is not a known route\"\n+    if decision.confidence < min_confidence:\n+        return (\n+            \"abstained\",\n+            f\"confidence {decision.confidence} below min_confidence {min_confidence}\",\n+        )\n+    outcome: Outcome = (\n+        \"correct\" if decision.choice == record.expected_route else \"incorrect\"\n+    )\n+    return (\n+        outcome,\n+        f\"confidence {decision.confidence} meets min_confidence {min_confidence}\",\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def _classify_guardrail(\n+    record: GuardrailRecord, noul_threshold: float\n+) -> tuple[Outcome, str]:\n+    decision, reason = _parse_decision(record, NoulDecision)\n+    if not isinstance(decision, NoulDecision):\n+        return \"failed\", reason\n+    if decision.noul >= noul_threshold:\n+        return \"accepted\", f\"noul {decision.noul} meets threshold {noul_threshold}\"\n+    return \"rejected\", f\"noul {decision.noul} below threshold {noul_threshold}\"\n+\n+\n+def _summarize_usage(records: Sequence[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord]) -> UsageSummary:\n+    usages = [r.metadata.usage for r in records if r.metadata and r.metadata.usage]\n+    inputs = [u.input_tokens for u in usages if u.input_tokens is not None]\n+    outputs = [u.output_tokens for u in usages if u.output_tokens is not None]\n+    return UsageSummary(\n+        input_tokens=sum(inputs),\n+        input_token_records=len(inputs),\n+        output_tokens=sum(outputs),\n+        output_token_records=len(outputs),\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def _summarize_latency(\n+    records: Sequence[RouteRecord | GuardrailRecord],\n+) -> LatencySummary:\n+    values = [\n+        r.metadata.latency_ms\n+        for r in records\n+        if r.metadata and r.metadata.latency_ms is not None\n+    ]\n+    return LatencySummary(\n+        count=len(values), mean_ms=sum(values) / len(values) if values else None\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def _parse_jsonl(text: str) -> list[tuple[str, Any]]:\n+    items: list[tuple[str, Any]] = []\n+    for number, line in enumerate(text.split(\"\\n\"), start=1):\n+        if not line.strip():\n+            continue\n+        try:\n+            items.append((f\"line {number}\", json.loads(line)))\n+        except ValueError as e:\n+            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid JSONL at line {number}: {e}\") from e\n+    return items\n+\n+\n+def _validate_threshold(name: str, value: float) -> None:\n+    try:\n+        _THRESHOLD.validate_python(value)\n+    except ValidationError as e:\n+        raise ValueError(\n+            f\"{name} must be a finite number in [0, 1], got {value!r}\"\n+        ) from e\n+\n+\n+def _rate(numerator: int, denominator: int) -> float | None:\n+    return numerator / denominator if denominator else None\n+\n+\n+def main(argv: Sequence[str] | None = None) -> int:\n+    \"\"\"Evaluate a dataset file and print the report as JSON.\"\"\"\n+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n+        description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter\n+    )\n+    parser.add_argument(\"dataset\", type=Path, help=\"a .jsonl or .json file\")\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--min-confidence\", type=float, required=True)\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--noul-threshold\", type=float, required=True)\n+    parser.add_argument(\n+        \"--route\",\n+        action=\"append\",\n+        dest=\"routes\",\n+        help=\"a known route; repeat for each (default: every expected_route)\",\n+    )\n+    args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n+    try:\n+        report = evaluate(\n+            load_dataset(args.dataset),\n+            min_confidence=args.min_confidence,\n+            noul_threshold=args.noul_threshold,\n+            routes=args.routes,\n+        )\n+    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:\n+        parser.error(str(e))\n+    print(report.model_dump_json(indent=2))\n+    return 0\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    raise SystemExit(main())\n", "test_patch": "diff --git a/lib/crewai/tests/test_jev_evaluation_runner.py b/lib/crewai/tests/test_jev_evaluation_runner.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000..9ca829461c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/lib/crewai/tests/test_jev_evaluation_runner.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,655 @@\n+\"\"\"Offline checks for the Jev routing and guardrail evaluation runner.\"\"\"\n+\n+import importlib.util\n+import json\n+from pathlib import Path\n+import sys\n+from types import SimpleNamespace\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+\n+def _load_runner():\n+    path = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3] / \"scripts\" / \"jev_evaluation_runner.py\"\n+    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"jev_evaluation_runner\", path)\n+    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n+    sys.modules[spec.name] = module\n+    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n+    return module\n+\n+\n+runner = _load_runner()\n+GuardrailRecord = runner.GuardrailRecord\n+RouteRecord = runner.RouteRecord\n+collect_live_decisions = runner.collect_live_decisions\n+evaluate = runner.evaluate\n+load_dataset = runner.load_dataset\n+\n+\n+EXAMPLE = [\n+    {\n+        \"id\": \"r1\",\n+        \"kind\": \"route\",\n+        \"state\": \"Refund for order 1234\",\n+        \"expected_route\": \"billing\",\n+        \"decision\": {\n+            \"choice\": \"billing\",\n+            \"confidence\": 0.91,\n+            \"probabilities\": {\"billing\": 0.95, \"tech\": 0.05},\n+        },\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+            \"latency_ms\": 212.0,\n+            \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 40, \"output_tokens\": 1},\n+        },\n+    },\n+    {\n+        \"id\": \"r2\",\n+        \"kind\": \"route\",\n+        \"state\": \"App crashes on login\",\n+        \"expected_route\": \"tech\",\n+        \"decision\": {\n+            \"choice\": \"tech\",\n+            \"confidence\": 0.62,\n+            \"probabilities\": {\"billing\": 0.19, \"tech\": 0.81},\n+        },\n+    },\n+    {\n+        \"id\": \"r3\",\n+        \"kind\": \"route\",\n+        \"state\": \"Change my plan\",\n+        \"expected_route\": \"billing\",\n+        \"decision\": {\n+            \"choice\": \"tech\",\n+            \"confidence\": 0.88,\n+            \"probabilities\": {\"billing\": 0.06, \"tech\": 0.94},\n+        },\n+    },\n+    {\n+        \"id\": \"r4\",\n+        \"kind\": \"route\",\n+        \"state\": \"Where is my invoice?\",\n+        \"expected_route\": \"billing\",\n+        \"decision\": None,\n+        \"error\": \"TypeSafeAPITimeoutError: request timed out\",\n+    },\n+    {\n+        \"id\": \"g1\",\n+        \"kind\": \"guardrail\",\n+        \"state\": \"Paris is the capital of France.\",\n+        \"expected\": \"accept\",\n+        \"decision\": {\"noul\": 0.97},\n+    },\n+    {\n+        \"id\": \"g2\",\n+        \"kind\": \"guardrail\",\n+        \"state\": \"The moon is made of cheese.\",\n+        \"expected\": \"reject\",\n+        \"decision\": {\"noul\": 0.8},\n+    },\n+    {\n+        \"id\": \"g3\",\n+        \"kind\": \"guardrail\",\n+        \"state\": \"Water boils at 100 C at sea level.\",\n+        \"expected\": \"accept\",\n+        \"decision\": {\"noul\": 0.79},\n+    },\n+    {\n+        \"id\": \"g4\",\n+        \"kind\": \"guardrail\",\n+        \"state\": \"2 + 2 = 5\",\n+        \"expected\": \"reject\",\n+        \"decision\": {\"noul\": 1.4},\n+    },\n+]\n+\n+\n+def write_jsonl(tmp_path, records, name=\"data.jsonl\"):\n+    path = tmp_path / name\n+    path.write_text(\"\".join(json.dumps(r) + \"\\n\" for r in records), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    return path\n+\n+\n+def route(decision, expected=\"billing\", **extra):\n+    return RouteRecord(\n+        id=\"r\",\n+        kind=\"route\",\n+        state=\"s\",\n+        expected_route=expected,\n+        decision=decision,\n+        **extra,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def guardrail(decision, expected=\"accept\", **extra):\n+    return GuardrailRecord(\n+        id=\"g\",\n+        kind=\"guardrail\",\n+        state=\"s\",\n+        expected=expected,\n+        decision=decision,\n+        **extra,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def outcome_of(record, **thresholds):\n+    kwargs = {\n+        \"min_confidence\": 0.7,\n+        \"noul_threshold\": 0.8,\n+        \"routes\": {\"billing\", \"tech\"},\n+    } | thresholds\n+    return evaluate([record], **kwargs).outcomes[0]\n+\n+\n+# Metric denominators\n+\n+\n+def test_example_dataset_report(tmp_path):\n+    report = evaluate(\n+        load_dataset(write_jsonl(tmp_path, EXAMPLE)),\n+        min_confidence=0.7,\n+        noul_threshold=0.8,\n+    )\n+\n+    assert report.routing.model_dump() == {\n+        \"total\": 4,\n+        \"decided\": 2,\n+        \"abstained\": 1,\n+        \"failed\": 1,\n+        \"correct\": 1,\n+        \"accuracy\": 0.25,\n+        \"coverage\": 0.5,\n+        \"abstention_rate\": 0.25,\n+    }\n+    assert report.guardrail.model_dump() == {\n+        \"total\": 4,\n+        \"decided\": 3,\n+        \"failed\": 1,\n+        \"accepted\": 2,\n+        \"rejected\": 1,\n+        \"false_accepts\": 1,\n+        \"false_accept_denominator\": 1,\n+        \"false_accept_rate\": 1.0,\n+        \"false_rejects\": 1,\n+        \"false_reject_denominator\": 2,\n+        \"false_reject_rate\": 0.5,\n+    }\n+    assert report.usage.model_dump() == {\n+        \"input_tokens\": 40,\n+        \"input_token_records\": 1,\n+        \"output_tokens\": 1,\n+        \"output_token_records\": 1,\n+    }\n+    assert report.latency.model_dump() == {\"count\": 1, \"mean_ms\": 212.0}\n+    assert [o.outcome for o in report.outcomes] == [\n+        \"correct\",\n+        \"abstained\",\n+        \"incorrect\",\n+        \"failed\",\n+        \"accepted\",\n+        \"accepted\",\n+        \"rejected\",\n+        \"failed\",\n+    ]\n+\n+\n+def test_failed_guardrails_are_excluded_from_false_rate_denominators():\n+    records = [\n+        guardrail(None, expected=\"reject\"),\n+        guardrail({\"noul\": 0.9}, expected=\"accept\"),\n+    ]\n+    report = evaluate(records, min_confidence=0.5, noul_threshold=0.8)\n+\n+    assert report.guardrail.failed == 1\n+    assert report.guardrail.false_accept_denominator == 0\n+    assert report.guardrail.false_accept_rate is None\n+    assert report.guardrail.false_reject_denominator == 1\n+    assert report.guardrail.false_reject_rate == 0.0\n+\n+\n+def test_empty_dataset_reports_none_rates():\n+    report = evaluate([], min_confidence=0.5, noul_threshold=0.5)\n+\n+    assert report.routing.accuracy is None\n+    assert report.routing.coverage is None\n+    assert report.guardrail.false_reject_rate is None\n+    assert report.latency.mean_ms is None\n+\n+\n+# Threshold boundaries\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    (\"confidence\", \"expected\"),\n+    [(0.69, \"abstained\"), (0.7, \"correct\"), (0.71, \"correct\")],\n+)\n+def test_choice_threshold_is_inclusive(confidence, expected):\n+    record = route({\"choice\": \"billing\", \"confidence\": confidence, \"probabilities\": {}})\n+\n+    assert outcome_of(record, min_confidence=0.7).outcome == expected\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    (\"noul\", \"threshold\", \"expected\"),\n+    [\n+        (0.79, 0.8, \"rejected\"),\n+        (0.8, 0.8, \"accepted\"),\n+        (0.81, 0.8, \"accepted\"),\n+        (0.0, 0.0, \"accepted\"),\n+        (1.0, 1.0, \"accepted\"),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_noul_threshold_is_inclusive(noul, threshold, expected):\n+    assert (\n+        outcome_of(guardrail({\"noul\": noul}), noul_threshold=threshold).outcome\n+        == expected\n+    )\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"bad\", [float(\"nan\"), float(\"inf\"), -0.1, 1.1, True, \"0.5\"])\n+def test_invalid_thresholds_raise(bad):\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"noul_threshold\"):\n+        evaluate([], min_confidence=0.5, noul_threshold=bad)\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"min_confidence\"):\n+        evaluate([], min_confidence=bad, noul_threshold=0.5)\n+\n+\n+# Missing and invalid decisions\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    (\"decision\", \"extra\", \"reason\"),\n+    [\n+        (None, {}, \"missing decision\"),\n+        (\n+            {\"choice\": \"billing\", \"confidence\": 0.9, \"probabilities\": {}},\n+            {\"error\": \"boom\"},\n+            \"recorded error: boom\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            {\"choice\": \"sales\", \"confidence\": 0.9, \"probabilities\": {}},\n+            {},\n+            \"not a known route\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            {\"choice\": \"billing\", \"confidence\": 1.2, \"probabilities\": {}},\n+            {},\n+            \"invalid ChoiceDecision: confidence\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            {\"choice\": \"billing\", \"confidence\": \"0.9\", \"probabilities\": {}},\n+            {},\n+            \"invalid ChoiceDecision: confidence\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            {\"choice\": \"billing\", \"probabilities\": {}},\n+            {},\n+            \"invalid ChoiceDecision: confidence\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            {\"choice\": \"billing\", \"confidence\": 0.9, \"probabilities\": {\"billing\": 1.5}},\n+            {},\n+            \"invalid ChoiceDecision: probabilities.billing\",\n+        ),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_unusable_route_decisions_fail(decision, extra, reason):\n+    result = outcome_of(route(decision, **extra))\n+\n+    assert result.outcome == \"failed\"\n+    assert reason in result.reason\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    \"decision\",\n+    [\n+        None,\n+        {\"noul\": -0.1},\n+        {\"noul\": 1.4},\n+        {\"noul\": True},\n+        {\"noul\": \"0.9\"},\n+        {\"confidence\": 0.9},\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_unusable_guardrail_decisions_fail_and_never_accept(decision):\n+    assert outcome_of(guardrail(decision, expected=\"reject\")).outcome == \"failed\"\n+\n+\n+def test_recorded_guardrail_error_fails_even_with_a_passing_decision():\n+    result = outcome_of(guardrail({\"noul\": 0.99}, error=\"boom\"))\n+\n+    assert (result.outcome, result.reason) == (\"failed\", \"recorded error: boom\")\n+\n+\n+def test_route_confidence_is_never_used_as_noul():\n+    record = guardrail(\n+        {\"choice\": \"accept\", \"confidence\": 0.99, \"probabilities\": {\"accept\": 1.0}}\n+    )\n+\n+    assert outcome_of(record).outcome == \"failed\"\n+\n+\n+# Invalid inputs\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    (\"lines\", \"message\"),\n+    [\n+        (['{\"id\": \"a\"', \"\"], \"line 1\"),\n+        (['[\"not\", \"an\", \"object\"]'], \"Invalid record at line 1\"),\n+        (\n+            ['{\"kind\": \"route\", \"state\": \"s\", \"expected_route\": \"b\"}'],\n+            \"Invalid record at line 1\",\n+        ),\n+        (['{\"id\": \"a\", \"kind\": \"other\", \"state\": \"s\"}'], \"Invalid record at line 1\"),\n+        (\n+            ['{\"id\": \"a\", \"kind\": \"guardrail\", \"state\": \"s\", \"expected\": \"maybe\"}'],\n+            \"Invalid record at line 1\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            [json.dumps(EXAMPLE[0]), json.dumps(EXAMPLE[0])],\n+            \"Duplicate record id 'r1' at line 2\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            [\n+                '{\"id\": \"a\", \"kind\": \"route\", \"state\": \"s\", \"expected_route\": \"b\", \"notes\": \"x\"}'\n+            ],\n+            \"Invalid record at line 1\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            ['{\"id\": \"a\", \"kind\": \"route\", \"expected_route\": \"b\"}'],\n+            \"Invalid record at line 1\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            [\n+                '{\"id\": \"a\", \"kind\": \"route\", \"state\": \"s\", \"expected_route\": \"b\", \"metadata\": {\"latency_ms\": -1}}'\n+            ],\n+            \"Invalid record at line 1\",\n+        ),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_malformed_jsonl_raises_with_location(tmp_path, lines, message):\n+    path = tmp_path / \"bad.jsonl\"\n+    path.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=message):\n+        load_dataset(path)\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"name\", [\"data.json\", \"data.jsonl\"])\n+def test_json_and_jsonl_with_bom_and_blank_lines_are_accepted(tmp_path, name):\n+    content = (\n+        json.dumps(EXAMPLE)\n+        if name.endswith(\".json\")\n+        else \"\\n\\n\".join(json.dumps(r) for r in EXAMPLE)\n+    )\n+    (tmp_path / name).write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n+\n+    assert [r.id for r in load_dataset(tmp_path / name)] == [r[\"id\"] for r in EXAMPLE]\n+\n+\n+def test_jsonl_strings_may_contain_unicode_line_separators(tmp_path):\n+    record = {\"id\": \"a\", \"kind\": \"route\", \"state\": \"a\\u2028b\\x85c\", \"expected_route\": \"b\"}\n+    path = tmp_path / \"data.jsonl\"\n+    path.write_text(json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+\n+    assert [r.state for r in load_dataset(path)] == [\"a\\u2028b\\x85c\"]\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    (\"name\", \"content\", \"message\"),\n+    [\n+        (\"data.json\", \"{}\", \"must be an array\"),\n+        (\"data.json\", \"[1,\", \"Invalid JSON\"),\n+        (\"data.json\", '[{\"id\": \"a\"}]', \"Invalid record at index 0\"),\n+        (\"data.csv\", \"\", \"Unsupported\"),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_wrong_json_shape_or_extension_raises(tmp_path, name, content, message):\n+    (tmp_path / name).write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=message):\n+        load_dataset(tmp_path / name)\n+\n+\n+# Command line\n+\n+CLI_THRESHOLDS = [\"--min-confidence\", \"0.7\", \"--noul-threshold\", \"0.8\"]\n+\n+\n+def test_main_prints_the_report_as_json(tmp_path, capsys):\n+    path = write_jsonl(tmp_path, EXAMPLE)\n+\n+    assert runner.main([str(path), *CLI_THRESHOLDS]) == 0\n+    expected = evaluate(load_dataset(path), min_confidence=0.7, noul_threshold=0.8)\n+    assert json.loads(capsys.readouterr().out) == expected.model_dump(mode=\"json\")\n+\n+\n+def test_main_reports_invalid_input_as_a_usage_error(tmp_path, capsys):\n+    path = tmp_path / \"bad.jsonl\"\n+    path.write_text(\"{\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+\n+    with pytest.raises(SystemExit) as exit_info:\n+        runner.main([str(path), *CLI_THRESHOLDS])\n+\n+    assert exit_info.value.code == 2\n+    assert \"Invalid JSONL at line 1\" in capsys.readouterr().err\n+\n+\n+# Usage and latency\n+\n+\n+def test_missing_usage_and_latency_are_not_counted_as_zero():\n+    records = [\n+        guardrail(\n+            {\"noul\": 0.9}, metadata={\"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 10}, \"latency_ms\": 100.0}\n+        ),\n+        guardrail({\"noul\": 0.9}, metadata={\"usage\": {\"output_tokens\": 2}}),\n+        guardrail({\"noul\": 0.9}),\n+    ]\n+    report = evaluate(records, min_confidence=0.5, noul_threshold=0.5)\n+\n+    assert report.usage.model_dump() == {\n+        \"input_tokens\": 10,\n+        \"input_token_records\": 1,\n+        \"output_tokens\": 2,\n+        \"output_token_records\": 1,\n+    }\n+    assert report.latency.model_dump() == {\"count\": 1, \"mean_ms\": 100.0}\n+\n+\n+# Live collection with a fake client\n+\n+\n+class FakeClient:\n+    def __init__(self, *results):\n+        self.results = list(results)\n+        self.calls = []\n+        self.closed = False\n+\n+    def system_one(self, state, questions, *, model=None):\n+        self.calls.append((state, questions, model))\n+        result = self.results.pop(0)\n+        if isinstance(result, Exception):\n+            raise result\n+        return result\n+\n+    def close(self):\n+        self.closed = True\n+\n+\n+LIVE_KWARGS = {\n+    \"route_instructions\": \"Pick a team\",\n+    \"route_criteria\": {\"billing\": \"Payments\", \"tech\": \"Bugs\"},\n+    \"guardrail_instructions\": \"Is it true?\",\n+}\n+\n+\n+def test_live_collection_builds_questions_and_records_metadata(monkeypatch):\n+    ticks = iter([1.0, 1.25, 2.0, 2.5])\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(\n+        runner, \"time\", SimpleNamespace(perf_counter=lambda: next(ticks))\n+    )\n+    choice = SimpleNamespace(\n+        choice=\"tech\", confidence=0.8, probabilities={\"billing\": 0.1, \"tech\": 0.9}\n+    )\n+    client = FakeClient(\n+        SimpleNamespace(\n+            model=\"jev-1\",\n+            usage=SimpleNamespace(input_tokens=5, output_tokens=1),\n+            answers={\"route\": choice},\n+        ),\n+        SimpleNamespace(\n+            model=\"jev-1\", usage=None, answers={\"guardrail\": SimpleNamespace(noul=0.9)}\n+        ),\n+    )\n+    records = collect_live_decisions(\n+        [route(None), guardrail(None)], client=client, model=\"jev\", **LIVE_KWARGS\n+    )\n+\n+    assert client.calls[0] == (\n+        \"s\",\n+        {\n+            \"route\": {\n+                \"type\": \"choice\",\n+                \"instructions\": \"Pick a team\",\n+                \"criteria\": {\"billing\": \"Payments\", \"tech\": \"Bugs\"},\n+            }\n+        },\n+        \"jev\",\n+    )\n+    assert client.calls[1] == (\n+        \"s\",\n+        {\"guardrail\": {\"type\": \"noul\", \"instructions\": \"Is it true?\"}},\n+        \"jev\",\n+    )\n+    assert records[0].decision == {\n+        \"choice\": \"tech\",\n+        \"confidence\": 0.8,\n+        \"probabilities\": {\"billing\": 0.1, \"tech\": 0.9},\n+    }\n+    assert records[0].metadata.model_dump() == {\n+        \"model\": \"jev-1\",\n+        \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 5, \"output_tokens\": 1},\n+        \"latency_ms\": 250.0,\n+    }\n+    assert records[1].decision == {\"noul\": 0.9}\n+    assert records[1].metadata.latency_ms == 500.0\n+    assert not client.closed\n+\n+\n+def test_live_client_errors_become_failed_records():\n+    client = FakeClient(RuntimeError(\"timeout\"), SimpleNamespace(answers={}))\n+    records = collect_live_decisions(\n+        [guardrail(None), guardrail(None)], client=client, **LIVE_KWARGS\n+    )\n+    report = evaluate(records, min_confidence=0.5, noul_threshold=0.5)\n+\n+    assert records[0].error == \"RuntimeError: timeout\"\n+    assert records[0].metadata is None\n+    assert records[1].error == \"no answer returned for 'guardrail'\"\n+    assert [o.outcome for o in report.outcomes] == [\"failed\", \"failed\"]\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    (\"response\", \"error\"),\n+    [\n+        (SimpleNamespace(answers=[\"guardrail\"]), \"no answer returned for 'guardrail'\"),\n+        (\n+            SimpleNamespace(\n+                usage=SimpleNamespace(input_tokens=-1, output_tokens=1),\n+                answers={\"guardrail\": SimpleNamespace(noul=0.9)},\n+            ),\n+            \"invalid usage: input_tokens: Input should be greater than or equal to 0\",\n+        ),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_malformed_live_responses_become_failed_records(response, error):\n+    [record] = collect_live_decisions(\n+        [guardrail(None)], client=FakeClient(response), **LIVE_KWARGS\n+    )\n+\n+    assert record.error == error\n+    assert record.decision is None\n+    assert record.metadata.latency_ms is not None\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    (\"record\", \"answers\", \"error\"),\n+    [\n+        (\n+            guardrail(None),\n+            {\n+                \"guardrail\": SimpleNamespace(\n+                    type=\"choice\", choice=\"tech\", confidence=0.9, probabilities={}\n+                )\n+            },\n+            \"expected a 'noul' answer for 'guardrail', got 'choice'\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            guardrail(None),\n+            {\"guardrail\": SimpleNamespace(type=\"choice\", choice=\"tech\", noul=0.9)},\n+            \"expected a 'noul' answer for 'guardrail', got 'choice'\",\n+        ),\n+        (\n+            route(None),\n+            {\"route\": SimpleNamespace(type=\"noul\", noul=0.9)},\n+            \"expected a 'choice' answer for 'route', got 'noul'\",\n+        ),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_live_answer_of_the_wrong_type_fails(record, answers, error):\n+    client = FakeClient(SimpleNamespace(answers=answers))\n+    [record] = collect_live_decisions([record], client=client, **LIVE_KWARGS)\n+\n+    assert record.error == error\n+    assert record.decision is None\n+    assert outcome_of(record).outcome == \"failed\"\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"probabilities\", [42, 0, False, \"\", []])\n+def test_malformed_probabilities_fail_without_stopping_collection(probabilities):\n+    bad = SimpleNamespace(choice=\"tech\", confidence=0.9, probabilities=probabilities)\n+    good = SimpleNamespace(choice=\"tech\", confidence=0.9, probabilities={\"tech\": 0.9})\n+    client = FakeClient(\n+        SimpleNamespace(answers={\"route\": bad}),\n+        SimpleNamespace(answers={\"route\": good}),\n+    )\n+    records = collect_live_decisions(\n+        [route(None, expected=\"tech\"), route(None, expected=\"tech\")],\n+        client=client,\n+        **LIVE_KWARGS,\n+    )\n+\n+    assert [outcome_of(r).outcome for r in records] == [\"failed\", \"correct\"]\n+    assert \"probabilities\" in outcome_of(records[0]).reason\n+\n+\n+def test_live_answer_without_probabilities_or_usage():\n+    answer = SimpleNamespace(choice=\"tech\", confidence=0.8, probabilities=None)\n+    client = FakeClient(SimpleNamespace(answers={\"route\": answer}))\n+    [record] = collect_live_decisions([route(None)], client=client, **LIVE_KWARGS)\n+\n+    assert record.decision[\"probabilities\"] == {}\n+    assert record.metadata.usage is None\n+    assert record.metadata.model is None\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    \"override\",\n+    [\n+        {\"route_instructions\": \" \"},\n+        {\"guardrail_instructions\": \"\"},\n+        {\"route_criteria\": {}},\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_live_collection_requires_questions(override):\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n+        collect_live_decisions([], client=FakeClient(), **(LIVE_KWARGS | override))\n+\n+\n+def test_live_collection_skips_recorded_decisions():\n+    client = FakeClient()\n+    records = [guardrail({\"noul\": 0.9}), guardrail(None, error=\"earlier failure\")]\n+\n+    assert collect_live_decisions(records, client=client, **LIVE_KWARGS) == records\n+    assert client.calls == []\n", "problem_statement": "[FEATURE] Build an offline Jev routing and guardrail evaluation runner\n## Python PR scope\n\nWrite a small Python evaluation runner for labeled routing/guardrail records and recorded or fake decisions. Report accuracy, route coverage/abstention, guardrail false accepts/rejects, and recorded latency/usage when available.\n\n**Difficulty:** medium. **Allocation index:** #8118. **Project:** #8065.\n\n## Cohort allocation\n\nThis ticket is reserved for maintainer-coordinated allocation to the Stanford semester collaboration. Please wait for @lorenzejay to confirm an assignee before implementing. A comment expresses interest; it does not establish ownership. Public `good first issue` / `help wanted` discovery labels will be considered after cohort allocation.\n\nGitHub usernames have not yet been supplied, so no individual assignment is implied.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Use a simple JSON/JSONL dataset and deterministic synthetic decisions for a runnable offline mode.\n- [ ] Treat Jev Choice confidence and Noul probability as separate fields; evaluate thresholds without converting one into the other.\n- [ ] Handle missing decisions explicitly in metrics; do not count failed evaluations as correct answers.\n- [ ] Add tests for metric denominators, threshold boundaries, missing records, and invalid inputs.\n- [ ] Make live SDK calls opt-in with explicit credentials and report measured results rather than vendor speed claims.\n\n## Dependencies and coordination\n\n- Offline implementation can start independently. Coordinate recorded-result shape with #8066 and #8068.\n\n## Starting points\n\n- [lib/crewai/src/crewai/experimental/evaluation](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/tree/main/lib/crewai/src/crewai/experimental/evaluation)\n- [lib/crewai-tools/tests](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/tree/main/lib/crewai-tools/tests)\n- [API/format reference](https://docs.typesafe.ai/confidence)\n\n## Submission\n\nThe contributor implements this scope and submits one focused PR linked to this open issue. Include full Python annotations, behavioral tests, and relevant quality checks. No paid API calls are required for the tests. Preserve existing APIs outside the scoped feature. For newly found defects, reproduce them and check active issues/PRs before fixing them. Docs edits, when needed, belong under `docs/edge/` and must sync ar, ko, pt-BR per `DOCS_TRANSLATIONS.md`. Follow [.github/CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md). Issue prepared with AI assistance.\n", "hints_text": "I can do this one. Thank you Lorenze!", "created_at": "2026-10-16T16:51:27Z"}
